PVD("fiji_ndp_2017-2021",{"docs":["","FIJI NDP 2017 21"],"s":{"1":[[1,"9","16","Tertiary Health Care and Medical Service Upgrading","In the next 20 years, medical services will be raised to international standards with a major focus on tertiary health care and overall medical service delivery.",""],[1,"9","17","Hospital Service and Capacity Improvement Programme","Investments will be made to reduce patient waiting time, improve hospital services, increase the number of beds, improve ambulance services and raise the doctor-to- patient ratio to 1 doctor per 1,000 people.",""],[1,"10","1","Health Facility Construction and Equipment Upgrade Programme","Investments in the construction of new hospitals, health centres and nursing stations will continue.",""],[1,"10","1","Health Supply Inventory Management Improvement","Inventory management will be improved, and other opportunities will be explored to ensure that drugs and consumables are available at all times.",""],[1,"10","2","Public Hospital Strategic Partnership Management Initiative","The government is exploring options to engage strategic partners in the management and operation of certain public hospitals to improve their service delivery.",""],[1,"10","3","Incentives for Private Investment in Tertiary Health Care","Incentives are already in place to attract private sector investment in tertiary health care.",""],[1,"10","3","Expansion of Domestic Tertiary Health Care Services","A major focus moving forward will be to ensure that Fijians can take advantage of specialised tertiary care in Fiji rather than having to pay high medical bills overseas.",""],[1,"10","3","Development of Fiji as a South Pacific Health Hub","Tertiary health care services have the potential to become an important growth sector and revenue earner and assist Fiji to become the health hub of the South Pacific.",""]],"2":[[1,"10","4","Preventive Health and NCD Reduction Initiative","More emphasis will be placed on preventive health care by promoting healthy eating habits, physical activity and other lifestyle changes to reduce Non-Communicable Diseases (NCDs).",""],[1,"44","7","National NCD Prevention Strategy","Strategies will be pursued to tackle NCDs in the country.",""],[1,"44","7","Multi-sectoral NCD Prevention Campaigns","A multi-sectoral approach through better health education, production and adequate supply of fresh fruits and vegetables, and promotional and awareness campaigns will be further enhanced to address this issue.",""],[1,"44","7","Private Sector and Partner Collaboration for NCD Prevention","Collaboration and partnership with the private sector, NGOs and development partners will be pursued.",""],[1,"45","3","Non-Communicable Disease Prevention and Response Investment","Expand investment in approaches to address non-communicable diseases, including nutrition, mental health and injuries, within and beyond the health sector.",""]],"3":[[1,"44","2","Divisional Hospital Upgrade and Expansion Programme","more investments will be made to upgrade and expand existing divisional hospitals to provide more beds and better facilities",""],[1,"44","2","Sub-divisional Hospital Construction and Upgrading Programme","New sub-divisional hospitals will be constructed and existing ones upgraded",""],[1,"44","2","Health Centre Construction and Staffing Programme","New health centres will be constructed with proper services and equipment",""],[1,"44","2","National Kidney Research and Treatment Centre","a new National Kidney Research and Treatment Centre will be constructed that will act as a national hub for treatment and prevention of kidney disease, and to provide patients the most economical access to treatment of kidney disease",""],[1,"44","9","Tertiary Health Care Standards and Investment Initiative","Adherence to international standards of tertiary health care will be pursued as a major initiative to ensure that Fijians are provided with advanced tertiary care.",""],[1,"44","9","Private Sector Tax Incentives for Tertiary Health Investment","Tax incentives to entice private sector investment in this area were introduced in the 2016-2017 National Budget.",""],[1,"44","9","Public Investment Exploration for Tertiary Health Care","Government will explore further opportunities for public investment in this area.",""],[1,"51","1","Hospital Construction and Health Centre Upgrade Programme","1 new hospital - Ba 1 Construction of Navosa Sub- divisional hospital 1 Construction of New Nausori Hospital 1 health centre upgrade to sub- divisional hospital -Valelevu",""]],"4":[[1,"44","4","Family Planning Education and Equal-Parenting Promotion","Education and information will be provided to men and women regarding family planning, and equal-parenting initiatives will be promoted.",""],[1,"44","5","Skilled Healthcare Worker Recruitment","Hiring of skilled healthcare workers will continue to ensure that the ratio of doctors, nurses and midwives per 1,000 people is increased to internationally accepted levels.",""],[1,"44","6","Free Medicine Scheme","the free medicine scheme will continue",""],[1,"45","4","Maternal, Infant, Child and Adolescent Health Services","Provide high quality and comprehensive maternal, infant, child and adolescent health family planning and sexual education, equal parenting programmes to the population.",""],[1,"45","5","Family Planning and Reproductive Health Information and Resources","Provide Family Planning and reproductive health information and resources.",""],[1,"45","5","Maternal, Newborn, and Child Health Services","All pregnant women, including teenagers, mothers and new-borns receive timely, safe, appropriate and effective health services before, during, and after childbirth.",""],[1,"45","5","Paediatric and Nutritional Health Services Expansion","Provide access to quality preventive and curative paediatric and nutritional services.",""],[1,"45","5","Adolescent and Youth Health Services Expansion","Expand public health and clinical services to appropriately address the needs of adolescents and youth.",""],[1,"45","8","Primary Health Care Expansion and Health Management Improvement","Expand primary health care, with an emphasis on providing a continuum of care and improved service quality and safety.",""],[1,"45","8","Health Management Improvement","Improve health management.",""],[1,"45","9","Primary Health Care Strengthening and Continuum of Care Improvement","Improve health-service delivery experience for patients through continued strengthening of primary health care and improved continuum of care.",""],[1,"46","8","Primary Eye Care Outreach Kit Procurement and Training","Primary eye care: Purchase portable kit (appliances, supplies, IEC); training for outreach",""],[1,"47","21","Severe Acute Malnutrition Treatment Supplement","Reduce severe acute malnutrition (Supplement for Malnourished Children - supply F-75 and F-100 in the 3 Divisional Hospitals)",""],[1,"49","12","In-Service Training Plan Implementation","Implementation of in-service training plan (Capacity Building/ Specialized training)",""],[1,"51","15","Sustainable Health System Financing","Establish sustainable financing of the health system",""],[1,"51","16","National Health Accounts Development","Develop National Health Accounts (NHA)",""]],"5":[[1,"7","10","Government Debt Reduction Strategy","government debt will be reduced to 35 percent of GDP over the next 20 years.",""],[1,"17","11","Accommodative Monetary and Exchange-Rate Policy","The RBF has kept monetary policy accommodative, with its twin objectives of adequate foreign reserves and low inflation safeguarded.",""],[1,"17","13","Priority Sector Budget Allocation","Government will continue to allocate adequate budgetary resources to key priority sectors that have the capacity to deliver better economic and social returns and support higher, broad-based, inclusive and sustainable economic growth.",""]],"6":[[1,"19","10","Financial Sector Development Plan 2016-2025","the Financial Sector Development Plan 2016-2025 provides the necessary overarching policy direction.",""],[1,"19","10","Diagnostic Review of Financial Legislation and Regulation","a diagnostic review of legislative and regulatory frameworks affecting the financial system",""],[1,"19","10","National Switch Establishment","establishment of the National Switch",""],[1,"19","10","Capital Markets Development","developing capital markets",""],[1,"19","10","Remittance Cost Reduction and Streamlining","streamlining and reducing the cost of overseas remittances",""],[1,"19","10","Non-Bank Financial Institution Competitiveness Enhancement","enhancing the competitiveness of non-bank financial institutions (NBFIs)",""],[1,"19","10","Secured Transaction Framework Implementation","implementing a Secured Transaction Framework",""]],"7":[[1,"96","3","Micro and Small Business Grant and SME Credit Guarantee Expansion","Government will continue and further expand financial assistance provided under the Micro and Small Business Grant (MSBG) scheme, SME credit guarantee, and subsidies through the Fiji Development Bank (FDB)",""],[1,"96","4","MSME Lending Promotion","continue to encourage the financial sector to provide loans to MSMEs.",""],[1,"96","4","Young Entrepreneurship Scheme","Government will also launch the Young Entrepreneurship Scheme (YES), which will provide immediate assistance in the form of grants to qualified young and budding entrepreneurs, who have bankable ideas/projects which financial institutions are not willing to support due to lack of collaterals.",""],[1,"96","6","Secured Transactions Framework","A Secured Transactions Framework is being drafted that will allow for the use of movable property such as equipment, inventory, accounts receivable, equities, crops and livestock as collateral for accessing loans.",""],[1,"96","7","Microfinance Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","To guide the operations of microfinance service providers, a legal and regulatory framework will be developed.",""],[1,"97","3","MSME Access to Finance Improvement","Improve MSMEs access to finance.",""],[1,"97","4","MSME Finance Expansion and Credit Support","Increase the provision of finance available through government funded programmes, including MSBG scheme, SME credit Guarantee Scheme, YES and SME financing support through FDB.",""],[1,"97","4","Medium Enterprise Stock Exchange Listing Incentives","Incentivise medium enterprises listing on South Pacific Stock Exchange (SPSE) as a way to raise funds and explore and implement innovative ways for MSMEs to source funding e.g. crowd-funding.",""],[1,"97","4","Secured Transactions Framework for Movable Collateral","Develop secured transactions framework that will allow for the use of movable property as collateral.",""],[1,"97","4","Microfinance Service Provider Regulatory Framework","Develop a legal and regulatory framework to govern microfinance service providers.",""],[1,"97","8","Secured Transactions Legislation","Enact secured transactions legislation",""]],"8":[[1,"11","14","Digital Connectivity Expansion","Apart from transport connectivity, there will be a major focus on digital connectivity.",""],[1,"13","2","Digital Connectivity Expansion","Digital connectivity through high-speed internet networks and broadband access will be improved, and all areas of Fiji will be digitally connected.",""],[1,"13","3","Broadband Competition Enhancement and Open Access Infrastructure","Competition will be enhanced in broadband internet services by making communication infrastructure available to multiple users under reasonable terms and conditions.",""],[1,"13","3","National Fibre Optic Connectivity Expansion","Fibre optic connectivity between Viti Levu and Vanua Levu will be established, and the fibre optic ring around Viti Levu will be completed.",""],[1,"13","4","Coordinated Fibre Optic Conduit Installation During Road Works","All utility providers will cooperate in laying fibre optic cable conduits and chambers when undertaking trenching works during road construction or maintenance.",""],[1,"13","5","Telecentre Expansion and Establishment Programme","Government will expand existing telecentres and establish new ones around the country.",""],[1,"13","5","Digital Literacy Improvement Initiative","Digital literacy will be improved.",""],[1,"135","5","Expansion of the Community Telecentre Project","Expand the outreach of the government Community Telecentre Project, where feasible.",""],[1,"135","5","Subsidies and Tax Incentives for Assistive ICT Access","Improve access to computers and assistive devices for visually impaired and the hearing impaired through targeted tax incentives and subsidies.",""],[1,"135","5","Subtitling Requirements for TV Broadcasters","TV broadcasters to provide subtitle services for hearing-impaired viewers.",""],[1,"135","5","Review of the National ICT Policy","Review the National ICT Policy to incorporate relevant aspects of the National Gender Policy 2014 and the National Disability Policy.",""],[1,"135","5","Subsidies for Disabled Access to Telecentres","Provide subsidies to improve access for disabled people to school and community telecentres e.g. wheelchair ramps.",""]],"9":[[1,"72","17","Digital Connectivity Investment Programme","Investments will build digital connectivity, and new and better technologies will be adopted for productivity improvement and better service delivery.",""],[1,"72","17","ICT Sector Job Creation and Efficiency Initiative","The ICT sector will be harnessed for job creation and efficiency gains and to raise the overall standard of living.",""],[1,"128","3","National Communications Coverage Expansion","Improve communication, mobile and internet coverage to all parts of Fiji.",""],[1,"134","5","Fibre Optic Cable Project between Viti Levu and Vanua Levu","The fibre optic cable project between Viti Levu and Vanua Levu via the Samoa-Fiji submarine cable is currently underway and will address bandwidth capacity constraints and make internet more accessible to all Fijians.",""],[1,"134","5","Private Sector Partnership Fibre Optic Cable Projects","Other planned fibre optic cable projects will be pursued through private sector partnerships.",""],[1,"134","6","Broadband Infrastructure Sharing and Competition Enhancement","Competition will be enhanced in broadband internet services by making communication infrastructure available to multiple users under reasonable terms and conditions.",""],[1,"134","7","Declared Universal Service Area Survey Mechanism","The Telecommunication Authority of Fiji (TAF) will regularly survey areas to be a \"Declared Universal Service Area\", which is a prerequisite for telecommunications companies to erect network towers in those areas.","Telecommunication Authority of Fiji (TAF)"],[1,"134","8","Climate-Resilient ICT Infrastructure Strategy","Government will adopt strategies to ensure that ICT infrastructure is climate resilient.",""],[1,"135","2","Telecommunications Infrastructure Improvement","Improve the telecommunications infrastructure.",""],[1,"135","3","Broadband Competition and Infrastructure Sharing Reform","Enhance competition in broadband internet services, by making the existing fixed line infrastructure",""],[1,"135","3","Communications Infrastructure PPP Development","Consider Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs) in the construction of communications infrastructure",""],[1,"135","3","Utility Fibre Optic Conduit Coordination","Fiji Roads Authority (FRA), the Water Authority of Fiji (WAF), Fiji Electricity Authority (FEA) and Telecom Fiji Limited (TFL) along with other utility providers to lay fibre optic cables, conduits and chambers when conducting trenching works during road construction or maintenance.","Fiji Roads Authority (FRA) | the Water Authority of Fiji (WAF) | Fiji Electricity Authority (FEA) | Telecom Fiji Limited (TFL)"],[1,"135","3","TFL Fibre Optic Ring Completion","Complete the TFL fibre optic cable ring around Viti Levu.",""],[1,"135","3","Redundant Inter-Island Fibre Link Development","Establish a second redundant link from Viti Levu to Vanua Levu through Lomaiviti, to provide resiliency",""],[1,"135","3","Inter-Island Fibre Optic Connectivity Project","Establish fibre optic connectivity between Viti Levu and Vanua Levu through the Samoa-Fiji submarine cable.",""],[1,"135","3","ICT and Broadband Policy Implementation","Fully implement the ICT Development Policy and National Broadband Policy 2011.",""],[1,"136","10","Inter-Island Fibre Optic Installation","Begin installation of unrepeatered fibre pair and full fibre branching unit between Viti Levu and Vanua Levu",""],[1,"136","13","TFL Fibre Optic Cable Ring Completion","Complete the TFL fibre optic cable ring around Viti Levu",""]],"10":[[1,"14","2","E-Government Platform Streamlining","E-Government platforms to speed up approvals processes, business registration, land use administration, taxation, and other services will be further streamlined.",""],[1,"14","3","ICT-Based Public Sector Planning, Budgeting and Monitoring","ICT-based planning, budgeting and monitoring will be used in the public sector to improve work processes, productivity and service delivery.",""],[1,"14","3","IT Skills Development and Retention","IT related skills will continue to be developed and retained.",""]],"11":[[1,"11","10","ICT and Audio-Visual Industry Development Partnership","Developing ICT and improving prospects for the audio- visual industry and film-making will be achieved in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"13","13","Cross-Sector New Technology Adoption Initiative","Appropriate new technology will be adopted to raise overall efficiency and productivity and to improve service delivery across all sectors.",""],[1,"13","13","Sectoral Technology Adoption Support","Adoption of new technology will be supported in areas like transportation, renewable energy, manufacturing, agriculture, ICT, education and other service-related sectors.",""],[1,"13","13","Innovation and Research Incentive Scheme","Innovation, research and implementation of new ideas will also be incentivised.",""],[1,"13","15","Manufacturing Value-Addition and Energy-Efficient Machinery Incentive","In the manufacturing sector, greater value-addition and investment in energy-efficient machinery and equipment will be incentivised.",""],[1,"13","15","Industrial Digital Technology Adoption Support","Government will support the increased use of cloud computing, 3D printing, inter-networking of smart devices and other emerging technologies to improve efficiency and productivity.",""],[1,"134","9","ICT Development Investment Promotion for Back-Office Operations and Call Centres","investment will be attracted for ICT development in back-office operations and call centres.",""],[1,"135","8","ICT Workforce Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen ICT capabilities in the workforce.",""],[1,"135","9","ICT Skills Retention Incentive","Incentivise the retention of skilled IT graduates in the workforce.",""],[1,"135","9","Technology Transfer for Access to Appropriate Technologies","Increase access to appropriate technologies via technology transfer between bilateral, regional and international partners.",""],[1,"135","9","ICT-Based Agricultural Weather Information Service","Support the widespread use of ICT to provide localized weather information and forecasts to farmers,",""],[1,"135","10","Green Technology Promotion","Promote the use of \"Green\" technology.",""],[1,"135","11","FDI Incentives for Sustainable Technology Industries","Incentivise large-scale FDI in industries that develop environmentally sustainable technology (particularly\n· Incentivise FDI in business process outsourcing.\n· Develop a national framework to promote innovation, research and development (R&D) towards\nenvironmentally sustainable technology.",""],[1,"135","11","Green Technology Import Standards",". Ensure that all imported technologies are consistent with \"Green\" technology specifications i.e. energy efficient, low carbon emissions, meet minimum quality standards and safety considerations, discourage\nparallel imports, etc.",""],[1,"136","28","National Innovation and R&D Framework","Develop a national framework for innovation and R&D",""]],"12":[[1,"3","8","National Development Plan Monitoring Mechanism","Progress of the NDP will be monitored to help keep implementation on track and ensure our collective vision is realised.",""],[1,"28","21","Master Plans for Other Growth Areas","Develop Master plans for other growth areas",""],[1,"139","1","National Plan Monitoring and Evaluation System","effective monitoring and evaluation of the Plan is needed to ensure delivery of planned results.",""],[1,"139","2","Effective and Accountable Public Service Delivery and Programme Implementation","The immediate priority is to ensure effective, efficient and accountable delivery of Ministry and Department outputs, i.e. the delivery of public services and implementation of public programmes and projects under the 5-year Development Plan and measuring national development targets, which are aligned to regional and international indicators like the SDGs.","Ministry and Department"],[1,"139","3","Performance-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Monitoring and evaluation of the Plan and the 5-year DP will rely on the standard performance-based monitoring and evaluation framework focusing on outcomes and outputs.",""],[1,"139","22","Institutional M&E Integration into Planning and Decision-Making","Incorporate M&E assessments by institutions and lead agencies into planning and decision-making processes",""],[1,"139","29","Official Statistics Coordination and Release","Coordinate compilation, collation and release of official statistics",""],[1,"140","2","Strategic Monitoring and Evaluation for Public Service Delivery","Being strategic about how and what to monitor and evaluate to ensure efficient, effective and accountable delivery of agency outputs, i.e. programmes and projects for provision of public services.",""],[1,"140","3","Periodic Monitoring and Evaluation of Development Plan Implementation","There will be ongoing periodic monitoring and evaluation of implementation progress and performance results for all programmes and projects under the 5-year DP identified for implementation under the National Budget or through other sources of funding.",""],[1,"140","3","Regular Review of Monitoring and Evaluation Priority Areas","There will also be regular review of priority areas for monitoring and evaluation to support achievement of the 20-year Development Plan.",""],[1,"140","4","Annual Audit Review Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Annual reviews by accountability institutions like the OAG and PAC will be used for monitoring and evaluation, with continued focus on implementing findings of annual audit reports.",""],[1,"140","5","Government Monitoring and Evaluation Reporting Streamlining","Efforts will be made by all government monitoring and evaluation agencies to streamline reporting processes for implementing agencies.",""],[1,"140","6","National Budget Monitoring and Evaluation System","Monitoring and evaluation of national performance and outcomes are an integral part of the National Budget process.",""],[1,"140","7","National Baseline Data Compilation for National Outcomes","Commence with existing baseline data for national outcomes and where necessary baseline data will be compiled (e.g. national baseline data for the state of Fiji's environment needs to be collated);",""],[1,"140","8","Public Sector Investment and Capital Budget Appraisal Assessments","Carry out assessments according to existing methodology (e.g. Public Sector Investment Programme - PSIP and Capital Budget Appraisals) for the provision of a service, adoption of a programme and allocation of resources.",""],[1,"140","9","Public Services and Programme Effectiveness Assessment","Determine viability through assessments of the effectiveness and impact of public services, policy objectives, strategies, programmes and projects; and",""],[1,"140","12","Public Engagement in Official Statistics Use","Involve all programme stakeholders, particularly the general public (increase use of official statistics to not only report performance but to support decision making);",""],[1,"140","13","Monitoring and Evaluation Review Process","Consideration will be given to monitoring and evaluation processes, such as consultations with the public and other national stakeholders and a Mid- Term Review.",""],[1,"140","14","Monitoring and Evaluation Template for Ministries and Departments","A Monitoring and Evaluation template for monitoring of outputs by Ministries and Departments under the 5-year DP and the national budget is reflected in Table 3.",""]],"13":[[1,"128","10","Public-Private Partnership Development","Develop public private partnerships.",""],[1,"128","11","Tourism Infrastructure Partnership Development","Foster partnerships with tourism stakeholders to develop and maintain tourism infrastructure while taking into account environmental, social and cultural concerns.",""],[1,"128","11","Tourism PPP Incentive Package","Incentivise PPP with innovative marketing and tax incentive packages for product diversification.",""],[1,"128","11","Targeted Support for New Tourism Operators","Provide targeted incentives to potential, new and upcoming tourism operators.",""],[1,"128","12","Accommodative Tourism Policy and Regulatory Reform","Formulate accommodative policies and regulations to stimulate tourism growth.",""],[1,"128","13","Tourism Agency Capacity and Sustainable Funding Support","Increase institutional capacity and resources of tourism facilitating agencies, including a sustainable funding formula for Tourism Fiji.",""],[1,"128","13","Immigration Law and Procedure Review for Extended Visitor Stays","Review immigration laws and procedures to accommodate extended stays by visitors.",""],[1,"128","13","Biennial Tourism Satellite Accounts","Prepare Tourism Satellite Accounts every two years.",""]],"14":[[1,"20","4","Civil Service Reform and Performance Improvement","Government will continue with the reform of the civil service to ensure strong leadership and service delivery.",""]],"15":[[1,"20","12","Whole-of-Government UPR Reform Implementation","A whole-of-government approach, in partnership with civil society, is needed to support reforms to implement the recommendations agreed to under Fiji's 2nd Universal Periodic Review (UPR) in 2014.",""],[1,"20","12","Ratification of Human Rights Treaties and Conventions","This includes ratification of all human rights treaties and conventions by 2024.",""],[1,"20","12","Human Rights and Anti-Discrimination Commission Resourcing","The Human Rights and Anti-discrimination Commission (HRADC) will be resourced to address all human rights complaints efficiently and effectively.",""],[1,"20","13","Standards of Conduct Enforcement and Freedom of Information Implementation","Effective administration and enforcement of standards of conduct for senior public officials and the Freedom of Information law are critical measures to ensure",""]],"16":[[1,"67","4","Court Facilities and Legal Services Upgrade","Upgrade court facilities and infrastructure and expand legal services to improve citizen's access to justice.",""],[1,"67","4","Digitization of Laws","Continue digitization of laws.",""],[1,"67","4","Rural and Outer Islands Court Sitting Expansion","Conduct regular court sittings in rural and outer islands and recruit experienced and independent prosecutors, judges, and magistrates to minimize backlog of cases.",""],[1,"68","12","Justice System Strengthening","Strengthen the justice system.",""],[1,"68","13","Court Facilities and Legal Services Upgrade","Upgrade court facilities and infrastructure and expand legal services to improve citizen's access to justice.",""],[1,"68","13","Digitization of Laws","Continue digitization of laws.",""],[1,"68","13","Rural and Outer Islands Court Sitting Programme","Conduct regular court sittings in rural and outer islands and recruit experienced and independent prosecutors, judges, and magistrates to minimize backlog of cases.",""],[1,"71","3","Court Complex Upgrade Programme","Upgrade of existing Court Complexes",""],[1,"71","7","Judicial Recruitment Expansion","Recruitment of more magistrate and high court judges",""],[1,"71","8","Prosecution Guidelines Development","Develop prosecution guidelines",""],[1,"72","14","Public Access to Information and Fundamental Freedoms Protection","Ensure public access to information and project fundamental freedoms, in accordance with national legislation and international agreements",""]],"17":[[1,"20","10","Strengthening Parliamentary Accountability and Committee System","Government will be fully accountable to the people of Fiji through Parliament, and resources will be allocated to support a robust and effective parliamentary and committee system, ensuring scrutiny of public programmes and policies through open and informed debates on issues of national interest.",""]],"18":[[1,"66","3","Police Force Strengthening for Security and Crime Prevention","The Police Force will be strengthened to ensure security and effective crime prevention.",""],[1,"66","16","Organized Crime and Drug Trafficking Countermeasures","Develop tactical and strategic approaches to combat the emergence of organized criminal networks, such as drug trafficking, illegal trade and arms.",""],[1,"66","16","Fiji Police Service Plan and Master Plan","Formulate and implement the Fiji Police Service Plan and Master Plan for all police stations and other",""],[1,"66","16","Community Crime Counselling and Awareness Services","Provide more community counselling and public awareness services on different forms of crimes and forms of services.",""],[1,"66","16","Police Station and Police Post Expansion","Upgrade and construct new police stations and police posts.",""],[1,"66","16","Police Resource and Equipment Upgrade","Adequately resource the police force to improve responsiveness to crime e.g. with police vehicles and crime detection equipment.",""],[1,"66","16","Security Support for Disaster Relief and Rehabilitation","Strengthen security and involvement of national security agencies during relief and rehabilitation for emergency response to natural disasters and other national emergencies.",""],[1,"68","9","Organized Crime and Drug Trafficking Countermeasures","Develop tactical and strategic approaches to combat the emergence of organized criminal networks, such as drug trafficking, illegal trade and arms.",""],[1,"68","9","Fiji Police Service Plan and Station Master Planning","Formulate and implement the Fiji Police Service Plan and Master Plan for all police stations and other forms of services.",""],[1,"68","9","Community Crime Counselling and Awareness Services","Provide more community counselling and public awareness services on different forms of crimes and of services.",""],[1,"68","9","Police Station and Police Post Upgrading and Construction","Upgrade and construct new police stations and police posts.",""],[1,"68","9","Police Force Resourcing for Crime Response","Adequately resource the police force to improve responsiveness to crime e.g. with police vehicles and crime detection equipment.",""],[1,"68","9","Security Support for Disaster Relief and Emergency Response","Strengthen security and involvement of national security agencies during relief and rehabilitation for emergency response to natural disasters and other national emergencies.",""],[1,"70","7","Police Reporting Strengthening","Strengthen police reporting",""],[1,"70","15","Construction of New Police Stations","Construction of new police stations",""],[1,"70","16","Construction of New Police Posts and Quarters","Construction of new police posts and quarters",""],[1,"70","33","Police Investigation and Interviewing Guidelines Review","Review police guidelines on investigations and interviewing procedures",""]],"19":[[1,"11","3","Continued Participation in UN Peacekeeping Missions","Fiji will also continue its role in UN Peacekeeping missions.",""],[1,"68","11","International Peacekeeping and Security Cooperation","Strengthen Fiji's involvement in international peacekeeping and security.",""],[1,"68","11","Regional and International Security Cooperation","Enhance regional and international cooperation to help strengthen national security partners and allies.",""]],"20":[[1,"20","8","Partial Divestment of State-Owned Enterprise Shares","Government had embarked on partial divestment of shares in a number of SOEs to encourage private sector partnerships and improve efficiency and service delivery.",""],[1,"20","8","Public-Private Partnership Legislation Review","Legislation governing public- private partnerships (PPPs) will be reviewed to support development of major national infrastructure, public utilities and other development projects.",""],[1,"92","14","Public-Private Partnership Policy Framework","A PPP policy framework will be adopted to support private-sector investment in major national infrastructure projects and other strategic areas.",""],[1,"92","14","Public Enterprises Act Review for Reorganisation","The Public Enterprises Act 1996 will be reviewed to support reorganisation",""],[1,"93","12","PPP and State-Owned Enterprise Policy Development","Develop PPP and SOE policies to support private sector development.",""],[1,"93","13","PPP Act and Public Enterprises Act Review","Review PPP Act and Public Enterprises Act.",""],[1,"93","13","State-Owned Enterprises Privatization Programme","Formulate privatization policy framework and implement privatisation programme for State Owned Enterprises (SOEs).",""],[1,"93","13","PPP Policy Framework and Project Development Programme","Formulate PPP policy framework and develop and implement a programme for PPP projects.",""],[1,"95","2","Policy and Legal Framework Reform","Adopt new Policy and legal frame- work",""],[1,"95","4","PPP and SOE Policy Development","Develop PPP and SOE policies to support private sector development",""],[1,"95","8","Privatization of Identified State-Owned Enterprises","Complete privatization of identified SOEs",""],[1,"95","9","Public-Private Partnership Policy Framework","Adopt new PPP Policy Framework",""],[1,"95","10","Multi-Sector Regulator Establishment","Establish multi-sector regulator",""],[1,"95","16","New Regulatory Framework Adoption","Adopt new regulatory framework",""],[1,"95","23","New Legal Framework Adoption","Adopt new legal frame- work",""]],"21":[[1,"67","4","Prison Infrastructure and Rehabilitation Upgrade","Improve infrastructure and design of prison facilities to be conducive to rehabilitation and security.",""],[1,"67","4","Fiji Correction Services Intelligence Framework","Embed an Intelligence Framework for Fiji Correction Services.",""],[1,"67","4","Community Corrections Front-End Diversion","Inception of Community Corrections - Front End Diversion - inmates to be sentenced to do community work.",""],[1,"67","4","Prisons Technology Modernization","Improve prisons technology and purchase modern equipment.",""],[1,"67","4","Fiji Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises","Inception of Fiji Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises.",""],[1,"67","4","Judiciary and Corrections Staff Capacity Building","Improve staff capacity (Human Resource Management) for judiciary and corrections services.",""],[1,"68","13","Prison Infrastructure Rehabilitation Upgrade","Improve infrastructure and design of prison facilities to be conducive to rehabilitation and security.",""],[1,"68","13","Intelligence Framework for Fiji Correction Services","Embed an Intelligence Framework for Fiji Correction Services.",""],[1,"68","13","Community Corrections Front-End Diversion","Inception of Community Corrections - Front End Diversion - inmates to be sentenced to do community work.",""],[1,"68","13","Prisons Technology Modernization","Improve prisons technology and purchase modern equipment.",""],[1,"68","13","Fiji Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises","Inception of Fiji Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises.",""],[1,"68","13","Judiciary and Corrections Staff Capacity Building","Improve staff capacity (Human Resource Management) for judiciary and corrections services.",""]],"22":[[1,"92","10","Titles Office Digitisation and National Land Register Development","Land-use administration will be improved through digitisation of the Titles Office and development of the national land register.",""],[1,"92","11","Town Planning and Land Subdivision Act Review","The Town Planning Act and the Sub-division of Land Act are currently under review",""],[1,"93","2","Land Use Administration Enhancement","Enhance land use administration.",""],[1,"93","3","Geospatial Information and Land Administration Capacity Building","Capacity building to develop the Fiji Geospatial Information System, National Land Bank and National Land Register.",""],[1,"93","3","iTaukei and State Land Development Support","Support development of iTaukei and State land to improve access for productive purposes, including Land Register.",""],[1,"93","3","Lease Administration Strengthening","Strengthen administration of lease processes.",""],[1,"93","3","Public Awareness for Land Bank Deposits","identification of land for deposit in the Land Bank through public awareness.",""],[1,"93","4","Development Control Capacity Building","Build capacity to enhance development control efficiency.",""],[1,"93","5","Town Planning and Land Subdivision Reform","Reform the Town Planning Act and Subdivision of Land Act.",""],[1,"93","5","Development Permission Processing Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the Department of Town and Country Planning and local authorities to improve consistency and efficiency in the processing of development permission.",""],[1,"94","1","Land Use Administration Enhancement","Enhance land use administration",""],[1,"94","10","Technical Capacity Building for Development Control","Build technical capacity to enhance development control",""],[1,"94","11","Strengthen the Department of Town and Country Planning","Strengthen Depart- ment of Town and Country Planning",""],[1,"94","12","Town Planning and Land Subdivision Legislative Reform","Adopt new Town Plan- ning Act and Sub-div of Land Act",""],[1,"94","14","Local and National Government Administration Harmonisation","Harmonise local and national government administration",""],[1,"94","16","National Building Code Reform","Adopt new National Building Code",""]],"23":[[1,"11","1","National Security and Rule of Law Protection","Government will ensure a safe, secure and stable Fiji guided by the National Security Strategy.",""],[1,"11","1","Constitutional Protection and Rule of Law Enforcement","The rule of law will be upheld and the Constitution will be protected.",""]],"24":[[1,"20","2","Sugar Industry Support and Productivity Enhancement Programme","Government will continue to support the sugar industry to sustain the livelihoods of the more-than 200,000 people who depend on it.",""],[1,"20","2","Sugar Industry Transport and Revenue Improvement Measures","Efforts will be geared towards increasing productive capacity, improving transportation, implementing a new cane-quality payment system and generating additional revenue.",""],[1,"20","2","Sugarcane Replanting, Lease Renewal, and Mechanisation Initiative","To raise sugarcane production, replanting on unused sugar cane leases, securing more lease renewals and mechanisation will be pursued.",""],[1,"111","12","Sugar Industry Reform Programme","In preparation for the phasing out of preferential access to the EU, industry reforms have been undertaken to depoliticise the industry, improve milling efficiency and increase cane production.",""],[1,"111","15","Sugar Cane Production Support Programme","In the next five years, the government will support FSC and farmers to raise cane production to 3 million tonnes each year.",""],[1,"111","15","Farm Access Roads, Cane Replanting and Fertiliser Subsidy Programmes","Existing programmes on farm access roads, cane replanting and fertiliser subsidy will continue to ensure that production costs remain stable.",""],[1,"111","15","FSC Own-Farm Investment Programme","In addition, FSC will invest in establishing its own farms.",""],[1,"112","1","FSC Operational Review and Restructuring","each aspect of its operation will be reviewed including organisational structure, milling efficiency, state of infrastructure and assets.",""],[1,"112","2","FSC Market Development Support for Sugar Competitiveness","Government will support FSC in developing new markets in order to support the revitalisation of the industry.",""],[1,"112","4","Sugar Industry Governance Reform","Improve industry governance through introduction of relevant legislation to support reform and reorganisation for growth of the industry.",""],[1,"112","4","Sugar Market Diversification Initiative","Secure new sugar markets.",""],[1,"112","4","Youth Engagement in Sugar Cane Farming Programme","Promote programmes to entice young and active famers into sugar cane farming.",""],[1,"112","4","FSC Owned Farms Establishment","Establish FSC owned farms to support production.",""],[1,"112","4","Sugar Cane Mechanisation Support Programme","Increase support for and adoption of mechanisation.",""],[1,"112","4","Sugar Cane Production Expansion Target","Increase cane production to 3.0 million tonnes per annum by 2022/23.",""],[1,"112","4","Mechanical Harvesting and Rail Transfer Infrastructure","Introduction of mechanical harvesting and establishment of lorry to rail transfer stations.",""],[1,"112","4","Cane Quality Payment System Implementation","Full implementation of the cane quality payment system by 2022/23.",""]],"25":[[1,"107","3","Agricultural Market Linkage and Farmer Support Strategy","Strategies will be implemented to improve production and better facilitate linkages between the agriculture sector and the market.",""],[1,"107","3","Rural Farmer Cluster Farming and Extension Support","This will assist in better organising rural farmers through cluster farming, provision of extension services, farm-access roads, irrigation, mechanisation, marketing support and export development.",""],[1,"107","3","Agriculture Marketing Authority Strengthening","The role of the Agriculture Marketing Authority will be strengthened to provide effective marketing support without crowding out the private sector.",""],[1,"107","6","Equal Access to Agricultural Production Factors Policy","There will be equal access by all to the factors of agricultural production.",""],[1,"108","4","MSME Development Support","Support development of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME).",""],[1,"108","4","Rural Transformation Centres","Establish rural transformation centres.",""],[1,"108","4","Inter-Island Maritime Connectivity Improvement","Inter-island shipping routes reviewed as well as improvement in inter island maritime infrastructure and frequency of services.",""],[1,"108","6","Rural and Maritime Collection Centre Access Expansion","Increase access to collection centres (agriculture, fisheries, and handicrafts) in rural and maritime areas.",""],[1,"108","6","Formal Savings and Credit Access Expansion","Increase access to formal savings and credit financial services, including rural banking, microfinance and savings and credit unions.",""],[1,"108","6","Market Access and Connectivity Infrastructure Upgrading","Increased market access and connectivity by upgrading infrastructure and the provision of basic services and amenities.",""],[1,"108","7","Land-Use Plan Guideline Development","Formulate a land-use plan guideline.",""],[1,"108","7","Integrated Community Capacity Building Mechanism","Review the existing government institutional mechanisms and develop integrated community capacity building programmes at grassroots level in collaboration with NGOs.",""],[1,"108","7","Sex- and Age-Disaggregated Data and Unpaid Work Research","Ensure the examination of sex and age disaggregated data and increase research on unpaid work in various sectors, including agriculture and family businesses, within the formal and informal contexts, as a basis for the allocation of resources for the training and development of unpaid workers.",""],[1,"108","8","Cooperative Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen cooperatives' institutional capacities.",""],[1,"108","9","Integration of Overlapping Community Projects under Cooperatives","Integrate overlapping community projects Integrated Human Resource Development Programme, Agriculture programmes, youth programmes, women's project) under the legal structure of cooperatives.",""],[1,"108","9","Decentralized Cooperatives Training and Capacity Building","Decentralize cooperatives training and capacity building in all divisions and provinces.",""]],"26":[[1,"11","11","Business Climate Improvement for Private Investment","The business climate, including administrative and regulatory processes, will be further improved to facilitate private sector investment, including enticing more foreign investment.",""],[1,"11","11","Regional Marketing Exploration for Tourism","Options will be explored for regional marketing in areas like tourism.",""],[1,"19","6","Regulatory Framework Administration Improvement","The regulatory environment for private-sector development has been improved through more effective administration of regulatory frameworks for land use, development control and building permissions.",""],[1,"19","6","Business-Friendly Tax Administration Reform","Tax administration has been made more business friendly,",""],[1,"19","7","Investment Incentives and Subsidies for Priority Sectors","Incentives, and where necessary subsidies, have been provided to spur investment and meet basic needs, particularly in areas like renewable energy and infrastructure development, and to support growth in key economic sectors such as ICT, tourism, manufacturing and agriculture.",""],[1,"20","1","Land Administration Efficiency Reform","The next area of focus is on the review of administrative processes, digitisation of land records and capacity-building to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of land-use administration.",""],[1,"20","3","Competition Framework and Market Liberalisation Measures","interventions to ensure competitive market behaviour in certain sectors will continue; however, progressive liberalisation (de-listing from the basket) will also be considered.",""],[1,"72","18","Business Environment Improvement for Private Sector Investment","The business environment will be improved to further reduce the cost of doing business and support private sector investments in the country.",""],[1,"72","18","Manufacturing and Services Sector Support Programme","Manufacturing and service sectors will be supported and new growth sectors will be nurtured and harnessed.",""],[1,"72","18","Niche Product and Comparative Advantage Development Incentives","Niche-product development and areas of comparative advantage will be incentivised and further developed.",""],[1,"72","21","Resource-Based Sector Development and Value Addition Initiative","Resource-based sectors will be developed with a major focus on value addition, efficiency gains and raising overall production.",""],[1,"72","21","Trade Promotion and Partnership Enhancement","Trade will be promoted and regional and multilateral partnerships will be enhanced.",""],[1,"92","7","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform Package","Government is continuously working towards improving the enabling environment for the private sector to thrive and expand.",""],[1,"92","7","Tax Reduction and Business Regulation Simplification","Tax rates have been reduced substantially, registration and licensing requirements are being streamlined, the new Companies Act has been enacted, business-opening hours have been relaxed, private sector participation in strategic areas is being pursued and supportive infrastructure is being developed.",""],[1,"92","8","Investment Policy and Regulatory Framework Review","The policy and regulatory framework for investment will be reviewed to entice more investment.",""],[1,"92","8","Investment Policy and Legislation Review with IFC","Government is working with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) on the review of the Investment Policy and legislation.",""],[1,"92","8","Single-Window Clearance Platform Strengthening","The implementation of the single-window clearance platform for tier 1 agencies will be strengthened and tier 2 agencies will be expedited.",""],[1,"92","8","Ease of Doing Business Technical Assistance","Government has engaged Singapore Cooperation Enterprise to provide technical assistance to improve the ease of doing business.",""],[1,"92","9","E-Government Enhancement of Regulatory Approval Processes","Approvals processes for regulatory agencies in the provision of services such as registration, land-use administration, development control, environmental protection, employment relations and tax administration will be enhanced through e-government.",""],[1,"92","11","Building Permits Approval Streamlining Reform","the Regulation of Building Permits Act 2017 has been passed and will provide a fast-track and streamlined process to enhance the existing building permits approvals process",""],[1,"92","13","Competition Policy Framework Enhancement","The competition policy framework will be enhanced to promote greater self-regulation and compliance and reduce restrictive trade practices.",""],[1,"93","18","Investment Policy and Legal Framework Review","Review Investment Policy and Legal Framework.",""],[1,"93","18","Client Relationship Management Database for Investments","Client Relationship Management Database on investments.",""],[1,"93","18","Single Window Clearance for Tier 1 and Tier 2 Agencies","Single Window Clearance for Tier 1 and Tier 2 Agencies.",""],[1,"95","14","Review of Restrictive Business Regulations","Review restrictive regulations under business regulatory framework",""],[1,"95","15","Review of Restrictive Business Regulations","Review restrictive regulations under business regulatory framework",""]],"27":[[1,"7","5","Growth Sector Nurturing and Connectivity Improvement","New and emerging growth sectors will be nurtured, connectivity within and to the outside world will be improved, new technologies will be embraced, productivity will be maximised, human capital development will be accelerated and green growth will be a key guiding principle in the implementation of this Plan.",""],[1,"11","5","New Growth Sector Development","Moving forward, new growth sectors will be nurtured to enable the economy to thrive and create more jobs.",""],[1,"11","5","Sector Expansion and Modernisation Programme","Existing sectors will be expanded and modernised.",""],[1,"11","5","Large-Scale Commercialisation and SME Development","Large-scale commercialisation will be pursued together with Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) development.",""],[1,"11","10","Service Sector Expansion and Manufacturing Support","Service sectors such as financial services and insurance will be expanded, and new manufacturing sectors will be supported.",""],[1,"11","11","Infrastructure and Enabling Services Provision","Government will provide the necessary infrastructure and enabling services.",""],[1,"17","2","Public Infrastructure Investment Programme","Infrastructure is continually improving through substantial public sector investment.",""],[1,"23","3","Substantial Investments for Transformational Strategic Thrusts","Government will concurrently undertake substantial investments to implement the transformational strategic thrusts identified under the long-term development plan.",""]],"28":[[1,"11","6","Niche Export Products and Services Development","Development of niche products and services for export will be pursued.",""],[1,"11","7","Value Addition Development in Resource-Based Sectors","Value addition will be further developed in resource-based sectors such as forestry, fisheries and agriculture to support new manufacturing industries.",""],[1,"11","7","Ecotourism Development Initiative","Ecotourism to promote our unique flora and fauna, cultural diversity and adventure tourism such as whale and dolphin watching will be",""],[1,"11","13","National Branding Campaign Enhancement","National branding campaigns such as the Fijian Made and Buy Fijian initiatives will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"19","7","Fijian Made National Branding Initiative","These initiatives complement national branding initiatives like 'Fijian Made'.",""],[1,"19","9","National Trade Policy Framework","The National Trade Policy Framework provides the policy settings and institutional framework to address challenges such as market access, trade facilitation and export growth.",""],[1,"19","9","Tariff Policy Review Process","Government has been undertaking tariff policy reviews consistent with its economic development aspirations and priorities.",""],[1,"131","18","Trade and Political Partnership Expansion","Fiji continues its policy to seek beneficial trade and political relationships with new and non-traditional partners and is engaged in discussions with China on a bilateral trade arrangement.",""],[1,"131","19","United Kingdom Economic Partnership Agreement Mirroring and IEPA Improvement Discussions","The Interim Economic Partnership Agreement between Fiji/Papua New Guinea and the European Union (EU) will be mirrored with the United Kingdom, in light of Britain's exit from the EU.",""],[1,"131","21","National Export Strategy Support for Priority Sectors","Export development will be supported through raising competitiveness, diversification and value addition under the National Export Strategy (NES) in priority sectors.",""],[1,"132","1","Trade Opportunity Development Initiative","new opportunities for trade between Fiji and Europe, the USA, Singapore, and other Asian countries will be developed.",""],[1,"132","2","Trade Promotion and Facilitation through Trade Commissions","Trade promotion and facilitation will be pursued through our trade commissions based in key markets, in collaboration with relevant domestic stakeholders.",""],[1,"132","4","Trade Capacity and Competitiveness Strengthening Initiative","Government will seek to improve Fiji's trading position and competitiveness through training, research and institution-building and continue to seek access to Aid for Trade from development partners to assist in building trade capacity and infrastructure.",""],[1,"132","12","Trade Agreement Engagement and Market Access Promotion","Facilitate the engagement of Fiji in multilateral, regional and bilateral trade agreements/arrangements.",""],[1,"133","3","Trade Negotiations and Preferential Trade Arrangement Enhancement","Trade negotiations: Comprehensive EPA, PACER Plus, Melanesian Free Trade Agreement, revision of PICTA trade in goods rules of origin, enhancement of the United States GSP scheme and preferential trade arrangement with China",""],[1,"133","9","Trade Promotion Missions to Potential Markets","Trade Promotion (trade and investment mission to potential markets each year)",""],[1,"133","10","Trade Commissions Establishment","Establishment of trade commissions",""]],"29":[[1,"11","8","Traditional Handicrafts and Local Product Promotion Programme","Promotion of traditional handicrafts, natural body products, local ceramic ware, and exotic herbs and spices will be nurtured and expanded, offering more opportunities for women to use their traditional skills to expand opportunities for economic empowerment.",""],[1,"11","12","MSME Support and Incentive Programme","Government, together with the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) Council, will continue to support and incentivise MSMEs and thereby create more jobs and encourage inclusive growth.",""],[1,"11","12","MSME Capacity Building Services","Training, mentoring, access to finance and advisory services will be enhanced to harness the true potential of the MSME sector.",""],[1,"11","12","Secured Transactions and MSME Credit Guarantee Scheme","The secured transactions framework to allow use of movable property as collateral, and government's MSME financing and credit guarantee scheme, will improve financing and growth of MSMEs.",""],[1,"11","12","MSME Market Access Improvement Measures","Access to markets through improvements in infrastructure and marketing services will be developed.",""],[1,"19","10","MSME Sector Strengthening","strengthening the MSME sector.",""],[1,"72","18","MSME Development Strengthening Initiative","MSME development will be strengthened for job creation and income generation.",""],[1,"96","1","MSME Institutional Support, Finance, Incubation and Market Linkage Programme","In the next 5 years, interventions will focus on improving the institutional setting, access to finance, business incubation and training and connecting MSMEs to markets.",""],[1,"96","2","Central Coordinating Agency for MSME Development","A Central Coordinating Agency will be established to develop, implement, monitor and evaluate MSME development in collaboration with various stakeholders.",""],[1,"96","2","MSME Financing, Training, Mentoring, and Data Support","The primary focus will be on coordinating financing, facilitating business training, mentoring, advisory and incubation, and data-collection support.",""],[1,"96","5","Roadside Stalls Project","A 'Roadside Stalls Project' will be piloted to provide vendors along the highway in the areas outside of municipalities with standardized stalls to sell their produce.",""],[1,"96","8","MSME Registration Database","A database will be established to register MSMEs to ensure availability of reliable data that will assist in policymaking.",""],[1,"96","8","Business Incubation and Skills Training Support","More funding and other resources will be channelled towards business incubation, skills training and other support services.",""],[1,"97","1","MSME Business Regulatory Reform","Reform of MSME business regulatory environment.",""],[1,"97","2","National MSME Council Establishment","Establishment of a National MSME Council.",""],[1,"97","2","MSME Central Coordinating Agency Establishment","Establishment of a new MSME Central Coordinating Agency.",""],[1,"97","2","MSME Legislative and Strategic Framework Review","Review the legislative and strategic framework for MSMEs in line with the recommendations of the Financial Sector Development Plan (FSDP).",""],[1,"97","2","Fiji Development Bank Review","Review of Fiji Development Bank.",""],[1,"97","2","MSME Data System Development","Review of current data sources on MSMEs and establishment of new MSME database.",""],[1,"97","5","Business Training Access Improvement","Improve access to business training.",""],[1,"97","6","Expansion of Business Training Services for Entrepreneurs","Expand the reach of business training services to more entrepreneurs across all divisions.",""],[1,"97","6","Entrepreneurship Innovation Training and Mentoring Programme","Encourage and support business innovation through entrepreneurship training and mentoring",""],[1,"97","6","Entrepreneur Refresher Courses and Trainer Development Programme","Develop refresher courses for entrepreneurs and training of trainers.",""],[1,"97","6","Online MSME Resource Portal","Establish an online MSME resource page with easy to access resources regarding business operations and planning.",""],[1,"97","8","SME Development Act Review","Review of SME Development Act 2002",""],[1,"97","8","National MSME Council Establishment","Establish National MSME Council",""],[1,"97","8","MSME Central Coordinating Agency Establishment","Establish MSME Central Coordinating Agency",""],[1,"97","9","Secured Transactions Framework Implementation","Implement the secured transactions framework",""],[1,"97","9","SME Development Act Review","Review of SME Development Act 2002",""],[1,"97","9","FDB Review","Review of FDB",""],[1,"97","10","Secured Transactions Framework Implementation","Implement the secured transactions framework",""],[1,"101","6","Secured Transactions Act Implementation","Implement the Secured Transactions Act.",""],[1,"101","6","MSME Listing Incentive Scheme","Encourage Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises (MSME) listings on SPSE through tax incentives.",""],[1,"101","6","SME Credit Guarantee Scheme Expansion","Expand Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) Credit Guarantee Scheme.",""],[1,"101","6","Bank Account Opening Simplification","Simplify procedures for opening a bank account.",""],[1,"101","6","Rural Agent Network Deployment for Financial Services","Facilitate and enhance the deployment of reliable and secure agent networks for financial services in rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"101","6","Inclusive Microfinance and Insurance Access Expansion","Improve access to microfinance and inclusive insurance products and services for low-income groups, and rural and marginalised communities.",""],[1,"101","6","Digital Financial Services Promotion","Encourage the use of digital financial services.",""],[1,"101","6","Climate and Disaster Insurance Product Development","Work with the insurance sector to develop insurance packages for climate and disaster related adversities.",""],[1,"101","7","Credit Union Development and Strengthening","Develop and strengthen Credit Unions.",""],[1,"101","8","Credit Union Legislative and Institutional Framework Review","Review the legislative and institutional framework for credit unions.",""],[1,"101","13","Secured Transactions Legislation Reform","Develop and enact secured transaction legislation",""],[1,"101","15","Credit Union Development and Strengthening","Develop and strengthen credit unions",""],[1,"101","16","Credit Union Legislative and Institutional Framework Review","Review the legislative and institutional framework for credit unions",""],[1,"101","17","Credit Union Act Review and Reform Roadmap","Complete review of Credit Union Act 1954 Map a way forward for credit unions",""],[1,"101","18","Credit Union Legislative Reform and Roadmap Development","Revised legislative framework and development of roadmap for credit unions.",""]],"30":[[1,"8","1","Multisectoral Poverty Reduction and Social Protection Initiative","A new measure of poverty that incorporates relevant and measurable social determinants will be developed to help guide improvements to service delivery.",""],[1,"18","9","Social Protection Programme Expansion","Social protection programmes have been expanded from welfare allowances to support the living expenses of needy families, the elderly and disabled persons.",""],[1,"18","9","Targeted Assistance for Education, Maternal Health, Utilities, and Medicines","In addition, targeted assistance is provided to support education, the health of pregnant women in rural areas, subsidies to access basic utilities, and access to essential medicine.",""],[1,"54","4","Social Inclusion and Basic Amenities Support Programmes","Social inclusion programmes such as the poverty benefit scheme, welfare graduation programme and social pension scheme will be maintained.",""],[1,"54","4","Targeted Assistance for Vulnerable Groups","Targeted assistance will be provided to the vulnerable, including children living in poverty, children in orphanages and foster care, people with disabilities and special needs, and the elderly.",""],[1,"55","3","Review of State Social Protection Systems","Review state social protection systems for the protection and care of vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"55","3","Family-Based Elderly Support Promotion","Encourage in-family support for the elderly.",""],[1,"55","8","Awareness Programme on Child Safety","Awareness Programme on Child Safety (APCS)",""],[1,"56","20","National Policy for Children","Develop National Policy for Children",""],[1,"142","12","Social Safety Nets Strengthening and Cultural Mapping Programme","strengthening of social safety nets including cash transfers, and cultural mapping programme implemented in 14 provinces.",""]],"31":[[1,"10","8","Women's Leadership and Decision-Making Empowerment Initiative","Women will be empowered, allowing them opportunities for greater participation in leadership and decision- making across all sectors.",""],[1,"10","8","Gender-Based Violence Response by Police and Courts","Police and the courts will appropriately attend to gender-based violence in all its forms.",""],[1,"10","8","Gender-Based Violence Reporting Improvement Target","100 percent reporting of these crimes is expected.",""],[1,"10","8","Responsive Law and Justice System Strengthening","The law and justice system that protects the public and deters crime will be functional and responsive.",""],[1,"10","9","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Measures","Gender inequality and discrimination will be eliminated, providing women with greater choice and freedom for their participation in the family and society.",""],[1,"10","10","Support for Women’s Paid Work and Shared Care Responsibilities","Women who choose to have children will be adequately remunerated for paid work and will be able to continue to advance their careers if that is their wish.",""],[1,"10","11","Women's Health and Family Planning Support","Support for women's health and decisions regarding family planning and sexual and reproductive health will be shared and respected.",""],[1,"10","11","Improved Access to Health and Social Services","Access to health and other social services will be improved and available as required.",""],[1,"10","11","Women's Participation in Development Project Planning","Women will be included and consulted in all planning for future development projects, and their input will be translated into tangible project outcomes.",""],[1,"10","11","Community-Level Adaptation Planning with Women as Change Agents","This includes adaptation planning at the community level, where women can be key agents to change unsustainable production and consumption practices within the family and community.",""],[1,"10","12","Gender-Based Violence Response Policy and Programmes","Response to Gender Based Violence (GBV) continues to be a strong focus of government policy and programmes.",""],[1,"10","12","GBV Service Delivery Protocols for the Health Sector","GBV service delivery protocols will ensure that the health sector provides strong support to victims.",""],[1,"19","1","National Gender Policy Implementation","Fiji has incorporated significant elements of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (CEDAW) into its laws and policies and is implementing the National Gender Policy and the Women's Plan of Action.",""],[1,"19","1","Domestic Violence Legislation Enforcement","Domestic violence legislation has been developed and utilised by the Fiji Police Force and courts as part of an overarching approach to bring down the amount of violence experienced by women and children.",""],[1,"19","2","24-Hour Toll-Free GBV Survivor Hotline","the establishment of a toll-free 24-hours' hotline to provide counselling and appropriate referral for survivors of GBV as well as to avenues for redress",""]],"34":[[1,"8","5","Adoption of Innovative Technologies for Water and Industrial Resource Management","Innovative technologies will be adopted for industrial recycling, rainwater harvesting and storage, storm water and aquifer management and use of renewable energy for desalination plants.",""],[1,"8","5","Climate-Resilient Water Infrastructure Programme","Building climate resilient water infrastructure will be a key aspect of all new projects.",""],[1,"8","5","Leak Reduction and Water Conservation Programme","Leak reduction programmes will continue so that piped- water losses are significantly reduced, and other water conservation initiatives will be pursued.",""],[1,"8","6","Freshwater Aquifer Protection Adaptation Measures","adaptation measures will be implemented to protect freshwater aquifers from saltwater intrusion.",""],[1,"8","6","Water Conservation Public Awareness and Education Campaign","Public awareness and education on water conservation and management will be increased to support adaptation to changes in seasonal rainfall patterns that may occur due to climate change.",""],[1,"23","9","Long-Term Water Supply Investment Programme","In the next 5 years, government will undertake major investments to cater for long-term water supply needs.",""],[1,"23","9","Water Leakage Reduction Programme","An aggressive leakage reduction programme to eliminate water loss will be pursued.",""],[1,"23","11","Water Infrastructure Renewal Programme","Investments will be made to renew existing water infrastructure, including pipeline replacement, construction and upgrade of water reticulation systems, electrical upgrades, valve replacements, reservoir upgrades and reducing non-revenue water.",""],[1,"23","14","Water Conservation Awareness and Strategy Initiative","Awareness and strategies for water conservation policies will be pursued to raise civic responsibility on the use of water and protection of water sources.",""],[1,"24","4","Climate-Resilient Water and Sewerage Infrastructure Upgrade","water and sewerage infrastructure will be made more climate-resilient, and freshwater resources will be protected from pollution and unsustainable use.",""],[1,"24","11","Green Growth Framework for Fiji Implementation","Implement Green Growth Framework for Fiji, in particular the Way Forward outlined in Thematic Area 6 on Freshwater Resources and Sanitation Management.",""],[1,"24","11","Renewable Energy-Based Desalination Technology Development","Water Authority of Fiji, Department of Water and Sewerage and Department of Energy to work with research institutions and academia to develop renewable energy based desalination technologies where financially and economically viable.","Water Authority of Fiji | Department of Water and Sewerage | Department of Energy"],[1,"24","11","Water Resources Education and Awareness Programme","Develop education and awareness programmes on the management and use of water resources in order to assist users in becoming more efficient in water use.",""],[1,"24","11","Water Cost Recovery Improvement","Improve cost recovery.",""],[1,"24","11","Water Catchment Management for Freshwater Protection","Employ water catchment management to ensure the protection of Fiji's sustainable freshwater resources from risk of pollution and other contaminants and other catchment security.",""],[1,"24","11","Freshwater Aquifer Saltwater Intrusion Adaptation Measures","Implement adaptation measures to protect freshwater aquifers from saltwater intrusion.",""],[1,"24","11","Ecosystem-Sensitive Water Infrastructure Development","Develop water infrastructure that minimizes ecosystem impacts.",""],[1,"27","2","Construction of Water Package Plants","Construction of 11 water package plants",""]],"35":[[1,"8","2","Universal Clean and Safe Water Access Expansion","Every Fijian has a right to clean and safe water in adequate quantities.",""],[1,"23","13","Rural Water Supply Programme Expansion","The rural water supply programme will be augmented to provide access to clean water in rural areas",""],[1,"23","13","Free Water Tank Distribution for Rural and Maritime Communities","Free water tanks will be distributed in the rural and maritime communities.",""],[1,"23","13","Remote Island Groundwater and Desalination Development","For the remote island communities, groundwater sources will be developed and diesel-powered water-desalination plants will be provided.",""]],"36":[[1,"8","7","Urban Sewerage System Expansion","Public sewerage treatment systems will be built and expanded in all urban centres.",""],[1,"8","7","Rural Sewerage and Sanitation Options Development","Sustainable and viable sewerage and sanitation options will also be explored for rural areas.",""],[1,"23","16","Sanitation Services Improvement","Sanitation services will be improved",""],[1,"24","1","Septic Tank Upgrade to Standardized Treatment Systems Investment","in the next 5 years with investments to support migration from septic tanks to standardised treatment systems.",""],[1,"24","2","Urban Sewerage Plant Construction and Expansion","Sewerage plants with larger treatment capacities and efficient technologies will be constructed in urban areas.",""],[1,"24","3","Small Sewerage Treatment Plant Construction","government will construct smaller sewerage treatment plants.",""],[1,"24","8","Water and Sanitation Service Equity Expansion","Expand access and work towards ensuring equity in the provision of water and sanitation services to all Fijians.",""],[1,"24","9","Sewerage Discharge Standards Rationalisation","Rationalise environmental legislation surrounding sewerage discharge standards to balance affordability in compliance with short-term and long-term environmental and health effects with concentration on trade waste monitoring.",""],[1,"24","9","Septic Tank Transition Strategy","Implement necessary strategies to migrate from the use of individual septic tanks to standardised treatment systems.",""],[1,"24","9","Regional Centralised Sewerage Plant Construction","Construct regional centralised sewerage plants with larger treatment capacities and efficient technologies.",""],[1,"24","9","Sanitation Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the institutional framework and enhance capacity in supplying basic sanitation facilities.",""]],"37":[[1,"72","21","Tourism Sector Expansion Programme","The tourism industry will be expanded with a focus on increasing source markets and also meeting the developing and diverse needs of tourists.",""],[1,"127","6","Investment Promotion and Facilitation","Facilitating and promoting domestic and foreign investment;",""],[1,"127","7","Tourism-Related Infrastructure Investment","Investing in tourism-related infrastructure;",""],[1,"127","13","Tourism Diversification into Niche Segments","In the next 5 years, Fiji will expand its tourism industry to niche segments, such as sports tourism, cruise tourism, wedding and honeymoon tourism, hosting of conferences and entertainment events, wellness tourism, and adventure tourism.",""],[1,"127","13","International Events Attraction Initiative","The Fijian Government will continue to bring international events such as rugby competitions, golf tournaments, sailing regattas and formal conferences and meetings to Fiji.",""],[1,"127","14","Film Production Studio Development and Incentive Support","The Fijian Government, in partnership with the private sector, is also exploring the possibility of developing large production studios, securing specialised equipment for hire by foreign crews, nurturing local acting and production talent and continuing to offer attractive tax rebates for production of films and television shows in Fiji.",""],[1,"127","15","MSME Support for Tourism and Niche Activities","Apart from supporting large-scale hotel development and related facilities, micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) in the tourism sector will continue to be supported.",""],[1,"127","15","Tourism Niche Product Development","Other niche activities, such as dolphin and whale watching, village tours, river rafting and zip lining, snorkelling and boating, eco-tourism and promoting Fiji's cultural and heritage sites will support MSMEs and local communities.",""],[1,"127","15","MSME Training, Mentoring, and Incubation Support","MSMEs will also be provided training, mentoring, incubation and other business development support services through the MSME Central Coordinating Agency.",""],[1,"127","16","Local Agricultural and Fisheries Market Linkage Development","Market linkages that enable the supply of local agricultural and fisheries produce to the tourism industry will be facilitated and developed.",""],[1,"127","16","High-End Niche Product Manufacturing Promotion","Manufacturing of high- end niche products such as natural body products, exotic herbs and spices, local confectionaries, local fruit juices, handicrafts and packed organic goods will be promoted.",""],[1,"127","16","Retail Sector Development and Buy Fijian Campaign Support","Retail-sector development that provides unique shopping experiences and promotes the Fijian Made-Buy Fijian Campaign will also continue to be supported.",""],[1,"127","18","Tourism Fiji Marketing Grant","Government will continue to provide a marketing grant to Tourism Fiji.",""],[1,"127","18","Pacific Tourism Destination Marketing Initiative","Fiji will participate in initiatives to market the Pacific as a tourism destination that would benefit Fiji and the region.",""],[1,"127","19","Tourism Satellite Accounts Preparation","the Tourism Satellite Accounts (TSA) will be prepared by the Fijian Bureau of Statistics on a two-year interval",""]],"38":[[1,"12","8","Road Transport Energy Efficiency and Clean Vehicle Support","Road transportation will be made more energy-efficient and environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"13","14","Technology Import Facilitation and Infrastructure Support","A facilitative environment will be created to assist the importation of new and modern technology.",""],[1,"73","8","Transport Emission Standards and Energy Efficiency Measures","Emission standards and energy efficiency for transport will be a key priority.",""],[1,"73","8","Vehicle Fleet Replacement with Hybrid and Electric Vehicles","The replacement of existing uneconomical vehicles with hybrid and electric vehicles will be supported.",""],[1,"73","8","Low-Carbon Fuel Use in Land Transport","Fuel savings through the use of biofuel, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) and liquefied natural gas (LNG) in land transport will be supported, as will be the use of cycling lanes.",""],[1,"73","8","Cycling Lane Expansion","Fuel savings through the use of biofuel, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) and liquefied natural gas (LNG) in land transport will be supported, as will be the use of cycling lanes.",""],[1,"75","3","National Vehicle Fleet Regulation and Transport Demand Alignment","Encourage the development of a national road vehicle fleet that is well matched to transport demand, as well as to the road network and if necessary regulate the composition of the national vehicle fleet where there is incompatibility with the road infrastructure, excessive environmental disturbance, unacceptable safety risk or the need to encourage long-term change in transport modes.",""],[1,"75","3","Public Transport Network Design Feasibility Studies","Feasibility studies to be undertaken to: (i) explore the viability of implementing public transport network design for an efficient and equitable public transport system; (ii) introducing peak period public transport zoning for high demand corridors; (iii) proper vehicle de-registration and scrapping of vehicles to maintain national fleet composition at manageable levels; and (iv) encouraging car-pooling.",""],[1,"75","18","Transport Management Systems through Bus Rapid Transit and Carpooling","Adopting better transport management systems through bus rapid transit (BRT) and carpooling; and",""],[1,"75","19","Public Transport Promotion","Promoting the use of public transport.",""],[1,"76","19","Green Growth Framework Implementation for Sustainable Transportation","Implementation of Green Growth Framework for Fiji, in particular the Way Forward outlined in Thematic Area 8 on Sustainable Transportation.",""],[1,"76","19","Environmental Practice Codes for Road and Bridge Works","Develop Codes of Environmental Practice (COEPs) for road and bridge works that will set out environmental standards and appropriate procedures to mitigate the environmental impact of the planning, design, construction, operation and maintenance of urban and rural roads and bridges.",""],[1,"76","19","Integrated Transport Assessment Policy and Guidelines","Fiji Roads Authority (FRA) to develop the Integrated Transport Assessment (ITA) policy and guidelines in consultation with the Transport Planning Unit (TPU) and other stakeholders, such as the Ministry of Local Government and the municipal councils that will apply to any new developments, or changes","Fiji Roads Authority (FRA) | Transport Planning Unit (TPU) | Ministry of Local Government"],[1,"76","19","Integrated Transport Planning Framework","LTA to explore and implement Integrated Transport Planning Framework under the three pillars of to development. sustainable development.",""],[1,"76","19","Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure Development","Explore the viability of developing electric vehicle charging infrastructure.",""],[1,"76","19","Public Transport Network Development","Develop a public transport network designed to accommodate land use and mobility patterns of the travelling public.",""],[1,"76","19","Green Vehicle Promotion for Public and Commercial Transport","Explore the use of green vehicles for PSVs and commercial vehicles.",""],[1,"76","19","Heavy Goods Vehicle Restriction in Inner City Areas","LTA to look into whether there is a need to restrict heavy goods vehicle movement in the inner city",""],[1,"76","19","Zero-Tolerance Emissions Enforcement for Land Transport","Stringent enforcement and zero tolerance on emission levels for land transport.",""],[1,"78","18","Suva Bus Rapid Transit Project","Suva Bus Rapid Transit Project to be constructed by 2020",""]],"39":[[1,"11","14","National Transport Network Modernisation","We will also continue to modernise Fiji's air, maritime and land transport networks and weather recording, forecasting and reporting services to meet our long term needs and aspirations.",""],[1,"12","1","Road Infrastructure Modernisation Investment","Modernising our road infrastructure will continue to support strong economic expansion, rising income levels, the increase in urban population and the growth in agriculture and industries.",""],[1,"12","2","Road Development and Improvement Programme","New roads will be developed and existing ones improved.",""],[1,"12","2","Road Expansion and Four-Lane Upgrade Projects","More road expansions, including four-lane projects, will be undertaken.",""],[1,"12","2","Completion of Existing Four-Lane Road Projects","Current four-lane projects such as Nausori airport to Suva and Nadi airport to Denarau will be completed by 2018.",""],[1,"12","2","Gravel Road Sealing Programme","Government will embark on major projects to seal a large portion of the existing gravel roads over the next 20 years.",""],[1,"12","3","Inland Road Diversion for Land Development","Where practical, consideration will be given to diverting roads inland to open up land for social and economic development.",""],[1,"12","4","Streetlight Installation and Expansion Programme","Installation of streetlights in all major urban centres and peri-urban areas and in front of villages and settlements along the Queens and Kings Roads will continue.",""],[1,"12","5","Footpath Construction for Road Safety","New footpaths will be constructed across populated areas, major cities and towns to make roads safer for pedestrians and drivers.",""],[1,"12","6","Traffic Light Installation at Critical Junctions","Traffic lights will be installed at critical junctions where there are high traffic flows.",""],[1,"12","6","Expansion of Car Parks and Bus Bays","To accommodate the rising number of vehicles, investments in larger car parks and the expansion of bus bays on high-traffic roads will be facilitated.",""],[1,"12","7","Bridge Upgrading and Construction Programme","Investment in upgrading our bridges and constructing new ones will continue.",""],[1,"12","7","Rural Access Road Development","This will include development of access roads to connect farming areas to markets.",""],[1,"14","1","Modern Traffic Management and Dedicated Freight and Bus Lanes","investment in modern traffic management software and equipment, as well as dedicated bus and truck lanes.",""],[1,"14","7","Urban Beautification and Traffic Management Improvement","Cities will be beautified with development of recreation facilities and parks, urban gardens and better zoning.",""],[1,"14","7","Traffic Management Plan Enhancement","Traffic management plans will be enhanced to ease traffic congestion.",""],[1,"72","22","Road Infrastructure Modernisation Programme","The government has already embarked on modernising the infrastructure with substantial funding to improve our roads, bridges, jetties, streetlights and footpaths over recent years.",""],[1,"73","2","Road Network Improvement Investment Programme","In the next 5 years, more investments will be made to further improve our road network.",""],[1,"73","2","Road Upgrading and Sealing Programme","Existing roads will be upgraded and sealed.",""],[1,"73","2","Nadi-to-Lautoka Four-Lane Corridor Project","Options are being explored for a four-lane project in the Nadi-to-Lautoka corridor.",""],[1,"73","2","Bridge and Jetty Upgrading and Rehabilitation Programme","The upgrading and rehabilitation programme for bridges and jetties will be pursued on a bigger scale.",""],[1,"73","6","Rural and Maritime Island Roads Upgrade Programme","Resources will be allocated to develop rural and maritime- island roads and other unsealed roads throughout Fiji.",""],[1,"73","6","Rural Transport Infrastructure Upgrade Programme","Irish crossings, suspension bridges, rural jetties, waiting sheds and foot crossings will be upgraded and constructed.",""],[1,"74","2","Rural Road Network Expansion","Expansion of the rural road network.",""],[1,"74","3","Farm Road Policy and Rural Road Standards Review","Review of the existing policies and legislation surrounding the management of farm roads and re- examine the standards for construction of rural roads.",""],[1,"74","3","Augmented Rural and Maritime Roads Programme","Implement an augmented programme for roads in rural and maritime areas that will also include construction of Irish crossings, suspension bridges, jetties, waiting sheds and foot crossings.",""],[1,"74","4","Road Network Maintenance, Rehabilitation and Upgrading Programme","Further development of full road network to international standards with a greater emphasis on maintenance, rehabilitation and upgrading.",""],[1,"74","5","Roads, Bridges and Jetties Upgrading and Maintenance Investment Programme","Continue with high levels of investment to reduce the backlog in the upgrading, replacement and maintenance of roads, bridges and jetty networks.",""],[1,"74","5","Major Roads Programme Continuation","Continue implementation of existing major roads programmes including the FRA Maintenance Bridges and Jetties. Programme, Renewals and Replacements of Roads and Services, and Upgrading and Replacement of .",""],[1,"74","5","Four-Lane Road Completion Projects","Completion of the four-lane projects from Suva to Nausori Airport and Denarau Road to Nadi",""],[1,"74","5","Four-Lane Feasibility Study and Extension Planning","Complete feasibility study of four-lanes to other stretches like Nadi to Lautoka with construction to Airport by 2018.",""],[1,"77","8","Lomaloma Slip Repair","Repair of Lomaloma Slip to be completed",""],[1,"77","21","Vanua Levu Transinsular 2 Road Construction","Construction of Vanua Levu Transinsular 2 Road",""],[1,"77","21","Nausori to Korovou Road Upgrading","Nausori to Korovou Road Upgrading",""],[1,"77","21","School and Healthcare Access Roads Programme","School and Healthcare Access Roads to be",""],[1,"77","21","Community Road Tar Sealing Programme","Tar sealing of roads in front of communities",""],[1,"77","21","Valaga Bay/Mid-Point Jetty Construction","Valaga Bay/Mid-Point Jetty Construction to start",""],[1,"78","20","Nadi to Lautoka Road Upgrade to Four Lanes","Nadi to Lautoka Upgraded (sections to be Four Lane) by 2020",""]],"40":[[1,"12","13","Port Modernization and Efficiency Improvement Programme","Government will work in partnership with strategic partners to make our ports more efficient and modern.",""],[1,"12","13","Port Infrastructure Modernization and Service Improvement","Port infrastructure will continue to be modernised, and services will be improved further to facilitate trade and commerce.",""],[1,"12","13","Port Technology and Cargo Handling Upgrade","Modern technology, efficient cargo- handling machinery and international best practices will be adopted to enhance Fiji's position as the hub of the Pacific.",""],[1,"12","14","Ports Master Plan Preparation","A Ports Master Plan is being prepared to guide the long- term development of our ports.",""],[1,"12","15","New Port Development and Site Feasibility Studies","Options are being explored for the establishment of a new port in Valaga Bay in Vanua Levu.",""],[1,"12","15","Modern Slipways and Shipbuilding Industry Revival","Investments in modern slipways, the revival of the shipbuilding and maintenance industry will be pursued.",""],[1,"12","16","Suva Wharf Upgrade and Expansion","Government is exploring the possibility of upgrading and expanding the current Suva wharf facility to cater for future cargo and passenger demand.",""],[1,"12","16","Outer Island Port Upgrade Works","Upgrade works at a number of outer island ports will also be undertaken.",""],[1,"12","17","Inter-Island Ferry Service Improvement","Shipping services will be improved to ensure reliability, safety, efficiency and affordability of ferry services.",""],[1,"13","1","Subsidy for Uneconomical Sea Routes","to subsidise uneconomical sea routes to ensure that shipping services are provided on a regular basis to these regions.",""],[1,"80","2","Inter-Island Maritime Transport Infrastructure Investment","Investments will be undertaken for construction and upgrade of jetties, waiting sheds, slipways, navigational aids like lighthouses and beacon piles, and assistance for purchase of smaller boats for inter-island connectivity.",""],[1,"80","2","Small-Boat Landing Development Programme","Funding will also be channelled towards developing small-boat landings in the maritime regions and other coastal areas.",""],[1,"80","4","Subsidies for Uneconomical Maritime Routes","and equipment will continue, together with subsidies for services to uneconomical routes under the franchise scheme.",""],[1,"80","4","Review of Maritime Subsidy and Fare Structure","Government will also continuously review the subsidy rate, passenger fares and freight charges in line with cost structures.",""],[1,"80","4","Acquisition of New Government Shipping Vessels","More investments will be undertaken in the acquisition of new vessels to boost Government Shipping Services' fleet (GSS), to support development projects and for passenger transportation to the maritime islands.",""],[1,"81","4","Fortnightly Shipping Services on Uneconomical Routes","Provision of fortnightly shipping services on all uneconomical routes.",""],[1,"81","4","Shipping Franchise Scheme Subsidy Review","Review the amount of subsidy for each route under the Shipping Franchise Scheme.",""],[1,"81","4","New and Shorter Sea Route Development","Identify and develop new and shorter sea routes.",""],[1,"81","4","Expansion of Government Shipping Capacity","Increase government shipping services' human resources and vessels to enable them to also service the uneconomical routes.",""],[1,"82","1","Safe and Sustainable Inter-Island Transportation Services","Ensure safe, efficient, affordable, environ- mentally sound and sustainable inter-island transportation services.",""]],"41":[[1,"12","9","Airport Modernisation and Upgrade Programme","International and domestic airports will be modernised and upgraded to international standards.",""],[1,"12","10","Nadi International Airport Terminal Development and Upgrade","a second terminal will be developed, and to improve service for passengers flying to other destinations in Fiji, the domestic terminal at the Nadi International Airport will be upgraded",""],[1,"12","10","Vanua Levu New International Airport Development","A new international airport will be developed in Vanua Levu",""],[1,"12","10","Nausori International Airport Revamp and Expansion","the Nausori International Airport will be revamped and expanded",""],[1,"12","11","Airline Fleet Renewal and Route Expansion","Fiji Airways will continue to renew and expand its fleet with leasing of new aircrafts.",""],[1,"12","11","New Air Connections and Route Development","New air connections will be explored and new routes developed.",""],[1,"12","11","Tourist Source Market Expansion Strategy","This will be aligned to our plans for the expansion of new tourist source markets, including attracting visitors from emerging regions such as Southeast Asia and North and South America.",""],[1,"12","12","Domestic Air Services Enhancement and Airport Upgrading Programme","Domestic air services will be enhanced to support the growth in the tourism industry and more-efficient mobility of all passengers within the country.",""]],"42":[[1,"80","6","Maritime Safety Awareness and Regulation Programme","Safety at sea will also be a key priority, with strategies and programmes implemented to raise awareness and regulate and enforce regulations in favour of safety.",""],[1,"82","2","Inter-Island Shipping Safety and Efficiency Improvement","Improve safety and efficiency in the provision of inter-island shipping through: ° The Maritime Safety Authority of Fiji (MSAF) will ensure compliance with International Maritime Organization (IMO) safety conventions to which Fiji is signatory; · MSAF will ensure the formulation of and implementation of the national strategy for implementation of IMO and International Labour Organization (ILO) maritime instruments; MSAF will pursue the inclusion of Fiji as a member of the IMO council Category C to voice concerns of Fiji and other Pacific Islands in the IMO assembly meetings; ° Government will continue to determine future accessions to or withdrawals from international conventions;","Maritime Safety Authority of Fiji (MSAF) | Government"],[1,"82","4","Small Craft and Ship Safety Compliance Enforcement","MSAF will oversee and require registration from unregistered ships.",""],[1,"82","6","Safe Ship Management Compliance Requirement","All Fiji registered ships will be required to comply with Safe Ship Management regulations.",""],[1,"82","6","Port State Control Inspection of Foreign-Flagged Ships","MSAF will inspect international ships visiting ports in Fiji to ensure that these foreign-flagged vessels are in compliance with the requirements of IMO and ILO maritime instruments.",""],[1,"82","6","Small Craft Safety Improvement and Community Education","MSAF will continue to explore and encourage ways of improving small craft safety through compliance with legislation, education programmes and sponsorship.",""],[1,"83","1","Maritime Navaid Restoration and Maintenance Programme","MSAF will oversee the continuing programme of maritime Navaid restoration and maintenance, provide hydrographic and surveillance systems to International Association of Lighthouse Authorities (IALA)17, International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) and IMO standards; and .","MSAF"],[1,"83","1","Regional Aids to Navigation Training Centre Establishment","MSAF will pursue the establishment of Fiji as a regional centre of excellence for training in the Pacific region for Aids to Navigation by accrediting SPC as a regional training institution.","MSAF"],[1,"83","1","National Rescue Coordination Centre 24/7 Maritime Search and Rescue Coordination","The National Rescue Coordination Centre (NRCC)19 will coordinate the land, sea and air RCCs and will be available 24/7 to respond to emergency situations.","National Rescue Coordination Centre (NRCC)19"],[1,"83","1","Search and Rescue Manual Continuous Update","A SAR Manual will be continuously updated as a quality control document.",""],[1,"83","1","Accession to the International SAR Convention and Regional SAR MOA","Fiji will accede to the international SAR Convention 1976 and a MOA will be entered into with other regional SAR organizations.",""],[1,"83","1","Maritime Security Coverage and ISPS Compliance Programme","Continue to improve and extend the systems to provide maximum possible coverage of the marine- land interface and security for shipping and small craft travelling within Fiji waters and across its international maritime boundaries; and · MSAF will ensure continual compliance of ports of entries including Suva, Lautoka, Levuka, Malau, Vuda-Wairiki with the Maritime (ISPS Code)20 Regulations 2014 and Fiji Ships travelling overseas are complaint with the ISPS Regulations to ensure that port of entries are safe and secure.","MSAF"],[1,"83","2","Marine Aids to Navigation Improvement and Harmonisation","The aim of IALA is to foster the safe and efficient movement of vessels through the improvement and harmonisation of marine aids to navigation worldwide, and by other appropriate means.",""]],"43":[[1,"127","17","Urban Public Space and Cultural Amenity Development","Urban centres will be developed with urban gardens, parks, seaside walkways, cultural and heritage sculptures, art installations and museums to entice visitors to explore urban and suburban areas.",""],[1,"127","17","Wharf and Jetty Modernisation and Upgrading","To further support this form of tourism, our wharves and jetties will be modernised and upgraded.",""],[1,"128","2","Tourism Infrastructure and Utilities Upgrade","Raise quality of services by developing modern infrastructure and utilities for tourism while protecting the environment.",""],[1,"128","3","Road Network Upgrade and Feeder Road Expansion","Upgrade and extend road networks with particular focus on upgrading linking and feeder roads.",""],[1,"128","3","Tourism Hotspot Water Supply Dam Development","Revisit plans to build more dams to improve water supply in tourism hotspots.",""],[1,"128","3","Outer Island Electricity Grid Development","Develop electrical grids on outer islands with active tourism facilities.",""],[1,"128","3","Sewerage Treatment System Upgrade in Tourism Hotspots","Upgrade sewerage treatment systems in tourism hotspots.",""],[1,"128","3","Airport and Seaport Modernisation Programme","Modernise and expand points of entry into Fiji - airports and seaports.",""],[1,"128","3","Urban Centre Modernisation and Town Planning Initiative","Modernise urban centres and promote innovative town and country planning.",""],[1,"128","3","Tourism Transport Diversification Initiative","Develop unique methods of land transport for tourism - i.e. existing railway lines, river cruises, caravans, quad biking.",""],[1,"128","7","International Flight Capacity Expansion","Increase international flight capacity to and from all major tourism source and emerging markets.",""],[1,"128","7","Airline Code-Sharing Initiative","Initiate medium-term code sharing with prominent foreign airlines, particularly the northern hemisphere countries.",""],[1,"128","7","Viability Studies for New International Destinations","Initiate viability studies of untapped international destinations.",""],[1,"128","7","Domestic Air and Sea Transport Service Upgrade","Upgrade domestic air and sea travel services to increase intra-country connectivity at affordable prices.",""],[1,"128","7","Outer Islands Port Development","Develop seaports and ports of call in Vanua Levu and outer islands to stimulate nautical tourism.",""],[1,"128","17","Tourism Area Public Transport Improvement","Improve public transportation services in and around tourism hotspots.",""]],"44":[[1,"9","2","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","All households will have access to affordable housing through the construction of new housing units.",""],[1,"9","2","Land Release for Home Construction","Ensuring that more land is made available for home construction will help increase the supply of housing.",""],[1,"9","2","Public and Private Housing Investment Incentives","Government will encourage both public and private investments in the provision of housing units with strata titles.",""],[1,"9","3","Vertical Villages Public Housing Investment","Investment in the establishment of \"vertical villages\" will be supported to accommodate a more diverse group of Fijians, that is, with differing incomes, cultural and occupational backgrounds and family sizes.",""],[1,"9","4","Residential Land Development and Affordable Housing Support","The Housing Authority and Public Rental Board will ensure that more land is developed for residential lots and more affordable and accessible housing is provided.",""],[1,"9","4","Private Sector Incentives for Residential Lot Development","Private sector investments in residential lot developments will be supported and incentivised.",""],[1,"9","5","Support for Residential Lot Development on iTaukei Land","Government will continue to support landowners to develop residential lots on iTaukei land.",""],[1,"9","6","Government Support for New Home Construction and First-Time Home Purchase","Government financial support for new home construction and purchase of first homes will be maintained.",""],[1,"18","10","Affordable Housing Assistance for First-Home Owners","Government assistance is provided for the purchase and construction of new homes for first-home owners.",""],[1,"33","12","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion Strategy","In the next five years, new strategies will be implemented to increase the supply of affordable housing, in particular housing units with strata titles, by both the public and private sector.",""],[1,"33","12","Continuation of Existing Housing Programmes","The existing housing programmes will continue.",""],[1,"33","13","Vertical Villages for Integrated Public Housing","To promote more integration and marketability of public housing and housing units with strata titles, \"vertical villages\" will be established.",""],[1,"33","16","Landowner Land Development Support Scheme","Government will also continue to support landowners to develop their land for subdivisions and residential purposes.",""],[1,"33","17","Homeowner Disaster Recovery Contingency Fund and Insurance Options","government will put in place a contingency fund and explore options for disaster insurance in the coming years.",""],[1,"34","3","Vertical Villages Housing Initiative","Establishment of \"vertical villages\".",""],[1,"34","3","Affordable Housing Finance and Insurance Options","Explore options for housing units under strata titles and increasing access to home insurance for low income",""],[1,"34","3","Housing Authority Residential Lot Development","New development of residential lots by Housing Authority.",""],[1,"34","3","Landowner Support for Subdivision Development","Providing financial support to landowners to households. develop subdivisions and residential lots.",""],[1,"34","3","Housing Disaster Contingency and Insurance Fund","Set up a contingency fund and explore options for disaster insurance to assist families who lose their houses in natural disasters and fire.",""],[1,"34","3","Housing Subsidy Review and Graduation Strategy","Annual review of government subsidies to housing providers and develop and implement strategies to graduate residents of low income HART (Housing Assistance & Relief Trust) and PRB housing towards Housing Authority programmes.",""],[1,"34","3","First Home Owners Grant Continuation","Continue with the grant to first Home Owners.",""],[1,"34","3","Standard Rural Housing Scheme Contribution Options","Consider both in kind and cash contributions for standard rural housing schemes.",""],[1,"34","3","Resilient Housing Building Standards","Develop and enforce building standards for new home construction that require improved resilience to cyclones and flooding.",""],[1,"34","7","Housing and Land Development Co-financing","Co-financing of housing and land development projects.",""],[1,"34","7","iTaukei Land Development for Low-Cost Housing","Develop more iTaukei land for low cost housing.",""],[1,"34","7","Grants for iTaukei Residential Land Development","Provide grants to iTaukei Landowners for residential land development.",""],[1,"34","7","Climate-Resilient Low-Cost Housing Support","Provide support and assistance towards the development of climate and weatherproof low-cost housing in both urban and rural environments.",""]],"45":[[1,"9","7","Informal Settlement Upgrading and Lease Regularization","Informal settlements will continue to be upgraded and leases granted to those on state land.",""],[1,"9","7","Lease Granting for Informal Settlements on iTaukei Land","Leases will also be granted to informal settlements on iTaukei land with the consent of landowners.",""],[1,"9","7","Income-Generating Livelihood Support Projects","Income-generating projects to support the creation of sustainable livelihoods will continue in economically depressed rural areas.",""],[1,"9","8","Inclusive Public Housing Design and Resilient Building Standards","Future public housing will be designed to cater for people with disabilities and special needs.",""],[1,"9","9","Household Disaster Contingency Fund and Insurance Scheme Exploration","government will set up a contingency fund and explore opportunities for disaster insurance schemes with bilateral development partners and multilateral financial institutions",""],[1,"18","10","Squatter Resettlement and State Land Leasing Programme","Major squatter resettlement programmes and provision of leases for those on state land are continuing.",""],[1,"18","10","Informal Settlement Land and Utility Services Expansion","Access to land and provision of utility services have been extended to informal settlements.",""],[1,"33","14","Settlement Lease Issuance on State and iTaukei Land","Leases will continue to be issued to settlements on state land, and those on iTaukei land will be provided leases only after approval from landowners.",""],[1,"34","4","Informal Settlement Upgrading Programme","Upgrade informal settlements.",""],[1,"34","5","Informal Settlement Redevelopment and Basic Services Provision","Redevelop informal areas with provision of basic amenities in current informal settlements.",""],[1,"34","5","Lease Facilitation for Informal Settlement Residents","Facilitate leases to those on informal settlements.",""],[1,"34","5","Housing Programmes for Informal Settlement Reduction","Develop housing programmes to reduce the existence of informal settlements and social housing.",""],[1,"34","5","Sustainable Rural Housing and Income Generation Support","Support sustainable rural housing and income generation projects.",""],[1,"34","6","Government-NGO Housing and Land Partnership","Strengthen Government - NGO partnerships in the provision of housing and land for the poor.",""]],"46":[[1,"40","3","School Facilities Construction and Upgrading Support","Further budgetary support will be provided for construction and upgrading of new and existing school facilities and equipment, including the rehabilitation of schools damaged by Cyclone Winston.",""],[1,"41","4","School Infrastructure and Learning Materials Improvement","Improve infrastructure, facilities and learning materials for all schools.",""],[1,"41","4","Timely School Textbook and Building Grant Provision","Timely provision of textbooks and building grants to schools.",""],[1,"42","22","Construction of New Infant Schools","Construction of new infant schools",""],[1,"43","1","Construction of New Secondary Schools","Construction of new secondary schools",""],[1,"43","2","New Bau Central College Construction","Complete new Bau Central College",""],[1,"43","3","Primary School Boat and Outboard Motor Procurement","Purchase of boat and outboard motor engine (Primary Schools)",""],[1,"43","4","School Water Tank Procurement","Purchase of water tanks for primary and secondary schools",""]],"47":[[1,"9","10","Universal Education Access and Quality Improvement","Universal access to education at all levels will be maintained with a focus on improving the quality of education.",""],[1,"9","11","Education Facilities and Learning Quality Improvement Programme","Investments will be undertaken to improve existing and new education facilities, purchase new equipment and materials, embrace digital learning and improve teacher performance.",""],[1,"9","11","Teacher Recruitment and In-Service Training Initiative","Teacher-to-student ratios will be improved and maintained, with more hiring and in-service teacher training to improve teaching quality.",""],[1,"9","12","Free Education Initiative through Per Capita Grants","Government will continue with the free education initiative through per capita grants to schools.",""],[1,"9","12","Student Transport Subsidy Support","Initiatives such as the bus-fare and boat-fare subsidies, free textbooks and other financial assistance will continue to ensure that no one is deprived of quality education.",""],[1,"9","13","Early Childhood Education Expansion and School Attachment Programme","Early childhood education (ECE) will be improved, and ECE centres will be attached to all primary schools around Fiji.",""],[1,"9","13","Primary and Secondary Curriculum Review Reform","The curriculum for primary and secondary schools will be reviewed to support national integration and prepare Fijians for a transformed Fiji, to accommodate creative and active learning and to develop entrepreneurial skills, learning by doing, and effective peer learning.",""],[1,"9","13","Parental Engagement for Learning Support Initiative","This holistic approach will incorporate enhanced parental engagement to support learning.",""],[1,"9","15","Inclusive Education Facilities for Children with Disabilities and Special Needs","The education system will be made more inclusive by establishing facilities to accommodate children with disabilities and special needs.",""],[1,"18","5","Education Access and Support Package","government has increased investment in education at all levels through the free education initiative, bus fare assistance, free textbooks for primary and secondary education, and tertiary education scholarship and loan schemes",""],[1,"40","2","Teacher Recruitment and Retention Initiative","More teachers have been recruited, and continuous hiring of quality teachers will continue to improve the teacher- to-student ratio for rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"40","3","Free Education and Financial Assistance Continuation","The free-education policy will continue together with other financial assistance.",""],[1,"40","4","Universal Early Childhood Education Access Expansion","To achieve universal access to early childhood education, an ECE centre will be attached to each primary school.",""],[1,"40","4","Early Childhood Education Grants for Facilities and Teacher Quality","Grants will continue to be provided for facility upgrades, development of new centres and improving the quality of ECE teachers.",""],[1,"41","4","Free Education and Student Support Initiative","Continuation of free education initiative, bus fare subsidy, free textbooks, toppers scholarships and tertiary loan scheme.",""],[1,"41","4","Inclusive Access for Physically Challenged Students","Provision of access for the physically challenged students.",""],[1,"42","3","Establishment of ECE Teacher Positions","Establishment of ECE teacher positions",""]],"48":[[1,"9","14","Tertiary Education Improvement and Technical College Expansion","Tertiary education will be further improved to focus on current and future needs, including the future demands of the labour market.",""],[1,"9","14","Technical and Vocational Training Expansion","Technical and vocational training for lifelong learning will continue with the establishment of more technical colleges.",""],[1,"40","6","Technical Colleges Expansion for Trade and Vocational Skills","Government has increased investment in trade and vocational skills with establishment of technical colleges around the country.",""],[1,"41","2","Fiji Qualification Framework Implementation","Implementation of Fiji Qualification Framework.",""],[1,"41","6","Technical Colleges Establishment","Establish Technical Colleges.",""],[1,"41","6","TVET Teacher Recruitment Initiative","Recruit qualified and experienced TVET teachers.",""],[1,"41","6","TVET Database Development","Establish TVET database.",""],[1,"41","6","Apprenticeship Scheme Revival","Revive apprenticeship scheme through the Training and Productivity Authority of Fiji (TPAF).",""],[1,"41","6","National Qualification Framework Development","Accelerate the development of National Qualification Framework in different trade areas.",""],[1,"41","6","Lifelong Skills Training for Students","Enhance students' understanding through lifelong skills training such as scouts and girl guides.",""]],"49":[[1,"7","12","Education and Skills Development for Workforce Entry","All Fijians will be empowered with education and skill sets so that they may be easily absorbed into the workforce.",""],[1,"13","8","Workforce Skills Development for Future Industry Demand","Government will work closely with industry, tertiary education institutions and development partners to prepare a workforce of highly skilled Fijians in line with future industry demand, in particular for the new growth sectors.",""],[1,"13","8","Sectoral Skills Development in Priority Occupations","Skills development in areas such as trades and craftsmanship, engineering and IT-related professions, health care services, hospitality and aged care, foreign languages, resource-based sector expertise, and education",""],[1,"19","11","Human Resource Development Capacity Building","Under this Plan, the strategic focus for human resource development will be on building individual and institutional capacity in all sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"57","1","Youth Education, Employment and Leadership Opportunities","Government will ensure that educational, employment and leadership opportunities are provided to young Fijians.",""],[1,"57","2","Youth Training, Empowerment and Awareness Programmes","In the next 5 years, initiatives will be strengthened for training, empowerment and awareness programmes for youth in areas such as entrepreneurship, leadership, climate change and sexual health awareness.",""],[1,"57","3","MSME Establishment Support for Rural and Urban Youth","Support will be provided for the establishment of MSMEs for rural and urban youth.",""],[1,"57","3","National Employment Centre One-Stop Job Assistance Service","The National Employment Centre will continue to provide the \"one-stop shop\" service to assist employment seekers to find jobs.",""],[1,"58","3","Youth Community-Based Entrepreneurship and Skills Training Programme","Support youth community-based capacity building programmes on entrepreneurship development and skills-based training under Ministry of Youth and Sports (MYS) and other relevant agencies.","Ministry of Youth and Sports (MYS)"],[1,"58","3","Rural Youth Leadership Training under iTaukei Affairs Board","Support the provision of leadership training under the iTaukei Affairs Board for rural youth and promote youths.",""],[1,"58","3","Small Business Entrepreneurial Training under Financial Inclusion Programme","Support business leadership through systematic training on Small Business Entrepreneurial training in partnership with RBF under the Financial Inclusion and Literacy Programme.",""],[1,"58","4","Youth Education and Training for Decent Employment","Promote the education and training of young people to secure decent employment.",""],[1,"58","5","Youth Education and Training Support Programme","Support the development and empowerment of youth through education and training in schools and tertiary institutions.",""],[1,"58","5","Youth Small and Micro-Enterprise Support","Support the establishment of small and micro-enterprise projects for youth in rural and urban centres.",""],[1,"58","5","National Employment Centre Skills Enhancement","Enhance job-skills through better education and strengthening of the National Employment Centre.",""],[1,"58","5","Technical, Vocational and Lifelong Skills Training for Youth","Promote technical and vocational and lifelong skills training for youth, as in Chapter 3.1.5 (Education).",""],[1,"58","5","Youth Training Centre Expansion for Non-Formal Education","Expand training programmes at Youth Training Centres (YTC) to accommodate non-formal education programmes as in the National Non-Formal Education Policy.",""],[1,"58","5","Youth Training Quality Improvement Programme","Improve the training programmes to meet labour market needs and increase the returns on investments in training.",""],[1,"58","5","International Partnership for Youth Training Modernisation","Explore partnerships with foreign partners to modernise youth training programmes and training centres through MOUs.",""],[1,"58","5","Youth Development and Training Plan of Action Implementation","Strengthen the promotion of youth development and training through the implementation of the Plan of Action as agreed and endorsed by either local or international parties in MOUs.",""]],"50":[[1,"40","5","University Grant Funding for Tertiary Education Infrastructure","The provision of grant funding to three major universities has improved tertiary education infrastructure and facilities as well as the quality of teaching and learning.",""],[1,"40","5","Tertiary Education Scholarship and Loan Scheme","Tertiary education scholarships and the loan scheme have also increased access and affordability for all tertiary students.",""],[1,"40","5","Toppers Scholarship Alignment to Priority Development Areas","The Toppers scholarship initiative will continue to be aligned to medium-term priority areas for socio- economic development.",""],[1,"41","7","Higher Education Institutions Support Strengthening","Enhance and strengthen the support for Higher Education Institutions",""],[1,"41","8","Recognition of Registered Institutions under FHEC","Expedite the number of registered institutions to be recognized under the Fiji Higher Education Commission (FHEC).",""],[1,"41","8","Public-Private Partnership Expansion for Higher Education","Increase private and public partnerships.",""],[1,"41","8","ICT Integration in Tertiary Institutions","Enhance the use of ICT for tertiary institutions.",""],[1,"41","8","Higher Education Incentive Strengthening","Strengthen incentives for higher education institutions.",""],[1,"41","8","National Accreditation Framework Implementation","Implement the National Accreditation Framework.",""],[1,"43","14","FNU Labasa Campus Construction","Construction of FNU Labasa Campus",""],[1,"43","15","Civil Works for Building A","Civil works, construct building A",""]],"51":[[1,"40","7","Curriculum Review and Strengthening","The curriculum will continually be reviewed and strengthened to achieve national objectives.",""],[1,"40","7","Integration of Contemporary Thematic Areas into the Curriculum","Incorporating contemporary thematic areas in educational curriculum such as cultural diversity, gender, nutrition, respectful relationships, drugs and alcohol, climate change and the environment will enrich students' understanding of wider social issues.",""],[1,"40","10","Inclusive Learning Environment Promotion","A safe and inclusive learning environment will be promoted.",""],[1,"40","10","Special Needs Education Grants","Education for persons with special needs will continue to be promoted through grants to specials schools.",""],[1,"40","10","Health and Wellness Programmes","Health and wellness programmes will continue.",""],[1,"41","2","Education Legislation and Policy Review","Review and amend legislation and policies pertaining to quality education including the Education Act.",""],[1,"41","2","Teacher Workforce Ratio Improvement","Improve student to teacher ratio.",""],[1,"41","2","Teacher In-Service Training Programme","Increase in-service training for teachers.",""],[1,"41","2","Public-Private Education Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen private and public partnerships.",""],[1,"41","2","School Library Expansion","Expand school libraries with relevant resources.",""],[1,"41","2","School Social Issues Education Expansion","Increase awareness of, and capacity for education on social issues such as Drug Education, HIV/AIDS, Gender Based Violence, Respectful Relationships, Sex Education, NCD, Cyber Safety, and Mental Health",""],[1,"41","2","Teacher Gender Sensitisation and Child Protection Training","Increase number of teachers undergoing training on gender sensitisation, equality and child protection, at school.",""],[1,"41","2","School Counselling Services Expansion","Increase counselling services for primary and secondary schools.",""],[1,"41","2","Teacher Basic Counselling Skills Training","Increase basic counselling skills training for teachers in schools.",""],[1,"41","2","National and Cultural Education Enhancement","Enhance national and cultural education in schools.",""],[1,"41","2","Literacy and Numeracy Assessment Strengthening","Strengthen assessment and learning through implementing critical skills such as literacy and numeracy assessment.",""],[1,"42","15","National Curriculum Rollout","Rollout of new National Curriculum at all levels",""],[1,"58","14","Early Childhood Physical Education Teaching","Ensure that young children receive proper teaching in physical education.",""],[1,"58","15","Physical Education Curriculum Review","Review physical education curriculum in primary and secondary schools.",""],[1,"58","15","Equal Access to School Sports Facilities","Ensure girls and boys participate equally in sporting activities and have access to facilities.",""]],"52":[[1,"72","19","Urban Development and New Growth Centres Programme","Urban development with better services and development of new cities, towns and growth centres will be pursued.",""]],"53":[[1,"14","5","Urban Scheme Review and Growth Centre Development","existing city and town schemes will be reviewed, and new growth centres will be identified and developed.",""],[1,"14","5","Urban Facilities and Services Modernisation","Urban areas will be further modernised with improved facilities and services.",""],[1,"14","5","Urban Infrastructure and Market Redevelopment","Transport infrastructure, housing development, law-and- order facilities, bus stands and fresh-food markets will be restructured and redeveloped where needed for improved convenience and better urban management.",""],[1,"14","6","New Town and City Development and Urban Boundary Expansion","New towns and cities will be established, and town boundaries will be extended where necessary.",""],[1,"14","6","Urban Spatial Planning and Long-Term Model Development","Spatial plans and long-term miniature models will be developed to guide the future development of all urban centres.",""],[1,"14","8","Decentralisation of Government Offices to Regional Divisions","Government is exploring options to decentralise some of its offices currently based in Suva to the Western and Northern divisions.",""]],"54":[[1,"8","8","Rural and Maritime Electrification Acceleration","Electrification projects in the rural and maritime areas will be expedited to ensure that the entire population has access to electricity by 2021.",""],[1,"8","9","Grid Extension Programme","Further grid extensions will be undertaken in Viti Levu, Vanua Levu, Ovalau and Taveuni.",""],[1,"8","9","Rural Electrification Funding Programme","Government will continue to fully fund rural electrification projects, including connections for households near the grid lines.",""],[1,"30","2","Rural and Maritime Electrification Expansion","Lack of access in the unserviced rural and maritime areas will be addressed over the next 5 years.",""],[1,"30","3","Grid Extension Acceleration Programme","grid extension programmes will be accelerated in Viti Levu, Vanua Levu, Ovalau and Taveuni.",""],[1,"30","3","Rural Electrification Full Funding Policy","Government will continue with the policy to fully fund rural electrification projects.",""],[1,"30","6","Decentralized Rural and Maritime Electrification Initiative","Decentralised renewable energy sources such as solar, mini-hydro, and wind systems will be used to electrify rural areas and maritime zones where feasible.",""]],"55":[[1,"19","11","Modern Employment Relations Regulatory Framework","Reforms have been implemented to put in place a modern employment-relations regulatory framework that can protect the fundamental rights of all employees and also support inclusive private sector-led growth.",""],[1,"19","11","Labour Market Standards Improvement Initiative","Continuous efforts will be focused on improving Fiji's labour-market standards to meet accredited international best practices, including the fostering of a modern workforce encouraging increased participation from women and recognising the abilities of those from diverse groups.",""]],"56":[[1,"10","14","Local Culture and Heritage Promotion for Tourism","Local culture and heritage will be promoted as part of our vibrant tourism industry.",""],[1,"10","14","Traditional Knowledge Intellectual Property Protection Framework","Intellectual property rights for protection of traditional knowledge will be developed and strengthened.",""]],"57":[[1,"63","1","Cultural Heritage Safeguarding and Promotion","This heritage will be safeguarded and promoted.",""],[1,"63","3","Fijian Crafted Cultural Promotion Campaign","This includes cultural performances and traditional arts and craft made by local artisans that will be promoted through the \"Fijian Crafted\" campaign.",""],[1,"63","5","Fiji Museum and National Library Upgrade","The upgrade of Fiji Museum and the National Library housed within the National Archives will greatly contribute to the preservation of Fiji's heritage.",""],[1,"63","5","Authentic Heritage Merchandise Scale-Up","The positive steps already undertaken to produce authentic heritage merchandise will be scaled up to provide genuine, culturally appropriate and iconic goods to tourists in an effort to boost the economic spin-off from Fiji's cultural and documentary heritage.",""],[1,"63","6","Cultural Heritage Site Protection and Sustainable Use Initiative","Cultural heritage sites and places will also be protected as part of our unique biodiversity and used sustainably for national development.",""],[1,"64","2","Cultural Heritage Protection and Digital Archiving Programme","Review, develop and implement new legislation.",""],[1,"64","4","Institutional Capacity Development for Cultural Heritage","Develop and upgrade capacities of institutions, programmes, and infrastructure that promote cultural heritage for sustainable development.",""],[1,"64","4","Community Participation in Heritage Site Development","Strengthen participation of resource owners through the development of heritage places and monuments for tourism purposes.",""],[1,"64","4","Cultural Heritage Promotion Materials Development","Develop promotional materials and tools (film, literature, theatre) to enhance understanding and appreciation of the diversity of cultures in Fiji.",""],[1,"64","4","Cultural Heritage Recognition and World Listing Nominations","Enhance recognition of the unique values of Fijian cultural heritage, natural heritage, intangible heritage and documentary heritage at international level through nominations for world listings.",""],[1,"64","4","Cultural Sites and Heritage Infrastructure Development","Develop and maintain cultural sites, heritage spaces and associated infrastructure.",""],[1,"65","4","Cultural Heritage Sub-Centres Establishment","Establishment of cultural heritage sub- centres",""],[1,"65","13","Cultural Impact Assessment Requirement","Conduct cultural impact assessments (Archaeological Impact Assessment, Built Heritage Assessment) (sites)",""]],"58":[[1,"14","5","Urban Disaster Response Strengthening","Disaster response within cities will be improved through better early warning systems, inter-agency coordination and enhanced disaster response capacities.",""]],"59":[[1,"103","4","Waste Management Authority Establishment","Consideration will be given to the establishment of a Waste Management Authority to provide more efficient,",""],[1,"103","5","Waste Recycling and Transfer Station Development","Waste recycling and transfer stations will also be developed in strategic areas around the country.",""],[1,"103","7","Smart City Programme","A special Smart City Programme shall be developed for the Towns and Cities to ensure that the towns are cities adapt to global modern urban management practices.",""],[1,"104","6","Waste Management Incentives and Packaging Controls","Incentivise waste management processes, including controlling the type of packaging material entering the country and recycling.",""],[1,"104","6","Waste Management Institutional Review and Authority Feasibility Study","Review institutional arrangements for waste management with a view to identifying the best model that can deliver an efficient, effective and financially viable waste management operation.",""]],"60":[[1,"107","4","Climate-Related Relocation Support for Vulnerable Communities","For disaster-risk management in rural and maritime areas, government has identified 830 vulnerable communities at risk from climate-related events to be relocated.",""],[1,"107","5","Disaster-Resilient Evacuation Centre Construction","the government is identifying and constructing evacuation centres that are compliant with the building code",""],[1,"107","5","Community-Based Adaptation Measures in Rural and Maritime Regions","Community-based adaptation measures in rural and maritime regions will also be prioritised",""],[1,"107","5","Coastal and Watershed Protection Works","These include the construction of sea walls, watershed management, river dredging and drainage, and riverbank protection",""],[1,"108","10","Integrated Climate Change and Disaster Management Plan","Develop an integrated policy, approach and operational plan to effectively address climate change and disaster management.",""],[1,"108","11","National Strategic Plan for Climate Change and Disaster Resilience","Develop a National Strategic Plan for Climate Change and Disaster Resilience.",""],[1,"108","11","Fiji National Disaster Management Arrangements Review","Review the Fiji National Disaster Management Arrangements to include Climate Change.",""],[1,"108","11","Climate Change Policy Review","Review the Climate Change Policy.",""],[1,"108","12","Rural Community Building Resilience Upgrade","Ensure rural community buildings are cyclone and flood resistant.",""],[1,"108","13","National Building Code Review and Resilient Construction Standards","Review the National Building Code and incorporate cyclone and flood resilient design and construction",""],[1,"108","13","Rural Building Code Compliance Incentive Scheme","Provide incentives for rural communities to support compliance with new building code standards.",""],[1,"108","15","Comprehensive Disaster Risk Assessment Framework","Develop comprehensive assessment framework, including adoption of the damage and loss assessment methodology.",""],[1,"108","15","Hazard, Vulnerability, and Exposure Data System","Institutionalise a mechanism to collect and analyse hazard, vulnerability and exposure data.",""],[1,"108","15","Cost-Benefit Analysis Mainstreaming in Mitigation and Preparedness","Mainstream cost-benefit analysis into decision-making processes in mitigation and preparedness measures.",""],[1,"108","15","Hazard Mapping and Modelling Programme","Develop hazard maps and models for all potential hazards (including sea level rise, storm surge, flood and tsunami).",""],[1,"108","15","Research Collaboration on Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction","Encourage collaboration with development partners and tertiary institutions in researching priority areas of climate change and disaster risk reduction.",""],[1,"109","1","Mainstreaming of Resourcing, Adaptation, and Disaster Risk Management into Development Planning and Budgeting","Resourcing and adaptation, and disaster risk management become part of the national and sub national development planning and budgetary process.",""],[1,"109","2","Post-Disaster Financing Modalities Exploration","Explore post disaster financing modalities.",""],[1,"109","2","Access to Global Climate Financing Facilities","Improve access to global financing facilities such as the Green Climate Fund.",""],[1,"109","3","Climate Change and Disaster Resilience Partnerships","Strengthen partnerships at all levels for building resilience to climate change and disaster.",""],[1,"109","4","Civil Society Partnership for Community Resilience Capacity Building","Partner with civil society to build capacity at divisional and community level on resilience to climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"109","4","Community Vulnerability Assessment Programme","Undertake vulnerability assessments for all communities.",""],[1,"109","4","Rural Climate and Disaster Resilience Planning","Develop climate and disaster resilience plans for rural communities.",""],[1,"109","4","Resilient Building Provision for Rural Communities and Schools","Ensure that every rural community and every rural school has at least one building resilient to a category 4",""],[1,"109","4","Relocation Support and Capacity Building for Climate-Vulnerable Communities","Provide capacity building to communities that have been identified as vulnerable to rising sea levels and in cyclone. need of relocation.",""],[1,"110","3","Integrated National Strategic Plan for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction","Develop an integrated national strategic plan for climate change and disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"110","7","Integrated Community Vulnerability Assessment","Undertake integrated vulnerability assessment for all communities",""],[1,"110","9","Disaster and Climate Change Financing Modalities Exploration","Explore disaster and climate change financing modalities",""],[1,"110","12","Hazard Mapping and Modeling Initiative","Develop hazard maps and models for all potential hazards (sea level rise, storm surge, flood and tsunami)",""],[1,"116","14","River Dredging Programme","Continue dredging of Ba, Labasa, Rewa and Sigatoka River",""]],"61":[[1,"15","50","Green Growth Framework Implementation","a 10% reduction will be achieved through implementation of the GGF for Fiji using available domestic resources with a further 20% reduction conditional on external funding.",""],[1,"21","5","National Low-Greenhouse-Gas Emission Development Strategy","Fiji will develop by 2020, mid-century long- term low greenhouse gas emission development strategies, laying out a plan to deeply decarbonize the Fijian economy by 2050.",""]],"62":[[1,"10","14","Forest, Mangrove, and Coral Reef Management","There will be an increased focus on proper management of our forests, mangroves and coral reefs because of the complex natural biodiversity that these systems support.",""],[1,"15","42","Marine Protected Areas Expansion","Establish MPAs targeting 30% of Fiji's marine areas (%)",""]],"63":[[1,"122","1","Sustainable Forest Management Support","Sustainable forest-management practices will continue for the wood growing and processing industry to flourish.",""],[1,"122","2","Private Sector Forest Plantation Development and Management Support","Moving forward, private sector involvement in forest-plantation development and management will be increased through long-term leasing arrangements and appropriate technical support.",""],[1,"122","2","National Plantation Policy","A National Plantation Policy will be introduced to provide guidelines for setting up private- sector plantations and their operations",""],[1,"122","2","Fire Management Strategic Plan","A National Plantation Policy will be introduced to provide guidelines for setting up private- sector plantations and their operations as well as a Fire Management Strategic Plan to address the threat of forest fires to standing stock.",""],[1,"122","3","Forest Reforestation and Conservation Expansion","The Government will support reforestation of native and exotic forests, and Fiji's forest area, which is protected under long-term conservation initiatives, will be increased further.",""],[1,"122","3","Fiji REDD+ Programme Expansion","More areas will be identified under the Fiji REDD+35 programme to protect our forests and at the same time generate financial benefits under carbon-trading mechanisms.",""],[1,"122","3","Native Forest Harvesting Regulatory Framework","A new framework has been adopted for the harvesting of native forests.",""],[1,"122","8","Sustainable Forest Management Strengthening","Strengthen sustainable forest management.",""],[1,"122","9","Forest Conservation and Sustainable Harvesting Measures","Strengthen efforts on forest conservation, sustainable forest harvesting practices and climate change mitigation",""],[1,"122","9","Long-Term Forest Leasing Mechanism","Long-term leasing mechanism(s) to support forest conservation, forest concessions and plantation leases.",""],[1,"122","11","Plantation Policy Development","Develop a Plantation Policy that will ensure better management, development and production from plantations.",""],[1,"122","11","National Land Use Plan Formulation","Formulation of a National Land Use Plan.",""],[1,"122","11","FHCL Re-planting Programme","Continue Fiji Hardwood Corporation Limited's (FHCL) re-planting programme.",""],[1,"123","2","New Regulatory Framework for Native and Pine Forests","New regulatory framework for native and pine forests",""],[1,"123","8","Emissions Reduction Programme Document Drafting","Drafting of Emissions Reduction Programme Document (ERPD)",""],[1,"123","9","Plantation Policy Preparation","Preparation of plantation policy",""]],"64":[[1,"13","11","Youth Sports Talent and Professionalism Development","Government will continue to invest in the potential of our youth to develop into world-class athletes and sports administrators.",""],[1,"13","11","Sports Facilities Upgrade and Construction Programme","Sports complexes, rural sporting grounds and school sporting facilities will be improved and new ones constructed to international standards.",""],[1,"13","12","National Academy of Sports Talent Development Programme","Talent will be identified and developed from an early age with world-class training and coaching through the National Academy of Sports.",""],[1,"13","12","International Sports Coach Recruitment Support","Assistance will continue to be provided to enable international coaches to be hired and thereby improve our competitiveness.",""],[1,"13","12","Sports Corporate Sponsorship Incentive Scheme","Corporate sponsorship in sports will also be incentivised to encourage better partnerships in sports development.",""],[1,"57","8","International Sporting Events Hosting Bid","Fiji will bid to host major regional and international sporting events, including the 2023 Pacific Games and 2026 Commonwealth Games.",""],[1,"57","8","Sporting Infrastructure Upgrading and Maintenance Programme","Government will continue to invest in the upgrading and maintenance of sporting infrastructure and facilities to raise them to international standards.",""],[1,"58","9","Sports Tourism Promotion Initiative","Promote sports tourism in partnership with the Ministry of Tourism and other national sporting Education. organizations.","Ministry of Tourism"],[1,"58","12","Universal Access to Sporting Facilities","Provide every citizen with access to proper sporting facilities.",""],[1,"58","13","Review of Tax Incentives for Sports Sponsorship","Review government tax incentives on sports sponsorship for national sporting federations.",""],[1,"58","13","Rural Sports Complex Construction","Continue with construction of rural sports complex projects.",""],[1,"58","13","Rural Sports Ground Development","Continue with rural sports ground field projects.",""],[1,"58","13","Fiji Sports Council Facilities Upgrade","Continue with upgrade of Fiji Sports Council's facilities.",""],[1,"59","12","Rural Sports Complex Construction","Construction of rural sports complex",""],[1,"59","20","Games Athletes Village Development","Preliminary works to establish a Games Athletes Village inclusive of proper facilities and amenities to support our bid to host the 2023 Pacific Games and 2026 Commonwealth Games.",""],[1,"59","22","Athletes Village Project Phase 3","Phase 3 of athletes village project implementation.",""]],"65":[[1,"57","7","Elite Sports Development and Facilities Modernisation Programme","Over the next 5 years, emphasis will be placed on developing elite sportspersons and modernising and building new state-of-the-art facilities.",""],[1,"57","7","Sports Professional Development Support Services","Support services associated with the professional development of sports will be strengthened.",""],[1,"57","7","Sports Science and Medicine Curriculum Integration","Sports psychology, sports science and sports medicine will also be part of the tertiary curriculum.",""],[1,"57","9","National Sports Academy","A National Sports Academy will be established to support the development of future sportspersons.",""],[1,"58","8","Systematic and Coordinated Sports Development Programme","Develop a productive and healthy nation through a systematic and coordinated sports development programme.",""],[1,"58","9","School and Tertiary Physical Education and Sports Programme Enhancement","Coordinate with Ministry of Education on the enhancement of the physical education and sports programmes in schools and tertiary institutions.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"58","9","Mental and Physical Literacy and Well-Being Promotion","Promote mental and physical literacy and well-being in partnership with the Ministry of Health and","Ministry of Health"],[1,"58","10","Elite Athlete Development Enabling Environment","Promote the enabling environment that develops local athletes into elite athletes.",""],[1,"58","11","National Sports Talent Identification and Development Programme","develop an overarching National Sports Talent Identification and Development Programme to strengthen it.",""],[1,"58","11","International Coach Hiring Budget Provision","Funding provision for the hire of international coaches in annual budgetary allocation.",""],[1,"58","11","Sports Grants to National Sporting Organisations","Provision of sports grants to NSOs.",""],[1,"58","11","National Academy of Sports","Establishment of the National Academy of Sports.",""],[1,"58","15","Fiji National Sports Commission Sports Outreach Program","Implementation of the Fiji National Sports Commission sports outreach program.",""],[1,"58","15","Sports-Specific Subjects in Tertiary Education","Encourage tertiary institutions to incorporate sports specific subjects into courses and programmes.",""],[1,"60","1","National Sports Talent Identification and Development Programme","Establishment of National sports talent identification and development programme",""],[1,"60","3","National Sports Academy Establishment","Establishment of National sports academy",""]],"66":[[1,"14","9","Rural Infrastructure and Public Utilities Improvement","Rural development will be prioritised with improvements in infrastructure and provision of adequate public utilities.",""],[1,"14","9","Rural and Maritime Income Generation Support","Agriculture and other sectors will be supported to generate income opportunities for people in rural and maritime areas.",""],[1,"14","9","Agricultural Marketing and Value Chain Linkages","The Ministry of Agriculture will create better linkages to enhance the marketing, promotion and value-","Ministry of Agriculture"]],"67":[[1,"60","9","Women’s Equal Opportunity and Participation Initiative","Government will provide equal opportunities for all, including the participation of women in education, leadership, and overall economic development, and will continue its strong efforts to eliminate violence against women.",""],[1,"60","10","Women's Workforce Participation through Equal Access to Social Services","Equal opportunities in education, health and other social services will raise women's participation in the workforce.",""],[1,"60","13","Women's Leadership and Decision-Making Participation Strategy","women's participation in leadership and decision-making at all levels will be increased through strategies that generate greater economic participation, recognition of domestic workers, and elimination of discrimination due the importance of the biological reproductive role of women.",""],[1,"60","13","Women's Occupational Freedom Support Policy","Government will support the freedom of all women to participate in any profession they choose.",""],[1,"60","13","Shared Decision-Making and Family Planning Policy","policies will focus on encouraging shared decision-making in relationships, especially as they relate to family planning, child care, economic independence and choices of paid work.",""],[1,"61","2","Women's Empowerment and Development Support","Government will continue to work with regional partners and civil society (including faith-based organisations) in the empowerment and development of women.",""],[1,"61","2","Support for Women's Income-Generating Projects","Resources will be provided to women's groups to support income-generating projects.",""],[1,"61","2","National Women's Expo","The National Women's Expo, sponsored by government, will continue to focus on marketing products produced by women for the local and international market.",""],[1,"61","3","Implementation of the Women's Plan of Action","This will be realised through the implementation of the Women's Plan of Action and the National Gender Policy over the next five years.",""],[1,"61","3","Implementation of the National Gender Policy","This will be realised through the implementation of the Women's Plan of Action and the National Gender Policy over the next five years.",""],[1,"61","5","Women's Formal Sector Employment Participation Initiative","Increase women's participation in formal sector employment.",""],[1,"61","6","Expand Women's Access to Income-Generating Activities","Review women's access to income-generating activities including programmes under the Women's all government assistance.",""],[1,"61","6","Promote Women's Equal Access to Public Services","Promote women's equal access to public services and programmes.",""],[1,"61","8","Sex-Disaggregated Data Collection for Gender Strategy Monitoring","Collect sex disaggregated data to inform women's participation in leadership and decision-making and to assist in monitoring and evaluation of gender strategies.",""],[1,"61","8","Rural Women's Empowerment Programme","Introduce or strengthen women's empowerment programmes in rural areas through leadership and to assist in monitoring and evaluation of gender strategies.",""],[1,"61","8","Girls' Training for Non-Traditional Occupations","Promote girls' training and participation in \"traditional male's occupations\" such as engineering and decision-making training, awareness of human and indigenous rights issues, and health needs.",""],[1,"61","8","Women's Leadership Training and Mentorship Support","Place more focus on women's leadership training, sponsorship, special assignments, mentoring and technical trade. coaching.",""],[1,"61","11","Women's Access to Social Services Improvement","Improve women's access to all social services.",""],[1,"61","12","Support for Non-Government Organisations under Women's Plan and Gender Policy","Help strengthen the work of Non-Government Organisations in complementing government programmes under the Women's Plan of Action (WPA) and National Gender Policy.",""],[1,"62","1","National Gender Policy and Women's Plan of Action Implementation","Implementation of the National Gender Policy and Women's Plan of Action",""],[1,"62","2","National Gender Policy Implementation","Legislation, policies and Plan as per the National Gender Policy revised to ensure gender equity is promoted.",""],[1,"62","5","Women's Plan of Action for Women's Economic Empowerment","Increase ability of women and their access to income- generating activities through the Women's Plan of Action.",""]],"68":[[1,"60","11","Domestic Violence and EVAW Institutional Reform","With legislative changes such as the introduction of the Domestic Violence Act, provisions in the Constitution and the reestablishment of the Elimination of Violence Against Women (EVAW) Task Force, government is working towards providing positive and innovative approaches to achieving gender equality and to eliminating discrimination and violence against women.",""],[1,"60","12","Support Services for Women Experiencing Gender-Based Violence","This Plan will provide women experiencing gender-based violence with access to greater help.",""],[1,"60","12","Strengthening Access to GBV Health, Advocacy, Police, and Justice Services","Effective access to health services, specialist advocacy and counselling, police protection and the justice system will be strengthened.",""],[1,"60","12","Gender-Based Violence Prevention Priority","Prevention of gender-based violence will be a priority for government, and police, the NGO partners and donor agencies will continue to work in close partnership.",""],[1,"61","9","Violence Prevention and Referral Network Strengthening","Eliminate violence against women and children through responsive policing and coordinated referral networks.",""],[1,"61","10","Improved Policing Strategy on Violence Against Women and Girls","Devise an effective strategy for improved policing in response to violence against women and girls.",""],[1,"61","10","Best Practice Response Protocols for Victims of Intimate Partner and Sexual Violence","Ensure best practice responses are adhered to when responding to victims of intimate partners and to sexual violence against women.",""],[1,"61","10","Inter-Agency Service Delivery Protocols for Violence Response","Develop service delivery protocols by the Ministry of Women & Children and Poverty Alleviation (MWCPA) in conjunction with the Fiji Police Force and Ministry of Health and Medical Services to clarify roles and referral pathways for all service providers and NGOs.","Ministry of Women & Children and Poverty Alleviation | Fiji Police Force | Ministry of Health and Medical Services"],[1,"62","12","Legal Review on Violence Against Women and Children","Review laws relating to eliminating violence against women and children as per the National Gender Policy.",""],[1,"67","4","Gender-Based Crime Response Improvement","Improve police responses to gender based crimes (Domestic Violence, Rape, Sexual Assault, child sex abuse) to attract more reporting, detection of perpetrators and justice administration.",""],[1,"67","5","Mainstreaming National Gender Policy for Violence Prevention","Mainstreaming Na- tional Gender policy to educate law enforce- ment agencies and the community to thereby prevent and eliminate violence against women.",""],[1,"67","6","Police Gender-Based Violence Service Delivery Protocol","Develop a service delivery protocol for Fiji police and improve the delivery of services in response to Gender Based Violence.",""],[1,"67","6","Police Awareness Raising on Women's Legal Protections","Raise police awareness of the existing legislation and policies that compel police responses and representations for women to attain fair outcomes.","Ministry"],[1,"67","6","Domestic Violence Decree Compliance Review","Review compliance of the police in enforcing the Domestic Violence decree.",""],[1,"67","6","Police and EVAW Legal Review of Family and Criminal Justice Laws","Work with Ending Violence Against Women (EVAW) task force to review Family Law Act and Regulations, the Domestic Violence Decree, the Crimes Decree, the Criminal Procedure Decree, the Sentencing and Penalties Decree, the Child Welfare Decree and the No Drop Policy.",""],[1,"68","13","Gender-Based Crime Response Improvement","Improve police responses to gender based crimes (Domestic Violence, Rape, Sexual Assault, child sex abuse) to attract more reporting, detection of perpetrators and justice administration.",""],[1,"68","14","National Gender Policy Mainstreaming for Violence Prevention","Mainstreaming National Gender policy to educate law enforcement agencies and the community to thereby prevent and eliminate violence against women.",""],[1,"68","15","Police Domestic Violence and Gender-Based Violence Response Strengthening","Work with Fiji police in relation to the conduct of the MOU between the Ministry and Fiji police.","Ministry | Fiji police"],[1,"68","15","Police Awareness and Compliance Review on Domestic Violence Legislation","Raise police awareness of the existing legislation and policies that compel police responses and Review compliance of the police in enforcing the Domestic Violence decree.",""],[1,"68","15","Police Service Delivery Protocol for Gender-Based Violence","Develop a service delivery protocol for Fiji police and improve the delivery of services in response to Gender Based Violence.","Fiji police"],[1,"68","15","Review of Family Law and Violence-Related Legal Frameworks","Work with Ending Violence Against Women (EVAW) task force to review Family Law Act and Regulations, the Domestic Violence Decree, the Crimes Decree, the Criminal Procedure Decree, the Sentencing and Penalties Decree, the Child Welfare Decree and the No Drop Policy.",""]],"69":[[1,"124","1","Sustainable Mining Sector Support","A sustainable mining sector will continue to provide employment, income, foreign exchange earnings and revenue for government.",""],[1,"124","3","Sustainable Mining Practices and Revenue-Sharing Framework","Government will ensure sustainable mining practices and ecological balance together with equitable sharing of revenue amongst investors, landowners and the State.",""],[1,"124","6","Strengthened Environmental Monitoring of Mining and Quarrying","Monitoring the environmental impact of mining and quarrying activities will be strengthened.","Ministry of Land and Mineral Resources"],[1,"125","3","Mining Safety and Environmental Compliance Enforcement","Protection of the environment and human life through the application of vigorous mining safety standards.",""],[1,"125","3","Exploration License and Safety Regulation Monitoring","Monitoring of exploratory licenses and safety regulations.",""],[1,"125","3","Environmental Impact Assessment and Enforcement of Environmental Management Provisions","Evaluation of environmental impact.",""],[1,"125","3","Environment Division Enforcement Arrangement with Ministry of Environment","Organize Memorandum of Agreement with the Ministry of Environment (MoEn) on the roles and responsibilities of the Environment Division in the enforcement of the Environment Management Act (EMA).","Ministry of Environment (MoEn)"],[1,"125","3","Environmental Best Practices in Mining SOPs","Embed environment best practices in the Ministry's standard operating procedures (SOPs) for mining and groundwater development.",""],[1,"125","3","Mineral Resources Legislation Reform","Enact and enforce appropriate legislation for all categories of minerals resources.",""],[1,"125","3","Geoscience Information Upgrade","Upgrade the quantity and quality of geoscience information and its availability.",""],[1,"125","3","Exploration Data Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity to receive, store, catalogue, process, collate and efficiently retrieve any information from stakeholders, entrepreneurs and companies provided with licenses for exploration.",""],[1,"125","3","Mineral Data Bank Upgrade","Upgrade data bank.",""],[1,"125","3","Mineral Data Reporting and Sample Submission Enforcement","Enforce legislation for the collection and supply of data such as reports, surveys, drilling logs, seismic profiles, photographs, charts, punch cards and computer printouts, core samples and geochemical samples.",""],[1,"125","3","Geochemical Laboratory Service Strengthening","Strengthen and improve services rendered by the department's geochemical laboratory to continue and maintain verification of ore grade analysis.",""],[1,"125","3","Fair Mineral Royalty Regime Development","Develop a fair royalty regime as required under Section 30 of the Constitution.",""],[1,"125","3","Mineral Act Review for Landowner Benefits","Reassess the Mineral Act to secure appropriate benefits to landowners.",""],[1,"125","3","Landowner-Investor Relations and Land Tenure Awareness","Encourage cordial relationships between landowners and investors, including awareness of land tenure issues and developments in the sector.",""],[1,"125","3","Updated Mineral Potential Information Provision","Provide updated and verified information on newly explored areas and their mineral potential.",""],[1,"125","3","Special Prospecting Licence Area Assessment","Carry out assessments on already explored Special Prospecting Licence (SPL) areas and other mineral potential .",""],[1,"125","3","Mined Area Resource Assessment","Carry out resource assessment on mined areas.",""],[1,"125","3","Local Skills and Employment Promotion in Mining","Strengthen local skills and increase employment opportunities generated through the mineral resources sector.",""],[1,"125","3","Mandatory Training Programmes for Investments","Ensure investments have training programmes as integral components.",""],[1,"125","3","Specialised Position Remuneration Review","Review remuneration of specialised positions to be on par with other industries.",""],[1,"125","7","Water Quality Control Legislation and Standards Reform","Strengthen legislation on water quality control, standards and use.",""],[1,"125","7","Geoscience Capacity Building for Groundwater Management","Provide necessary capacity building in geosciences that ensures better management and control of groundwater resources.",""],[1,"126","18","Staff Retention Training and Financial Assistance Initiative","Explore training opportunities, formalise and seek financial assistance JER to ensure staff retention",""],[1,"126","25","Formalisation of Roles and Responsibilities between MoA and MoEn","Formalise roles and responsibilities under MoA with MoEn","MoA | MoEn"],[1,"126","31","Government Advisory Services for Landowners on Royalty Use","This involves advisory services provided by government to land owners regarding share of royalties, environmental issues and utilisation of royalties for development purposes.",""]],"70":[[1,"18","1","Tax Administration and Compliance Reform","The tax regime has been reformed to improve tax administration, strengthen compliance and maintain broad-based and low tax rates.",""],[1,"92","12","National Tax Information System Development and Tax Administration Streamlining","Tax administration will be further improved through development of the National Tax Information System (NTIS), opening new Fiji Revenue & Customs Services (FRCS) offices around Fiji and streamlining processes to improve efficiency and consistency in tax administration.",""],[1,"93","11","National Tax Information System Development","Develop National Tax Information System.",""],[1,"93","11","FRCS Office Decentralisation for Tax Service Access","Decentralise FRCS Offices to improve access to taxation services.",""]],"71":[[1,"128","5","Tourism MSME Finance and Capacity Building Support","Support micro, small and medium scale tourism businesses through finance and capacity building initiatives.",""],[1,"128","5","Industry-Aligned Tourism Training Reform","Align training programmes with industry needs and focus on developing soft skills in tandem with management",""],[1,"128","5","Tourism Language Skills Promotion","Promote and support Mandarin and other Asian language proficiency in the tourism sector to support growth in skills.",""],[1,"128","5","Outer Islands Hospitality Training Centres","Set up hospitality training centres on outer islands experiencing consistent tourism activity.",""],[1,"128","5","International Scholarships for Culinary and Management Skills","Provide international scholarships to develop world-class culinary and management skills amongst locals.",""]],"72":[[1,"135","3","Digital Government Services Expansion","Digital Government implementation - make priority government services, particularly Disaster, Recovery",""],[1,"135","9","ICT-Based Public Sector Planning and Monitoring Tools","Prioritise the use of ICT based planning and monitoring tools in the public sector.",""],[1,"135","9","Digital Public Consultation Platform","Promote the use of social media to facilitate public consultations during policy formulation.",""],[1,"135","9","Expanded ICT Use in Public Service Delivery","Encourage widespread use of ICT in the public sector to improve work processes, productivity, and service delivery.",""],[1,"136","2","Online Government Services Expansion","Make priority Government services available online",""],[1,"136","3","Digital Government Systems Implementation","Implement Digital Government Registrar of Titles; Registrar of Companies; BDM registry; and Integrated Labour Market Information System",""],[1,"136","5","Digital Government NEC Registration","Implement Digital Government NEC registration",""]],"74":[[1,"3","6","2050 Decarbonisation Pathway","we will develop a 2050 Pathway to decarbonise the Fijian economy.",""],[1,"8","10","Renewable Electricity Expansion Programme","Electricity generation from renewable energy sources will be increased to 100 percent by 2036.",""],[1,"8","10","Ongoing Hydropower Projects","Apart from the ongoing hydro projects such as the Qaliwana/Upper Wailoa Diversion Hydro Project and Lower Ba Hydro Project, new areas will be identified for feasibility studies.",""],[1,"8","10","Renewable Energy Feasibility and Development Programme","Other renewable energy sources such as wind, solar, biomass, geothermal and wave and tidal energy will be developed where they are viable and affordable.",""],[1,"8","11","Climate-Resilient Electricity Infrastructure Projects","Future electricity infrastructure projects will be climate- resilient, and opportunities for underground cables for electricity distribution will be explored and adopted where feasible.",""],[1,"8","11","Clean Development Mechanism Financing for Electricity Infrastructure","Carbon credits under the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) will be employed as part of the financing arrangements.",""],[1,"8","11","Access to Additional Climate Finance","Other sources of climate finance will also be accessed.",""],[1,"9","1","Support for Independent Power Producers","Independent power producers of both small- and large- scale electricity production will be supported with fair pricing for sale of electricity.",""],[1,"9","1","Electricity Sector Regulatory Reform and FEA Divestment","The ongoing regulatory reforms in the electricity sector with the partial divestment of FEA will promote private sector participation and raise efficiency and service delivery.",""],[1,"30","4","Renewable Electricity Expansion Investment Programme","Electricity from renewable sources will be increased further.",""],[1,"30","5","Hydropower Project Development Programme","Three major hydro projects are currently being developed by the Fiji Electricity Authority (FEA).",""],[1,"30","5","Hydropower Site Investigation and Feasibility Studies","Future sites are being investigated, including the Upper Ba River, the Waivaka Hydropower Scheme in Namosi, and Wailevu River in Cakaudrove.",""],[1,"30","6","Renewable Energy Research and Development Programme","The research and development of new and renewable energy technologies will continue.",""]],"75":[[1,"11","2","Domestic and Transnational Crime Prevention and Response Programme","Adequate resources will be allocated to prevent and appropriately respond to domestic and transnational crimes, border security and access to justice.",""],[1,"11","2","Responsive Security Forces and Police Strengthening","Responsive security forces and police, together with an adapting legislative and policy framework, will support a strong approach to the administration of justice and maintenance of the rule of law.",""]],"76":[[1,"7","12","Job Creation Policy Package","With sustained economic expansion and the implementation of new job creation policies, the unemployment rate will be reduced to below 4 percent.",""],[1,"7","12","Skills Development and Entrepreneurship Promotion","A key focus will be on skills development and turning job seekers into job creators.",""],[1,"7","12","MSME Council and Central Coordinating Agency","With the establishment of the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) Council and Central Coordinating Agency, greater support and incentives will be provided to small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"7","12","Growth Sector Expansion Initiative","New growth sectors with high labour- absorption capacity will be nurtured and expanded.",""],[1,"7","12","Seasonal Overseas Employment Utilisation","Seasonal employment opportunities overseas will also be effectively utilised.",""],[1,"13","10","Employment Promotion for Skilled Fijians","Initiatives will be introduced to promote the employment of Fijians with these new skills by both small and large- scale businesses.",""],[1,"13","10","Youth Entrepreneurship Support","Support will be provided for youth entrepreneurship.",""]],"77":[[1,"8","3","Free Water Programme","To support low-income households, the free water programme will continue.",""],[1,"23","15","Free Water Initiative for Eligible Households","The free water initiative for households with combined household income of $30,000 that are consuming less than 91,250 litres per year will also continue.",""],[1,"24","9","Free Water Programme for Low-Income Households","Continuation of the free water programme for low-income households.",""]],"78":[[1,"10","5","Food and Nutrition Security Improvement Measures","Food and nutrition security will be improved by ensuring increased local production, raising farm efficiency and productivity, and developing more effective distribution systems.",""],[1,"10","5","Agriculture and Fisheries Programme Enhancement","Agriculture and fisheries programmes will be enhanced, and local produce made available to all Fijians.",""],[1,"10","6","Agricultural Technology and Mechanisation Adoption","New technology, mechanisation and better production practices will be adopted.",""],[1,"10","6","Market Linkage Improvement Initiative","Market linkages will be improved.",""],[1,"10","6","Large-Scale Production Support Programme","Large-scale production will be encouraged and supported to achieve greater economies of scale.",""],[1,"13","16","Agricultural Mechanisation and Modern Farming Techniques Initiative","government will further explore mechanised land preparation and harvesting, modern seed-breeding methods, and hydroponic and greenhouse farming techniques to address the issues of poor soil fertility, declining farm productivity and intermittent local supply.",""]],"79":[[1,"10","7","Organic Farming Promotion and Climate-Resilient Agriculture Support","Organic farming will be promoted, and production of traditional crops and niche agricultural and fisheries products will be pursued.",""],[1,"10","7","Agricultural Research Funding for Climate-Resilient Crop Varieties","To adapt to climate change, increased funding will be directed towards agriculture research into crop varieties that can be more resilient to expected changes in weather patterns.",""],[1,"10","7","Climate Adaptation Extension Training for Farmers","In addition, extension training will evolve to ensure that farming practices adapt to changes due to climate change.",""]],"80":[[1,"11","9","Sports Tourism Infrastructure Investment Programme","To support development of sports tourism, investments in new sporting facilities built to international standards will be prioritised together with increased accommodation capacity.",""],[1,"11","9","International Sports Event Hosting Strategy","Fiji will continue to position itself to host international sporting events such as the Pacific Games, Commonwealth Games, International Rugby Sevens, Super 15 rugby matches, golf tournaments and other sports.",""]],"81":[[1,"8","11","Access to Additional Climate Finance","Other sources of climate finance will also be accessed.",""],[1,"14","12","Domestic Revenue Mobilization and External Financing for Development Projects","government will mobilise its domestic revenues, both tax and non-tax, and access international financial resources, including funding from multilateral development partners.",""],[1,"14","12","Self-Financing of SOE and Municipal Council Projects","Self-funding of projects undertaken by State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) and municipal councils will complement funding from the central government.",""],[1,"14","13","Private Sector Partnership and Climate Finance Mobilization","Financing through private sector partnerships and climate finance will increasingly be a core source of financing.",""],[1,"21","6","Climate Finance Mobilization and Adaptation Support","We will work together with other nations to access climate finance and explore innovative ways of mobilising public and private sector resources for adaptation and mitigation.",""]],"82":[[1,"21","6","Community-Based Adaptation Planning Support","This includes support for community-based adaptation planning.",""]],"83":[[1,"20","5","Public Finance Management Reform","Reforms to improve management of public finances will continue.",""],[1,"20","6","Public Sector Accounting Reform and Asset Register Development","government has adopted cash-basis International Public Sector Accounting Standards (IPSAS) and will move towards accrual accounting in the future.",""],[1,"20","7","Government Procurement and Public Financial Management Capacity Building","Government procurement systems and processes have been enhanced, and we will continue to build capacity to improve the efficiency, effectiveness and accountability of the public financial management systems.",""]],"84":[[1,"20","11","Support for Independent Commissions and Elections Office Capacity","Resources have been allocated to independent commissions to enable the effective performance of their constitutional roles and responsibilities.",""],[1,"20","11","Local Government Legislative Framework Reform","Reforms to the legislative framework for local government will be implemented to facilitate the conduct of municipal elections.",""]],"85":[[1,"21","1","Corruption Prevention Risk Reduction Assessments","Effective enforcement of the anti-corruption legal framework will be complemented by Corruption Prevention Risk Reduction (CPRR) Assessments for government ministries and departments and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"21","1","Annual Auditor-General Audits","It will also be supported by annual audits by the Office of the Auditor-General under the accountability framework to maintain the integrity of, and public confidence in, the government's systems.",""]],"86":[[1,"21","2","Public Records Management Enhancement","The management of public records will be enhanced to ensure open and transparent government.",""]],"87":[[1,"30","9","Renewable Energy Tax Incentives","Tax incentives aimed at investments in renewable energy technologies will continue.",""],[1,"30","9","Support for Small-Scale Renewable Energy Systems","There are also opportunities for the private sector and households to invest in small- scale renewable systems that will be supported by government.",""],[1,"31","2","Biomass Energy Generation Expansion","Energy generation from biomass will be expanded over the next 5 years.",""],[1,"31","2","Navutu 10 MW Biomass Power Plant Construction","a10MW biomass power plant at Navutu, Sigatoka is currently being constructed by Nabou Green Energy Limited.",""],[1,"31","5","Piggery and Dairy-Farming Biogas Projects","Piggery and dairy-farming biogas projects that address waste management, health and energy needs are ongoing.",""],[1,"31","8","Grid Electricity Expansion and Improvement","Continue to develop the existing grid electricity supply in Viti Levu, Vanua Levu, Ovalau and · Develop small grid systems in other islands where practical.",""],[1,"31","8","Hydropower and Renewable Energy Facility Optimization","Review operation of hydropower and other renewable energy facilities to maximize output under new climate conditions.",""],[1,"31","9","Renewable Electricity Generation Expansion","Increase share of electricity generation from renewable energy resources.",""],[1,"31","10","Renewable Energy Research and Investment Identification Programme","Implement a research, data collection and investment identification programme to accelerate the renewable energy share in electricity generation.",""],[1,"32","6","Biofuels Development for Electricity and Transport","Reduce cost of petroleum imports and further develop biofuels (biodiesel and ethanol) for electricity and transport, while ensuring safety and security of supply.",""],[1,"32","9","Green Growth Framework Implementation","Implement Green Growth Framework for Fiji, in particular Way Forward outlined in Thematic Area 7 on Energy Security.",""],[1,"32","9","Off-grid Rural Electrification Management Improvement","Improve the effectiveness and sustainability of existing management models for off grid rural electrification including Renewable Energy Service Companies and community cooperatives to provide electricity to isolated communities and areas not served by the FEA.",""]],"88":[[1,"30","8","Partial Divestment of Fiji Electricity Authority","To encourage further private sector participation in the electricity sector, partial divestment of FEA is underway.",""],[1,"30","8","Independent Power Producer Framework Development","In developing an IPP framework to increase private sector generation of electricity from both renewable and non-renewable sources, government will ensure that a system of fair pricing and a transparent process are maintained.",""],[1,"31","10","Net-Metering Mechanism for Small-Scale Renewable Electricity","Establish a net-metering (or similar) mechanism to set out clear rules for small companies or households to feed excess electricity from renewables to the grid at a price fair to them and to FEA.",""],[1,"31","10","Feed-in Tariff Framework for Renewable Electricity","Set economically justified feed-in tariffs or pricing framework (price differential system) including studies to provide incentives for production of electricity from various renewable energy sources.",""],[1,"31","10","Independent Power Producer Framework Development","Undertake a study and develop an Independent Power Producer (IPP) framework that addresses the issue of intermittent supply of power from IPPs.",""],[1,"31","10","Transparent IPP Procurement and Grid Connection Standards","Establish a transparent process for procurement of new large-scale capacity from IPPs, pricing and other principles to be applied in all new power purchase agreements and grid connection standards.",""],[1,"31","11","Electricity Sector Regulatory Reform","Increase private sector participation in electricity supply through reform of regulatory aspects of the electricity sector.",""],[1,"31","12","Electricity Sector Regulatory Reform","Reform the regulation of the electricity sector to establish a more enabling environment for private sector participation in the electricity sector, including both large-scale and small-scale supply.",""]],"89":[[1,"30","10","Smart Grid Technology Adoption Exploration","FEA will also explore the possibility of adopting smart grid technologies, allowing for greater customer participation in managing demand.",""],[1,"30","10","Electricity Conservation and Energy-Efficient Technology Promotion","Electricity conservation and efficient technology to support energy saving will be promoted.",""],[1,"30","11","Mandatory Energy Efficiency Standards for Buildings and Industry","The codes and standards for buildings and industry will be updated to require mandatory minimum standards for energy use for ventilation, cooling and lighting, among other improvements.",""],[1,"31","4","Monitoring of Harmful Energy Sources","Government will monitor energy sources that may have a detrimental health effects",""],[1,"31","4","Affordable and Safe Alternative Energy Support","will provide an enabling environment for affordable and safe alternative energy sources.",""],[1,"32","2","Electricity Sector Energy Efficiency Improvement","Improve energy efficiency in the electricity sector.",""],[1,"32","3","Energy Efficiency Programmes","Implement programmes to ensure efficiency in energy use.",""],[1,"32","3","Building and Industry Energy Standards Update and Enforcement","Update the codes and standards for buildings and industry to require, among others, minimum standards for energy use for ventilation, cooling and lighting and enforce the application of these in both the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"32","4","Fiji Rocket Clean Cook Stove Expansion","Increase the number of communities utilising Fiji Rocket clean cook stoves",""],[1,"32","5","Community Education on Rocket Clean Cook Stove Construction and Maintenance","Continue to educate communities regarding the construction and maintenance of the Rocket Clean Cook stoves.",""]],"90":[[1,"30","7","Drought Contingency Power Supply Measures","Contingency plans to address prolonged periods of dry weather have been put in place with installation of an additional 40 MW of diesel generators.",""],[1,"30","12","Disaster-Resilient Electricity Infrastructure Upgrade","it will ensure that electricity infrastructure is made disaster-resilient.",""],[1,"30","12","Underground Cabling Options for Grid Distribution","Options for further underground cabling for grid distribution are being explored.",""],[1,"30","12","Cyclone-Resilient Renewable Energy Design and Certification Support","Government will also work closely with the private sector to improve designs, offer practical training and possibly support mandatory certification of designers/installers in order to improve resilience to cyclone conditions for renewable energy systems.",""],[1,"30","13","Environmental Appraisal of Future Energy Resource Projects","Environmental considerations will be factored into the appraisal of future hydro power, geothermal and other energy resources.",""],[1,"30","14","Electricity Sector Human Resource Development Programme","government will support education for civil, electrical and hydrological engineers and other required skill needs of the sector.",""],[1,"31","8","Energy Sector Human Resource Capacity Development","Continue to develop and improve the human resource capacity in the energy sector.",""],[1,"31","8","Climate-Resilient Energy Facility Standards Review","Review design and construction standards for energy facilities that are climate change resilient.",""]],"91":[[1,"30","16","Hybrid and Electric Vehicle Import Incentive","government has incentivised the importation of hybrid and electric cars over the last few years.",""],[1,"30","16","Vehicle Emissions Standard Upgrade","Fiji is complying with the Euro 2 emissions standard of 500 parts per million (PPM) of sulphur content and is moving towards the Euro 5 emission standard of 50 PPM.",""],[1,"30","16","Promotion of Environmentally Friendly Fuel Standards","Government will continue to promote and encourage the use of environmentally friendly fuel standards.",""],[1,"30","18","Biofuel Research and Development and Transport Sector Use Incentives","Government will continue research and development on biofuel and its use in the transport sector.",""],[1,"31","1","Biofuel Investment Promotion","promote investments in biofuel will continue.",""],[1,"32","7","Imported Petroleum Reduction Measures and Programmes","Implement various measures and programmes to reduce the volume and cost of imported petroleum",""],[1,"32","7","Domestic Product Development and Production Expansion Programme","Continue research and implementation of programmes to develop and increase production of products, while ensuring safety and security of supply.",""],[1,"32","7","Copra Replanting Support for Rural Biofuel Mills","Improve sustainable supply of copra to the rural biofuel mills through replanting programmes.",""]],"92":[[1,"36","6","Food and Nutrition Security Assessment Framework","an overarching framework will be developed to objectively assess the status",""],[1,"37","1","National Food and Nutrition Security Policy Framework","Develop a national food and nutrition security policy or framework.",""],[1,"37","2","Agriculture-Nutrition Enabling Environment","Create an enabling environment for agriculture nutrition nexus.",""],[1,"37","2","Joint Agriculture and Fisheries Census Surveys","Conduct periodic joint agriculture and fisheries census surveys.",""],[1,"37","2","Domestic Food Production Database Development","Strengthen statistics and information through the development of a Domestic Food Production Database (agriculture and fisheries) as well as through the existing Food Balance Sheet and National Nutrition Survey.",""],[1,"37","2","Sub-sector Plan Formulation Support","Support the formulation of sub-sector plans for agriculture, fisheries, biosecurity, health (nutrition) and · Strengthen the national commitment from across all sectors, industries and communities to collectively discuss education.",""],[1,"37","2","Evidence-Based Food Security Policy Support","Support evidence based policy and planning.",""],[1,"37","2","Crop Insurance Exploration","Explore opportunities for introduction of crop insurance.",""],[1,"37","2","Sustainable and Resilient Food Systems Promotion","Promote sustainable and resilient food systems.",""],[1,"37","2","Nutrition-Sensitive Value Chain Promotion","Promote nutrition-sensitive value chains to improve accessibility of nutritious food products.",""],[1,"37","2","Food and Nutrition Security Coordination Mechanism","Improve multi-sector co-ordination of food and nutrition security policy.",""],[1,"37","2","Nutrition Mainstreaming in Sectoral Policies","Mainstream nutrition into national sectoral policies and action plans.",""],[1,"37","5","Food and Nutrition Security Priority Implementation","Encourage the better implementation of food and nutrition security priorities in agriculture and fisheries and other sectors.",""],[1,"38","5","Multi-Sectoral Framework for Agrinutrition and NCD Response","Establish a framework for multi-sectoral approach for addressing agrinutriton and tackling NCDs in Fiji",""],[1,"38","6","Multistakeholder Technical Working Committee","Establishment of multistakeholder technical working committee",""]],"93":[[1,"36","7","Domestic Food Production and Fisheries Supply Expansion","Over the next 5 years, government will ensure increased domestic food production and supply of fisheries products.",""],[1,"36","8","Support for Large Commercial Agriculture and Aquaculture Projects","Large commercial agriculture and aquaculture projects will be supported to achieve economies of scale and competitive pricing.",""],[1,"36","8","Cluster Farming Promotion","Cluster farming will be encouraged",""],[1,"36","10","Agricultural Mechanisation and Technology Adoption Programme","Production efficiencies will be improved through mechanisation and the adoption of new technologies and better product varieties.",""],[1,"36","10","Agricultural Research and Extension Services Expansion","More research and extension services will be provided by government to improve farm productivity and awareness of best farming practices.","government"],[1,"36","10","Organic Farming Promotion","Organic farming practices will be employed.",""],[1,"36","11","Promotion of Locally Produced Fresh and Traditional Foods","Government will encourage the consumption of locally produced fresh foods and ensure that it is conveniently accessible at fresh food markets, supermarkets and road- side stalls.",""],[1,"36","11","Expansion of Traditional Food Supply","Assistance will be provided to expand the supply of traditional foods such as Uvi, Tivoli, Via, Dalo, Cassava and Kumala given their suitability to the local climate.",""],[1,"36","12","Fresh Food Consumption Awareness Programme","The consumption of fresh, home-grown food will be promoted through awareness programmes.",""],[1,"36","12","Climate-Resilient Food Supply Mitigation Measures","Strategies to mitigate climate change related effects on food supply will also be promoted.",""],[1,"37","6","Agricultural and Fisheries Research and Climate-Resilient Crop Development","Strengthen research and development and cooperation with regional and international research efforts in agricultural and fisheries and climate change implications and development of climate-resilient staple food",""],[1,"37","6","Soil Management Improvement Measures","Adoption of better soil management techniques to address increased soil salination and erosion.",""],[1,"37","6","Farm-Level Productivity Improvement Programme","Improve efficiency at farm level that ultimately contributes to low commodity pricing in the market.",""],[1,"37","6","Crop Breeding and Seed Storage Infrastructure Upgrade","Improve crop breeding infrastructure and seed storage facilities.",""],[1,"37","6","Food and Nutrition Security Programmes","Specific domestic Food and nutrition security programmes for key primary food industries for agriculture, fisheries and health (nutrition).",""],[1,"37","6","Traditional Farming Skills Revitalisation Programme","Promote the revitalisation and enhancement of traditional farming skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"38","25","Climate-Resilient Crop Research and Development","Strengthen research and development, including development and promotion of crops resilient to climate change",""]],"94":[[1,"37","3","Food and Nutrition Security Awareness Campaign","Raise more awareness on the importance of food and nutrition security.",""],[1,"37","4","Local Media Awareness Programmes for Food and Nutrition Security","Strengthen existing and pursue new awareness programmes on local media to maximize outreach.",""],[1,"37","4","Food and Nutrition Security Partnership Framework","Strengthen partnerships & shared responsibilities for increased food and nutrition security.",""],[1,"37","4","Local Food Initiative with Corporate and Civil Society Participation","Encourage the involvement of corporate and civil society entities to be part of the initiative to feed Fiji locally.",""],[1,"37","4","School-Based Food Security Awareness Engagement","Increase interaction and involvement of primary, secondary and tertiary schools to encourage the younger generation to be more food secure conscious.",""],[1,"37","6","Mobile Market Information System","Establish an efficient system for collecting and disseminating market information through mobile networks.",""],[1,"37","6","Primary Agriculture and Fisheries Market Arrangements Reform","Improve market arrangements for primary agriculture and fisheries produce.",""],[1,"38","18","Market Information System Rollout","Rolling out Market Information System (MIS)",""]],"95":[[1,"40","8","Digital Literacy Programme for Teachers and Students","A digital literacy programme has been introduced to encourage teachers and students to benefit from",""],[1,"40","9","National E-Learning Expansion Programme","This initiative will be expanded and rolled out to the entire education system in a phased approach.",""],[1,"41","2","School ICT and E-Learning Expansion","Strengthen use of ICT, distance learning and e-learning in schools.",""],[1,"41","4","FEMIS Upgrade","Updating of the Fiji Education Management Information System (FEMIS) to cover all aspects of school information.",""],[1,"41","4","National E-Library Development","Development of an e-library or virtual library for all citizens.",""]],"96":[[1,"44","8","Communicable Disease Early Detection and Prevention Strengthening","Early detection and preventive measures will be strengthened to address communicable diseases like HIV/ AIDS and tuberculosis.",""],[1,"45","6","Integrated Communicable Disease, Environmental Health, and Emergency Preparedness Services","Improve and integrate services targeting communicable diseases, environmental health, and emergency preparedness, response and climate change resilience.",""],[1,"45","7","Multi-Sectoral Communicable Disease Risk Management and Resilience","Improve multi-sectoral approach to risk management and resilience for communicable diseases,",""],[1,"45","7","Communicable Disease Case Detection and Coordinated Response","Improve case detection and coordinated response to reduce communicable disease morbidity and health emergencies, climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"66","12","Health Emergency Contingency Planning","Introduce contingency plans to counter health risks and global disease outbreaks (such as Ebola and other contagious diseases or influenzas).",""]],"97":[[1,"44","3","Health Supplies and Procurement Streamlining","Funding will be channelled towards purchase of more equipment, drugs and consumables.",""],[1,"44","3","Procurement and Supply Chain Management Streamlining","The procurement process and supply-chain management will be streamlined",""],[1,"44","8","Referral and Evidence Preservation for Violence Cases","Physical and sexual violence against women and children will be addressed as Fiji practitioners will adhere to processes of referral and evidence preservation to support women and increase the rate of perpetrator accountability.",""],[1,"45","7","Health Facility Energy and Water Efficiency Retrofit","Retrofit health facilities to improve energy and water efficiency.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Facility Quality and Safety Monitoring","Continuous monitoring and improvement of quality and safety standards in government health facilities.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Customer Feedback Centre","Establish Customer Feedback Centre.",""],[1,"45","9","Evidence-Based Health Planning and Budgeting","Policy, planning and budgeting based on sound evidence, considerations of efficiency and cost- effectiveness and health information systems that provide relevant, accurate information to the right people at the right time.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Legislation and Policy Review","Review and develop new health legislation and policies that will facilitate delivery of safe and quality healthcare at all levels.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Financing Improvement","Improve health financing, equity and efficiency.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Workforce Recruitment, Training and Retention","Recruit, train and retain a qualified, motivated health workforce that is caring, customer-focused, and responsive to population health needs.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Supply Chain Reform","Reform Supply Chain Management and ensure high quality medicinal products are rationally used and readily accessible to all residents.",""],[1,"45","9","Biomedical Equipment Provision for Health Facilities","Ensure that all health facilities in Fiji have the minimum required functional biomedical equipment for the level of the facility.",""],[1,"45","9","Health Infrastructure Database and Maintenance System","Develop a health infrastructure database and ensure that all MoHMS infrastructure is built and maintained to meet operational and population needs in compliance with all relevant health service standards.",""],[1,"49","14","Expansion of Electronic Patient Management Information Systems","Expand coverage of electronic patient management information systems in facilities",""],[1,"50","1","Health Data and Statistics Improvement Initiative","Improve availability and consistency of key health data and statistics",""],[1,"50","3","Medical Supplies Inventory Management System Improvement","Improve Medical Supplies Inventory Management System at all levels",""],[1,"50","14","Functional Supply Chain Management System for Medicinal Products","Establish functional supply chain management system to improve medicinal product availability",""],[1,"51","11","FPBS Property Maintenance and Infrastructure Upgrading","Maintenance of existing FPBS Property",""]],"98":[[1,"54","5","MSME and Self-Employment Support Initiative","A major focus in the years ahead will be to support MSMEs and other self-employment initiatives to ensure all Fijians have a stable source of income.",""],[1,"54","5","Socio-Economic Rights Realisation Measures","Major government initiatives will ensure that the guarantee of socio-economic rights in the Constitution is realised.",""],[1,"55","3","Baseline Data and Needs Assessment Strengthening","Strengthen data gathering for baseline studies and analyses of the needs of children, elderly, people with disabilities and assessments of poverty.",""],[1,"55","3","Policy Review for Vulnerable Group Empowerment","Review and, if needed, enhance education, employment, trade, fiscal and other government policies as they impact vulnerable groups and social empowerment programmes.",""],[1,"55","3","Child Rights and Vulnerable Persons Legislation Implementation","Implement, monitor and review legislation relating to the principles and provisions of the Convention on the Rights of the Child, Convention on the Rights of Older Persons, Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disability and other relevant international instruments.",""],[1,"55","5","Empowerment Programmes for Vulnerable Groups","Strengthen empowerment programmes to build capacity among vulnerable groups and create access to productive resources to facilitate migration from welfare to workfare.",""],[1,"55","5","Partnerships with Faith-Based Organisations and NGOs","Continue to engage with faith based organisations and NGOs in promoting family values and social affairs.",""],[1,"55","5","Social Inclusion and Participation of Vulnerable People","Promote greater integration and participation of vulnerable people in decision-making and community cohesion.",""],[1,"55","5","Older Persons and Special Needs Employment Support","Increase labour force participation and self-employment of older persons and those with special needs.",""],[1,"55","5","Post-Traumatic Counselling and Disaster Vulnerability Mapping","Provision of post-traumatic counselling services for the vulnerable groups after natural disasters including the identification and mapping of communities that are most vulnerable to disasters.",""],[1,"55","16","Vocational and Skills Training Programme","Vocational/ Skill Training Programme formulated and implemented",""],[1,"56","19","Establish NCOP Administration Arm","Establish Administration arm for (NCOP)",""]],"99":[[1,"57","2","Financial Support for Voluntary Organisations","Financial support will continue to be made available for voluntary organisations in these areas.",""],[1,"57","4","Youth Participation in National Policy Development Initiatives","Initiatives that empower youth and encourage their participation in national policy development will continue, such as the International Youth Exchange Programme, National Youth Conference and Youth Parliament initiative.",""],[1,"58","3","Youth Leadership Participation and Dialogue Forums","Promote youth issues and youth participation in leadership and decision-making processes at all levels through Annual National Youth Conferences, Youth Parliament initiatives and national dialogue forums for",""],[1,"58","3","Youth Community Development Engagement Strategy","Initiate collaborative strategies between government and communities to increase the capacity and engagement of Fiji's youth in the community and economy.",""],[1,"58","3","Youth Civic Education and Democracy Awareness Programme","Educate youth on decision-making and leadership in government through a systematic awareness programme on the founding principles of democracy as in the Constitution and the National Youth Policy in partnership with the Elections Office, the Electoral Commission and UNDP.",""]],"100":[[1,"61","6","Review Labour and Employment Laws for Gender Equality","Review labour and employment laws and human resource development as per the National Gender Policy and ensure equal access of men and women to formal sector employment.",""],[1,"61","6","Review Wage Setting and Informal Sector Inequities","Examine wage differentials and the drivers of inequity in wage setting and informal sector",""],[1,"61","6","Gender-Responsive Agriculture Policy Review","Review agriculture policies and laws with a view to enabling men and women to benefit equally from employment.",""],[1,"61","12","Review of HIV/AIDS Decree Effectiveness","Ongoing review of the effectiveness of the HIV/AIDS Decree in removing stigma and discrimination for those living with or affected by HIV and AIDS in relation to the right to employment, promotion",""],[1,"61","14","Review of Legislation and Policies for Gender Equality","Review legislation and policies to enhance their relevance to women and gender equality.",""]],"101":[[1,"63","2","Cultural Mapping and Cultural Statistics Framework","The ongoing cultural mapping programme and framework for gathering cultural statistics will be a key initiative to gather information on traditional knowledge and heritage.",""],[1,"63","2","Mainstreaming Culture in the Educational Curriculum","This will also support the mainstreaming of culture in educational curriculum.",""],[1,"63","4","National Documentary Preservation and Public Access Programme","The nation's vast documentary will be preserved in accordance with archival conservation practices and made available to all Fijians.",""],[1,"64","4","Archives Valuation Exercise","Finalise an archives valuation exercise to determine the total monetary value of the heritage items at National Archives of Fiji (NAF).",""],[1,"64","4","Culture and Heritage Curriculum Integration","Integrate culture, heritage and arts in formal education curricula at all levels through the Fiji cultural and education strategy as outlined in the Green Growth Framework for Fiji.",""],[1,"65","7","Digital Archival System for iTaukei Customs and Knowledge","Develop a digital archival system for preservation of iTaukei customs and knowledge",""]],"102":[[1,"66","2","Protection from Environmental Risks and Natural Disasters","focus will also be placed on protecting Fijians from environmental risks and natural disasters, transnational crimes (human and drug trafficking), food and nutrition security and public health risks and financial and cybercrime.",""],[1,"66","4","Community Engagement and Public Awareness Programmes","Programmes to promote community engagement and public awareness will be pursued.",""],[1,"66","5","Border Security Coordination and Resource Support","Border security will be maintained through improved coordination and ensuring availability of adequate resources.",""],[1,"66","5","National Security Strategy Implementation","Fiji will continue implementation of its National Security Strategy and support for UN Peacekeeping operations.",""],[1,"66","9","Strengthen National Security and Defence Institutional Arrangements","Strengthen institutional arrangements within the national security and defence framework.",""],[1,"66","10","National Security Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the National Security Strategy (NSS).",""],[1,"66","10","Ministry of Defence and National Security Restructuring","Restructure the Ministry of Defence and National Security to strengthen its arm in coordination of national security matters, including strengthening technical capacities.","Ministry of Defence and National Security"],[1,"66","10","National Security Public Awareness Campaign","Enhance publicity and public awareness on 'National Security? (Relations with the public) by dissemination of timely information on key policies of government and national security matters.",""],[1,"66","11","Border Security Strengthening","Strengthen border security.",""],[1,"66","12","Border Security and Migration Management Measures","Introduce contingency plans to prevent any form of illegal incursions into Fiji and invest in technologies to improve passport issuance and border security.",""],[1,"66","12","Transnational Crime Border Management Practices","Reduce threats of transnational crimes by adopting and implementing the best border management practices at all ports of entry.",""],[1,"66","12","Migration Monitoring Enhancement","Enhance management and monitoring of migration.",""],[1,"66","12","Maritime Surveillance and Patrol Strengthening","Strengthen maritime surveillance systems and patrols to eliminate illegal fishing and human trafficking.",""],[1,"66","12","Hydrographic Service Strengthening","Strengthen the hydrographic service.",""],[1,"66","12","Search and Rescue and Civil Defence Capacity Strengthening","Enhance Search and Rescue and Civil Defence capabilities.",""],[1,"66","14","Implementation of Defence White Paper Recommendations","Implementation of the recommendations of the Defence White Paper.",""],[1,"66","14","Review of the Republic of Fiji Military Forces Act","Review of the Republic of Fiji Military Forces (RFMF) Act.",""],[1,"66","14","Compliance with International Treaties and Agreements","Compliance with international treaties and agreements in the best interest of Fiji.",""],[1,"67","2","International Peacekeeping and Security Cooperation","Strengthen Fiji's involvement in international peacekeeping and security.",""],[1,"67","2","Regional and International Security Cooperation","Enhance regional and international cooperation to help strengthen national security partners and allies.",""]],"103":[[1,"66","1","Constitution Protection and Rule of Law Safeguarding","The Fijian Constitution will be protected and defended at all times.",""],[1,"66","6","Access to Justice Improvement","Government will continue its efforts to further improve access to justice.",""],[1,"66","6","Correctional Services and Inmate Rehabilitation","Correctional services and rehabilitation of inmates for re-integration of inmates into society will continue.",""],[1,"66","7","Legal Aid and Decentralized Justice Services Expansion","Provision of resources will continue for legal aid services, court sittings in rural and outer islands, and the greater decentralisation of services.",""],[1,"67","3","Justice System Strengthening","Strengthen the justice system.",""],[1,"67","4","Court Facilities and Legal Services Upgrade","Upgrade court facilities and infrastructure and expand legal services to improve citizen's access to justice.",""]],"104":[[1,"68","2","Institutional Strengthening of the National Security and Defence Framework","Strengthen institutional arrangements within the national security and defence framework.",""],[1,"68","3","National Security Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the National Security Strategy (NSS).",""],[1,"68","3","Ministry of Defence and National Security Restructuring","Restructure the Ministry of Defence and National Security to strengthen its arm in coordination of national security matters, including strengthening technical capacities.","Ministry of Defence and National Security"],[1,"68","3","National Security Public Awareness Campaign","Enhance publicity and public awareness on 'National Security' (Relations with the public) by dissemination of timely information on key policies of government and national security matters.",""],[1,"68","7","Implementation of Defence White Paper Recommendations","Implementation of the recommendations of the Defence White Paper.",""],[1,"68","7","Review of the Republic of Fiji Military Forces Act","Review of the Republic of Fiji Military Forces (RFMF) Act.",""],[1,"68","7","Compliance with International Treaties and Agreements","Compliance with international treaties and agreements in the best interest of Fiji.",""],[1,"69","5","Ministry of Defence and National Security Restructuring","Restructure the Ministry of Defence and National Security.","Ministry of Defence and National Security"],[1,"69","9","Public Awareness Programme on National Security","Public Awareness programme on National Security",""]],"105":[[1,"68","4","Border Security Strengthening","Strengthen border security.",""],[1,"68","5","Border Security and Migration Management Measures","Introduce contingency plans to prevent any form of illegal incursions into Fiji and invest in technologies to improve passport issuance and border security.",""],[1,"68","5","Migration Monitoring Enhancement","Enhance management and monitoring of migration.",""],[1,"69","11","Integrated Passport Issuance System","Establish an Integrated Passport Issuance System",""],[1,"69","15","Immigration Rule Review for Work Permit Facilitation","Review immigration rules to remove unnecessary obstacles for foreigners such as the issuance of work permits",""],[1,"69","18","Security Contingency Planning","Establish contingency plans for security: i) Global disease outbreaks ii) Illegal incursions",""]],"106":[[1,"68","5","Maritime Surveillance and Patrol Strengthening","Strengthen maritime surveillance systems and patrols to eliminate illegal fishing and human trafficking.",""],[1,"68","5","Hydrographic Service Strengthening","Strengthen the hydrographic service.",""],[1,"68","5","Search and Rescue and Civil Defence Capacity Enhancement","Enhance Search and Rescue and Civil Defence capabilities.",""],[1,"70","3","Enhance Fiji Hydrographic Service","Enhance Fiji Hydrographic Service",""],[1,"70","28","Water Police Strengthening","Strengthen water police (e.g. police boat and training)",""],[1,"70","30","Specialised Police Boat Procurement and Vessel Retrofit","7 new specialised police boats and retrofit of M.V. Veiqaravi",""]],"107":[[1,"68","5","Health Emergency Contingency Planning","Introduce contingency plans to counter health risks and global disease outbreaks (such as Ebola and other contagious diseases or influenzas).",""]],"108":[[1,"73","3","Street Lighting Upgrade Programme","A major street lighting programme is being undertaken to replace all faulty streetlights and install new ones with LED lights in both urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"73","5","Urban and Peri-Urban Footpath Construction Programme","Construction of footpaths will be continued in populated urban and peri-urban areas including industrial areas and residential subdivisions.",""]],"109":[[1,"73","4","Road Traffic Safety and Congestion Reduction Measures","Government will install traffic lights at junctions, develop roundabouts and re-design some of the existing high- traffic roads to ease traffic congestion and make our roads safer.",""],[1,"73","7","Weighbridge Construction and Road Weight Compliance Enforcement","more weighbridges will be constructed to ensure that shippers comply with the weight limits on our roads and bridges.",""],[1,"75","3","Road Safety Action Plan Implementation","Continue implementation of actions under the Fiji Decade of Action for Road Safety 2011-2020",""],[1,"75","3","Road Accident and Fatality Reduction Measures","Introduce effective measures to reduce the number of road accidents and deaths.",""],[1,"75","3","Driver Education, Licensing, Testing and Enforcement Reform","Improve driver education, licensing, testing and enforcement through:",""],[1,"75","3","Driving Instructor Code of Practice and Simulator-Based Testing","Code of practice (COP) for driving instructors; driving tests to be conducted using a simulator and independent parties; and increase in required training hours to secure a driving licence.",""],[1,"75","7","Specialized Driving School Driver Training","Specialized driving school that provides driver training for all classes of license;",""],[1,"75","8","Defensive Driving Training for Public Service Vehicle Drivers","All Public Service Vehicle (PSV) drivers will complete a defensive driving course (DDC);",""],[1,"75","9","Driver Demerit Point Reform Training Program","Habitual offenders to undergo DDC reform training program.",""],[1,"75","9","Coordination Improvement Among Road Safety Institutions","Improve coordination between LTA, Police and Driving Schools Association (DSA);",""],[1,"75","10","Driver Records Linkage System","Link driver records at Police and LTA; and",""],[1,"75","11","Transport Data Collection and Sharing Improvement","LTA to improve data collection, analysis and sharing of data with relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"75","12","Safer Vehicle Standards Development","Develop safer vehicles standards through:",""],[1,"75","13","Used Vehicle Import Safety Standards","Importation of used vehicles to be made conditional on satisfactory safety features;",""],[1,"75","14","Automated Vehicle Roadworthiness Inspection System","Establishing an automated vehicle roadworthiness inspection system within LTA;",""],[1,"75","15","Vehicle Repairer and Tyre Accreditation System","Establishing accreditation of vehicle repairers and service agencies and tyres to guard against counterfeiting;",""],[1,"75","16","Automotive Technical Trades Training","Providing automotive technical trades-training in-house and through overseas courses;",""],[1,"76","2","Road Safety Education and School Zone Safety Programme","Extend road safety education to all levels of education through teacher training courses and materials, police and LTA educational visits to schools, discounted driving courses for older children and the continuation of practical safety measures in school zones;",""],[1,"76","3","Road Safety Education Curriculum Review","LTA and Ministry of Education to discuss whether road safety education could be made mandatory for school curriculum;","LTA | Ministry of Education"],[1,"76","4","Driving School Audit and Penalty Enforcement","Frequent audits on driving schools and having stricter penalties;",""],[1,"76","5","Road Safety Park Establishment","Exploring the establishment of a Road Safety Park;",""],[1,"76","6","Road Safety Education and Pedestrian Enforcement","Road safety education to focus on pedestrians, drivers, passengers and vehicles.",""],[1,"76","17","Traffic Accident Data System Upgrade and Staff Training","Enhance traffic accident data and research through review of the Microcomputer Accident Analysis Package (MAAP) accident data system and new computer systems, accident reconstruction software for forensic accident investigation and train new and existing staff in the traffic-accident data system, including data entry of input forms and crash data extraction.",""],[1,"76","19","Vehicle Garage Accreditation and Road Marshal Programmes","Explore accreditation of all vehicle garages, introduction of Japan Export Vehicle Inspection Centre (JEVIC) and encourage voluntary road marshal and junior marshal programme.",""],[1,"77","19","Fiji Decade of Action for Road Safety Plan","Fiji Decade of Action for Road Safety Plan to be implemented",""]],"110":[[1,"74","6","Rural Transportation Services Expansion","Extending rural transportation services.",""],[1,"74","7","Rural Service License and Rural Transport Service Review","Review the guidelines and the legal framework on the issuance of Rural Service Licenses (RSLs).",""],[1,"74","7","Rural Bus Route and Timetable Expansion","Review bus routes and timetables with the intention to increase services in the rural areas.",""],[1,"74","7","Land Transport Industry Reform Implementation","Implement the key recommendations of the \"Report on Land Transport Industry\" by Ministry of Justice and Anti-Corruption (2015) after assessment by the Land Transport Authority (LTA).","Ministry of Justice and Anti-Corruption"],[1,"74","7","Rural-Urban Transport Network Design Model","Explore whether a rural transport network design model could be developed that will improve and facilitate the efficient operation of rural-urban hubs.",""],[1,"74","7","Rural Transport Operator Incentive Scheme","Consider provision of incentives for rural transport operators; for example in the form of tax rebates, concessions, and operators given licence to operate on an economical route to service an uneconomical route.",""]],"111":[[1,"76","7","Post-Accident Emergency Response Time Improvement","Improve the post-accident emergency response time by:",""],[1,"76","9","Ambulance Fleet Expansion and Personnel Training","Provision of 20 additional ambulances and trained personnel;",""],[1,"76","11","Community and Patrol First Aid Training","First aid training to be provided to communities and Police and LTA patrols;",""],[1,"76","12","Medical Trauma Response Kit Provision","Medical trauma response kits to be provided to health centres along the main highways.",""],[1,"76","13","Expansion of Service Coverage to Additional Areas","Extend areas served from Suva to another 11 areas namely Navua, Deuba, Sigatoka, Ba, Rakiraki, Korovou, Nadi, Lautoka, Savusavu, Labasa and Taveuni;",""],[1,"76","14","Rapid Assessment and Response Kit Procurement","Procure complementary rapid assessment and response (RAR) kits, communication and data entry equipment; and",""],[1,"76","16","Road Trauma Emergency and Injury Care Capacity Improvement","Improve A&E capacity and management for road-trauma injury patients.",""]],"112":[[1,"76","17","Accident Compensation Act and Fiji Accident Compensation Commission","Introduction of Accident Compensation Act by 1 January 2018 and establishment 'Fiji Accident Compensation Commission' to provide a 'no fault' compensation scheme.",""]],"113":[[1,"80","5","Seafarer and Maritime Skills Development Programme","Education and training of seafarers and development of other skilled personnel needed by the industry will be strengthened through provision of scholarships and review of the training module by the Fiji Maritime Academy.",""],[1,"81","2","Seafarer Training and Scholarship Programme","Review the training module for seafarers by Fiji Maritime Academy and provision of at least 10 imported. scholarships each year for the next five years to train more seafarers.",""],[1,"82","5","Seafarer Certification and Maritime Training Oversight","Crew on Fijian registered ships are required to hold certificates of competency issued through MSAF or equivalent overseas certification; MSAF will maintain records of seafarers and their qualifications which will be periodically audited for · MSAF will continue to undertake a five yearly independent audit of the Fiji Maritime Academy and accuracy; any other approved maritime training institution with reports sent to IMO to ensure that Fiji remains in the IMO white list16 ; and · Government will undertake a review of recruitment, training and retention of Fiji-certified seafarers.",""]],"114":[[1,"81","2","Seaway and River Dredging Programme","Develop and dredge seaways and main rivers.",""],[1,"81","2","Transport Facilities Upgrade for Trade and Transshipment","Provide economical, safe, adequate and efficient facilities for the transport of goods and people to facilitate trade, transhipment and other related functions.",""],[1,"81","2","Jetties Location, Design, and Construction Upgrade","Ensure optimal location, updated design and construction of existing and new jetties.",""],[1,"81","6","Island Jetty and Small Boat Landing Policy Development","Develop necessary policies for provision of jetties and small boat landings for inhabited islands and isolated coastal populations.",""],[1,"81","6","Maritime Infrastructure Upgrade and Construction Programme","Upgrade and construct new infrastructure (jetties and berthing facilities) in the maritime islands including construction of waiting sheds.",""],[1,"81","6","Maritime Navigation and Mooring Infrastructure Provision","Provide adequate maritime infrastructure such as Aids to Navigation (AtoNs), Mooring Buoys, and · Replacement and/or maintenance of all AtoNs and beacons.",""],[1,"81","6","Public-Private Slipway Facility Development","Develop improved slipway facilities through a public private partnership.",""],[1,"81","6","Outer Island Port Upgrading Programme","Continue upgrading port facilities at a number of outer island ports to improve transport links for the residents in maritime areas.",""],[1,"88","1","Port Infrastructure Modernization","plans have been developed to modernise port infrastructure.",""],[1,"88","5","FSHIL Service Expansion Partnership","Partnerships between government and the private sector will be pursued to support the company in expanding its services in these areas.",""],[1,"89","6","Port Infrastructure Development","Develop port infrastructure to a level expected of international and regional ports.",""],[1,"91","23","Slipway Expansion and Ship Repair Facility Upgrade","Expansion of Slipway and upgrading Ship Repair facility (this include modernising the workshop facilities)",""],[1,"91","28","Lautoka Port Upgrade and Suva Wharf Strengthening","Upgrade and Expand Lautoka and upgrade by strengthening the wharf structure at Suva Ports",""]],"115":[[1,"80","6","Fuel Efficiency Improvement and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Options","Options will be explored to improve fuel efficiency at sea and ensure that infrastructure development is disaster-resilient.",""],[1,"83","1","Green Growth Framework for Sustainable Transportation","Implementation of the Green Growth Framework for Fiji, in particular the Way Forward outlined in Thematic Area 8 on Sustainable Transportation.",""],[1,"83","1","Low-Carbon and Renewable Shipping Measures","Strategies and actions not covered elsewhere include support for improved hull and propeller designs, purchase and trial of a vessel fuelled by renewable shipping. energy, assessment of 4-stroke outboard motors, and study of incentives for low-carbon domestic · Implement other climate change adaptation measures for environmentally friendly shipping services through:",""]],"116":[[1,"80","6","Marine Pollution Regulation and Enforcement","Environmental concerns such as risk of oil spills, waste discharge and damage to our marine ecosystem will be properly regulated and enforced.",""],[1,"81","6","Port Environmental Assessment and Planning Requirements","Undertake Environmental Impact Assessments (EIA) and Environmental Management Plans (EMP) and economic studies for any new port development.",""],[1,"83","1","Marine Pollution Convention Accession and Legislative Alignment","Fiji will become a signatory to the International Convention for the Prevention of Pollution from Ships (MARPOL) and other marine environment protection conventions including Antifouling Convention, Ballast Water Management, OPRC (International Convention on Oil Pollution) Convention and MSAF will maintain and implement legislation in conformity with these international convention","MSAF"],[1,"83","1","Oil Pollution Response Capability Upgrade","Fiji's pollution response capability will be upgraded using revenues from the Oil Pollution Levy (OPL) obligations; 21,22,23 · Review the level of the OPL on ship operators to a point that achieves a balance between readiness to Fund; respond to pollution incidents and costs to visit ships, particularly the cruise ship industry;",""],[1,"83","1","National Spill Contingency Plan Maintenance and Training Exercises","Maintain the National Spill Contingency Plan (NATPLAN) by regularly convening the Marine Spill Advisory Committee and conducting training exercises with national and international partner response organizations, in particular the Australian Maritime Safety Authority (AMSA);",""],[1,"84","1","Implementation of the NATPLAN and National Oil Spill Response Strategy","MSAF will pursue the implementation of the NATPLAN and National Oil Spill Response Strategy;","MSAF"],[1,"84","1","Establishment of Oil Spill Response Equipment and Facilities","MSAF will pursue the establishment of oil spill response equipment and facilities in strategic locations highlighted in the risk assessment report carried out by AMSA and the South Pacific Regional in Fiji waters;","MSAF | AMSA | South Pacific Regional Environment Programme (SPREP)"],[1,"84","1","Bilateral Agreements for International Marine Spill Assistance","Formulate and maintain bilateral agreements for engaging international assistance to respond to polluting cargo major pollution incidents beyond the normal capacity of Fiji, such as the sinking of a vessel containing Marine Infrastructure . Standards Subcommittee of NRCC, Fiji Ports Corporation Limited (FPCL), FRA and MSAF to prepare guidelines for environmental impact mitigation and climate change adaptation for maritime infrastructure, delineating each agency's responsibility.","NRCC | Fiji Ports Corporation Limited (FPCL) | FRA | MSAF"],[1,"89","5","Port Environmental Assessment and Management Requirements","Undertake environmental impact assessments and environmental management plans (EIA and EMP) and economic studies for any new port development.",""],[1,"90","1","Sustainable Port Environmental Practices","Promote sustainable development through application of world environmental best practices in all ports.",""],[1,"90","2","Maritime Pollution Prevention and Response Strengthening","The Maritime Safety Authority of Fiji (MSAF) to strengthen Fiji's implementation of the Tokyo Memorandum of Understanding.",""],[1,"90","2","Regional Maritime Standards and Cooperation Initiative","The Fiji maritime transport agencies will need to continue to engage in cooperative efforts with other countries in the region, working through regional organisations to achieve consistent and compatible standards and practices appropriate to the region across the maritime sector.",""],[1,"90","7","Oil Pollution Levy Fund Facility and Equipment Upgrade Programme","MSAF has requested Government that the Oil Pollution Levy (OPL) Fund be used to upgrade existing and implement new facilities and equipment to cover the risks and gaps in cover.",""]],"117":[[1,"85","2","Domestic Airport and Airstrip Upgrade Programme","government will allocate funding to upgrade and maintain domestic airports, airstrips, runways and associated facilities.",""],[1,"85","2","Maritime Airstrip Development Exploration","Construction of new airstrips in maritime areas will also be explored.",""],[1,"85","2","Domestic Flight Subsidy Scheme","government will continue subsidising domestic flights.",""],[1,"86","3","Rural Airstrip Upgrading and Maintenance","Continue with the upgrading and maintenance of rural airstrips.",""],[1,"86","3","Domestic Air Service Subsidy","Continue to provide subsidy to the domestic air service providers under the domestic air service subsidy",""],[1,"86","4","Domestic Air Services Expansion","Expand domestic air services.",""],[1,"86","5","Obstacle Limitation Survey Review for Matei Airport","Review of the Obstacle Limitation Survey (OLS) for Matei airport.",""],[1,"86","5","Matei Airstrip Scope Definition for ATR72-600 Operations","Define the scope of works for Matei airstrip for ATR72-600 performance requirements.",""],[1,"86","5","Rotuma Airstrip Upgrade and Resurfacing","Upgrade and resurface Rotuma Airstrip for ATR72-600 domestic operations.",""],[1,"86","5","Vanua Levu Airport Site Technical Studies and Infrastructure Support","Conduct technical studies (OLS and Geo Technical Surveys) to finalize the ideal location for an airport in Vanua Levu and government to assist AFL by investing in the necessary infrastructure required.",""],[1,"86","6","Outer Islands Airstrip Infrastructure Upgrading","Ensure better air service infrastructure facilities at all airstrips located in outer islands.",""],[1,"86","7","Domestic Airstrip Development and Upgrade Programme","Implement a programme to facilitate the development of new airstrips and upgrade current airstrips to ensure provision of reliable and quality domestic air services.",""],[1,"86","14","Rotuma Airport Upgrade and Resurfacing","Upgrade and resurfacing of Rotuma Air- port to accommodate ATR72-600",""]],"118":[[1,"85","3","Aviation Professional Training Strengthening","Training and education for aviation professionals like aircraft engineers; pilots and air traffic controllers will be strengthened to meet International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) standards.",""],[1,"85","3","Aviation Academy Training Expansion","The Aviation Academy will provide training for more controllers, air navigation engineers, security officers and rescue fire service officers for Airports Fiji Limited (AFL) and also train students from other Pacific Islands.",""],[1,"85","3","Fiji National University Aircraft Engineer Training","Fiji National University will continue to provide training for aircraft engineers for Fiji and the region.",""],[1,"85","3","Pilot Training School Continuation","The existing pilot training schools will also continue.",""],[1,"86","9","Aviation and Transport Professional Education Support","Encourage education and training for aviation professionals and transport economists, and other professionals and workers. by providing tertiary education scholarships and access to the Tertiary Education Loans Scheme (TELS).",""],[1,"91","22","Fiji Aviation Academy Construction and Training Facility","Construction of the Fiji Aviation Academy (flight simulators, new pilot training, cabin crew training and all wet and dry drills for cabin and pilot crew)",""]],"119":[[1,"85","4","Annual Aviation Safety Audit Programme","Safety audits will be continued on an annual basis for airlines operating under Air Transport Licensing Board (ATLB) licences and other aviation activities with certificates granted by the Civil Aviation Authority of Fiji (CAAF).",""],[1,"86","3","Civil Aviation Authority Operating Grant","Provide an operating grant to the Civil Aviation Authority of Fiji for air transport services, and a further programme. subsidy to serve uneconomical domestic routes.",""],[1,"86","8","Domestic Air Safety Standards Improvement","Ensure higher level of safety standards in domestic air services.",""],[1,"86","9","Domestic Air Services Safety and Security Standards Enforcement","Continue to enforce international standards in domestic air services to ensure safety and security of passengers",""],[1,"86","17","Safety and Security Standards Compliance Programme","Safety and security standards compliance programme (ensuring ICAO standards) (annual certification)",""],[1,"89","5","Aviation Regulatory Framework Modernisation","Modernisation of the Fijian aviation regulatory framework that meets International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) standards and recommended practices.",""],[1,"89","5","Civil Aviation Authority Sustainable Funding Mechanism","Ensure Civil Aviation Authority of Fiji (CAAF) is adequately funded through independent and sustainable source of funding.","Civil Aviation Authority of Fiji (CAAF)"],[1,"89","5","Civil Aviation Human Resource Capacity Retention","Maintain and retain a competent human resource capacity to effectively oversee civil aviation plans, strategies and activities.",""],[1,"89","5","ICAO Safety and Security Rating Improvement Programme","Improve Fiji's international safety and security ratings under the ICAO Universal Safety (USOAP) and Security (USAP) Audit programmes.",""],[1,"89","5","Civil Aviation Safety Oversight System Implementation","Effective and efficient implementation of safety oversight system.",""],[1,"89","6","Civil Aviation Oversight System Strengthening","Maintain a strong, independent, autonomous and efficient civil aviation oversight system that meets ICAO standards and international best practices.",""],[1,"91","7","Performance Based Navigation Implementation at Nausori Airport","Provide Performance Based Navigation (PBN) for Nausori Airport similar to Nadi Airport",""],[1,"91","13","AIM and SWIM Implementation","Implementation of AIM & SWIM as per ICAO ASBU plan",""],[1,"91","21","Aviation Safety Oversight System Strengthening","Progress Fiji's implementation of an effective safety oversight system to meet ICAO standards",""]],"120":[[1,"87","7","Airport and Seaport Modernisation and Expansion","modernising and expanding Fiji's airports and seaports and provision of efficient services will continue in partnership with relevant agencies.",""],[1,"87","8","Second International Terminal and Domestic Terminal Upgrade","There are now plans to construct a second international terminal and an upgraded domestic terminal.",""],[1,"87","9","Nausori International Airport Upgrade Works","Upgrade works for the Nausori International Airport terminal and runway will also be undertaken to continually raise standards and facilities.",""],[1,"87","9","New International Airport Development in Vanua Levu","Government is also exploring options for development of a new international airport in Vanua Levu that will support our vibrant tourism industry and international passenger movements.",""],[1,"87","10","National Air Carrier Fleet Renewal Investment","Fiji Airways has also been undertaking major investments in renewing its fleet through both outright purchases and leasing arrangements.",""],[1,"87","11","Airline Route Expansion Support","government will assist Fiji Airways in exploring and establishing new routes across the globe.",""],[1,"89","3","Nadi International Airport Upgrade and Modernisation","Complete upgrade and modernisation of Nadi International Airport.",""],[1,"89","3","Fiji Airways Fleet Modernisation and Route Expansion","Ongoing modernisation of the Fiji Airways fleet and the introduction of new international destinations.",""],[1,"89","4","Nausori Airport Upgrade and New Airport Development","Continue upgrading Nausori airport and development of new airport to provide more international services.",""],[1,"89","5","Nausori Airport Terminal and Runway Upgrade","Construct new Terminal and upgrade and extend runway at Nausori Airport.",""],[1,"89","5","Vanua Levu International Airport Construction","Construct new international airport in Vanua Levu.",""],[1,"90","13","Nadi Apron Expansion","Expand Nadi Apron space to cater for business jets and increased commercial movement",""],[1,"91","1","International Transit Hotel Construction","Construction of International Transit Hotel in Nadi",""]],"121":[[1,"88","4","Ports Master Plan Development","A long-term Ports Master Plan with a 7-year implementation plan is currently being developed to determine the current state and scope of international port operations.",""],[1,"88","4","New International Seaport Development in Vanua Levu","Government is exploring options for development of a new international seaport in Vanua Levu and the possibility of relocating cargo services from the Suva Wharf.",""],[1,"88","4","Vanua Levu Port Feasibility and Design Studies","An initial feasibility study for the port in Vanua Levu has been undertaken, with work underway for technical, economic and environmental impact assessment and detailed design work.",""],[1,"89","5","Ports Master Plan Formulation and Implementation","Formulate Ports Master Plan and implement its recommendations.",""],[1,"89","5","Rokobili Port Feasibility Study","Explore the viability for the construction of Rokobili Port.",""],[1,"91","24","New International Port Feasibility and Detailed Design Studies","Undertake further technical, economic and environmental studies and detailed design to confirm the viability of new international port in Vanua Levu.",""],[1,"91","25","Rokobili Port Construction Feasibility Study","Explore viability for construction of Rokobili Port",""],[1,"91","27","Secure PPP Financing for Rokobili Port","Secure PPP for financing of Rokobili Port",""]],"122":[[1,"88","2","Port Capacity and Efficiency Upgrade","Investments will be made to raise berthing capacity and water depth, improve port efficiency, reduce turnaround time, adopt modern technology (communications and information technology), and make supporting industries and services available, with reasonable charges levied.",""],[1,"89","5","Fiji Ports Terminal Market Access and Route Expansion Support","Support Fiji Ports Terminal Limited to secure additional routes and services and access to wider markets, i.e. increased competition for shipping lines and additional and new shipping lines.","Fiji Ports Terminal Limited"],[1,"89","5","Shipping Freight Rate Review and Logistics Efficiency Reform","Review shipping freight rates with view to lowering the cost of doing business in Fiji through all freight being sorted at the hub, improved efficiency, and reduced risk of error.",""],[1,"89","5","Port Efficiency Improvement Programme","Improve port efficiency by improving average container movement and cargo handling turnaround time.",""],[1,"90","4","Port Operational Efficiency and Revenue Enhancement Measures","Improve operating income by continuously introducing modern systems and controls, standards, new working conditions, and more skilled workers to improve port operational efficiency.",""],[1,"90","4","Prudent Cost Control and Internal Audit Strengthening","Minimize or sustain operating expenditure by implementing prudent controls over major overhead costs and effective audit and internal control systems.",""],[1,"90","4","Port Infrastructure Expansion and Facility Investment","Invest in infrastructure and expansion of facilities generating higher asset base and profits.",""],[1,"90","4","Higher-Income Generating Asset and Project Investment","Generate and invest in higher income generating activities to boost profit levels, such as infrastructure upgrade, acquisition of profitable assets and high returns of investment projects.",""]],"123":[[1,"93","7","Environment Management Act Administration Capacity Building","Capacity building to improve administration of the Environment Management Act (EMA) 2004",""],[1,"93","7","Natural Resource and Environment Data Reporting Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity to collate and report on natural resource and environment related data.",""],[1,"94","21","Natural Resource and Environment Data Collection Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen Capac- ity for collection of natural resource and environment related data",""]],"124":[[1,"93","9","Labour Market Information System Development","Develop Labour Market Information System.",""],[1,"93","9","Workmen's Compensation Act Review","Review Workmen's Compensation Act.",""]],"125":[[1,"93","14","National Competition and Consumer Protection Policy","Develop a National Competition and Consumer Protection Policy.",""],[1,"93","15","Comprehensive Competition and Consumer Protection Policy Framework","Develop a Comprehensive Competition and Consumer Protection Policy Framework, including review of Commerce Commission Act.",""],[1,"93","15","Public Awareness and Stakeholder Engagement for Best Practices","Public awareness and stakeholder engagement to promote best practices.",""],[1,"93","15","Voluntary Compliance and Self-Regulation Promotion","Promote voluntary compliance and self-regulation.",""],[1,"93","16","Trade Standards and Metrology Legal Framework Reform","Review and revise legal framework relating to Trade Standards and Metrology.",""],[1,"93","16","Department of National Trade Measurements and Standards Reorganisation","Reorganise Department of National Trade Measurements and Standards.",""],[1,"95","12","National Competition and Consumer Protection Policy","Develop national competition and consumer protection policy",""],[1,"95","19","Capacity Building for Restrictive Trade Practices Administration","Build capacity to administer restrictive trade prac- tices",""]],"126":[[1,"98","8","Manufacturing Sector Development and Fiscal Incentive Support","the manufacturing sector will be developed further, with more value addition and expansion into new areas of manufacturing.",""],[1,"98","8","Fijian Made-Buy Fijian Promotion Campaign","the Fijian Made-Buy Fijian campaign has augured well for the promotion of locally manufactured products, both within Fiji and internationally.",""],[1,"98","9","Manufacturing Hub Development Initiative","Government's focus in the next 5 years is to develop Fiji as a manufacturing hub of the Pacific.",""],[1,"98","10","Support for Competitive High-Value-Added Industries","Investments will be supported for competitive high- value-added industries with an emphasis on agro- based manufacturing and niche products for export development.",""],[1,"98","10","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion in New Industries","Foreign direct investment will be encouraged in a number of new industries.",""],[1,"98","10","Specialised Economic Zones Development","Government will develop specialised economic zones built on the \"plug and play\" concept with tailor made incentives to attract investments in the services and manufacturing industries.",""],[1,"98","11","Specialised Economic Zone Development in the Western Division","in the Western Division, will be the first such specialised economic zone.",""],[1,"98","11","Joint Venture and PPP Promotion for Technology Transfer","Joint ventures between foreign and local investors and other PPP modalities will be encouraged, with a key focus on technology transfer.",""],[1,"99","2","Foreign-Local Joint Venture Promotion","Promote joint ventures between foreign and local investors.",""],[1,"99","2","Public-Private Partnership Project Facilitation","Promote and facilitate Public-Private Partnership (PPP) projects.",""],[1,"99","4","Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Promote investment in infrastructure to stimulate Global Value Chain activities.",""],[1,"99","4","Investment Policy Development","Develop an Investment Policy.",""],[1,"99","4","Investment Promotion Missions","Undertake investment missions to capital and technology exporting nations and within the domestic economy.",""],[1,"99","4","Technology Transfer Incentives","Provide incentives to facilitate technological transfer.",""],[1,"99","4","Investment Policy and Regulatory Framework Reform","Establish a more cohesive policy and supportive regulatory and institutional framework for investment.",""],[1,"99","4","Private Sector Research and Development Promotion","Promote private sector driven research and development activities.",""],[1,"99","7","Rural-Based Industrial Enterprise Development","Develop rural based industrial enterprises.",""],[1,"99","8","Appropriate Infrastructure Development","Promote and facilitate the development of appropriate infrastructure.",""],[1,"99","8","Rural Industrialisation Strategy","Develop and implement a rural industrialisation strategy.",""],[1,"99","8","On-site Agro-processing Promotion","Encourage on-site agro-processing in agricultural farm blocks.",""],[1,"99","8","Agricultural Value Chain Linkages","Establish linkages between agricultural farming blocks, industrial estates and out-grower schemes.",""],[1,"99","10","Promotion of Locally Produced Goods and Services","Promote the consumption of quality locally produced goods and services.",""],[1,"99","10","Formalisation of the Domestic Trading Sector","Promote formalisation of the domestic trading sector.",""],[1,"99","15","Land Reclamation and Master Planning Initiative","Phase 1: Reclamation works Phase 2: Secure investment and draft Master Plan and Design Concept",""],[1,"110","1","Overarching Rural-Based Industry Policy","Develop an overarching rural based industry policy",""]],"127":[[1,"98","12","Specialised Manufacturing Skills Training","To meet the skills requirements of the manufacturing sector, specialised training and skill development will be provided.",""],[1,"98","12","Manufacturing Skills Development Collaboration with Technical Institutions","The required skills will be developed in collaboration with the technical colleges and tertiary institutions.",""],[1,"98","12","Apprenticeship Programme Strengthening","The apprenticeship programme will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"99","5","Specialised Programmes with Tertiary and Vocational Institutions","Establish specialised programmes with tertiary and vocational institutions to support the manufacturing and commerce sector.",""],[1,"99","6","Specialised Training for Manufacturing and Commerce Sectors","Introduce specialised training relevant to the manufacturing and commerce sector in existing institutes.",""],[1,"99","6","Apprenticeship Programme Revitalisation","Revitalise the apprenticeship programme.",""],[1,"100","1","Introduction of Technical Programmes in Tertiary and Vocational Institutions","Introduction of technical programmes in tertiary and vocational insti- tutions.",""]],"128":[[1,"99","11","Green Manufacturing Promotion","Encourage green manufacturing.",""],[1,"99","12","Environment-Friendly Industrial Practices Promotion","Encourage industries to adopt more environment-friendly technology and practices.",""],[1,"99","12","Sustainable Water Resource Use Promotion","Promote sustainable use of water resources.",""],[1,"99","12","Biodiversity Conservation for Sustainable Manufacturing","Strengthen conservation of biodiversity for sustainable manufacturing practices.",""],[1,"99","12","Energy Efficiency Promotion","Promote energy efficiency.",""],[1,"99","12","Waste Management Enhancement","Enhance waste management.",""],[1,"99","19","Green Manufacturing Incentive Scheme","Provide incentives for industries that adopt green manufacturing processes.",""],[1,"99","20","Green Manufacturing Incentives","Incentives for green manufac- turing devel- oped.",""]],"129":[[1,"100","13","Financial Inclusion and Access to Finance Expansion","In the next 5 years, more emphasis will be placed on improving financial literacy, financial inclusion, improving access to finance, integrated digital-payment systems, access to insurance services, capital market development, and establishing the legal framework for regulation of credit unions and moneylenders.",""],[1,"101","1","Financial Literacy Improvement Initiative","Improve financial literacy.",""],[1,"101","2","Financial Education Programme Review and Monitoring","Review and monitor financial education programs for primary and secondary schools.",""],[1,"101","2","Financial Literacy Expansion Programme","Introduce financial literacy programs for tertiary students, low-income groups, and rural and marginalised communities.",""],[1,"101","2","Youth Savings Promotion Initiative","Encourage a savings culture amongst youths.",""],[1,"101","2","Adult Financial Education Coordination Mechanism","Improve coordination of adult financial education training programs between government, the private sector and development partners.",""],[1,"101","3","Capital Markets Awareness and Participation Initiative","Improve awareness and participation in the capital markets.",""],[1,"101","4","Regional and International Securities Listing Promotion","Encourage regional and international securities listing and transactions on the South Pacific Stock Exchange (SPSE).",""],[1,"101","4","State-Owned Enterprise Listing on SPSE","Prioritize listing of State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) on SPSE to boost stock market activity.",""],[1,"101","4","New Investment Products and Capital Raising Platforms","Encourage the introduction of new and alternative investment products and/or capital raising platforms on the SPSE.",""],[1,"101","4","Investor Awareness and Education Initiative","Support the provision of appropriate investor awareness and education initiatives (both general and targeted) throughout Fiji.",""],[1,"101","4","Capital Markets Capacity Building","Support the provision of relevant capacity building opportunities within the capital markets.",""],[1,"101","4","Capital Markets Technology Upgrade","Support the use of appropriate locally and internationally developed technology that will reduce transaction costs and time, and support ease of doing business in Fiji's stock market.",""],[1,"102","1","Capital Markets Investor Base Expansion","Increase the number of investors in the capital markets.",""],[1,"102","4","Increase the Number of Listed Companies on the SPSE","Increase the number of listed companies on the SPSE.",""]],"130":[[1,"103","1","Urban Development and City Services Improvement Programme","government in the next 5 years will focus on better urban development strategies, the identification and development of future growth centres, extension of town boundaries, urban waste management, beautification, disaster planning and response, upgrading and relocation of informal settlements, better traffic management and provision of basic services.",""],[1,"103","2","Urban Policy Action Plan Review and Institutional Reform","The Urban Policy Action Plan 2007 will be reviewed with a view to undertaking institutional reforms.",""],[1,"103","2","Urban Spatial Planning and Miniature Model Development","Spatial plans and miniature models will be developed to guide long- term development in all urban centres.",""],[1,"103","2","New Town Development Planning","Areas identified for new-town development include Navua, Korovou, Nabouwalu, Keiyasi, Vunidawa, and Seaqaqa.",""],[1,"103","2","City and Town Planning Scheme Review and Boundary Extension","The City and Town Planning Scheme will be reviewed and town boundaries will be extended to enable provision of municipal services.",""],[1,"103","3","Nature and Recreation Parks, Gardens and Walkways Development","Nature and recreation parks, gardens and walkways will be developed to beautify towns and cities and also ensure balance between urban expansion, nature and quality of living.",""],[1,"103","8","Sister-City Partnership Programme","Sister-city arrangements shall be formed to drive the agenda at the town and city level.",""],[1,"104","1","Urban Management and Municipal Town Planning Strengthening","Strengthen urban management and administration of town planning at municipal level.",""],[1,"104","2","Urban Policy Action Plan Review and Institutional Reform","Review status of Urban Policy Action Plan to determine achievements and areas for future work.",""],[1,"104","2","Town-Planning Scheme Update Programme","Update all town-planning schemes to ensure they reflect the current state on the ground.",""],[1,"104","2","Urban Spatial Planning and 20-Year Model Development","Develop spatial plans with associated 20-year miniature models for all urban centres.",""],[1,"104","2","Municipal Council Capacity Support Programme","Develop a programme to support the capacity of all municipal councils to effectively administer town-planning responsibilities.",""],[1,"104","2","Small Town Town-Planning Scheme Update","Update town-planning schemes of small towns.",""],[1,"104","2","Small Town-Rural Linkage Development Plan","Develop functional linkages between small towns and surrounding rural areas.",""],[1,"104","3","Long-Term Growth Centre Planning and Urban Development","Strengthen long-term planning for identification of growth centres and their development into vibrant urban centres.",""],[1,"104","4","Division-Level Growth Area Identification and Growth Centre Support","Identify areas for future growth in line with the development plans of each Division.",""],[1,"104","4","Private-Public Partnership Support for Growth Centre Industries","Identify potential industries to support development and viability of growth centres in each relevant area through private-public partnerships.",""],[1,"104","4","Town Boundary Identification and Extension","Continue with the identification and extension of town boundaries that will ensure standardisation of building structures, creation of employment opportunities and bring social services to the people.",""]],"131":[[1,"103","6","Climate-Resilient Urban Development Compliance Guidelines","All new urban development projects will need to comply with guidelines to ensure resilience to climatic hazards and natural disasters.",""],[1,"103","6","Climate- and Disaster-Proof Urban Design Standards","Structural integrity and climate and disaster-proof designs will be key aspects of future projects, together with early-warning systems, disaster- response plans, inter-agency coordination and enhanced disaster-response capacity.",""],[1,"104","6","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Incentives","Incentivise households and businesses to invest in renewable energy and adopt energy efficiency practices and technology including provision for subsidies.",""],[1,"104","6","Energy Efficiency Standards for New Buildings","Develop and legislate energy efficiency standards for new buildings.",""],[1,"104","6","Building Energy Efficiency Rating and Certification System","Introduce a rating system based on energy efficiency level of buildings (both existing and new) relative to legislated standards.",""],[1,"104","6","Urban Rainwater Harvesting Systems Review","Examine options for effective and efficient rainwater harvesting systems within urban centres.",""],[1,"104","7","Climate and Natural Hazard Vulnerability Assessment Integration","Include vulnerability assessments, and climate change and natural hazards impact projections in infrastructure and urban planning.",""],[1,"104","8","Urban Climate Change Modelling and Hazard Mapping","Undertake climate change modelling on all urban centres and develop hazard maps for all urban centres.",""],[1,"104","8","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management in Town Planning","Incorporate climate change adaptation and disaster risk management into town planning schemes.",""],[1,"104","8","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Design Standards","Infrastructure designs to incorporate building resilience to disasters.",""],[1,"104","8","Coastal Resilience Design Competition for Urban Centres","Strengthen coastal boundaries of urban centres through running a competition on design for coastal development of main urban central business districts that not only support natural biodiversity but also build resilience and protect urban infrastructure.",""],[1,"104","8","Urban Disaster Risk Reduction and Response Planning","Ensure disaster risk reduction and disaster management response plans are developed for all urban centres.",""],[1,"104","8","Municipal Hazard Map Capacity Building","Improve knowledge and understanding at all levels of municipal governance of the hazard maps relevant to their respective jurisdictions.",""],[1,"104","8","National Platform for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management","Establish a National Platform for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management where stakeholders can interact and better coordinate resources.",""],[1,"104","8","Urban Climate Change Awareness and Community Disaster Management","Undertake awareness on climate change adaptation and strengthen disaster management at community level through the dissemination of user-friendly brochures, public debates, social media and other multimedia sources.",""],[1,"104","8","Mangrove Revitalization Program","Implement a mangrove revitalization program.",""]],"132":[[1,"107","1","Rural Development Gap Bridging Initiative","government is committed to bridging the development gap between the rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"107","1","Rural Infrastructure and Services Investment Programme","Recent years have witnessed substantial government investment in the development of rural infrastructure, provision of education and health services, rural electrification, access to water, income-generating opportunities, better communications and transportation.",""],[1,"107","2","Integrated Divisional Development Planning","Divisional development plans will be developed in consultation with the relevant communities and other stakeholders for consideration for funding support by government.",""],[1,"108","1","Rural and Outer Island Community Support Programme","Assist rural and outer island communities to meet their basic needs, improve living standards and quality of life towards self- sufficiency.",""],[1,"108","2","Integrated Rural Development Framework Enhancement","Strengthen the integrated rural development framework to incorporate an inclusive package when undertaking rural infrastructure development (roads, water, energy etc.) that will strengthen interagency coordination in facilitating implementation.",""],[1,"108","2","Divisional Development Planning with Stakeholder Consultation","Develop divisional development plans in consultation with divisional stakeholders, including communities.",""],[1,"108","2","Rural Awareness and Civic Education Programme","Awareness programmes to educate rural population on government programmes, social assistance schemes and their civic responsibilities.",""],[1,"109","12","Rural Development Capital Projects Implementation","Consolidation and implementation of rural development capital projects endorsed by the Divisional Development Boards",""]],"133":[[1,"111","14","Farm Drainage and Irrigation Infrastructure Investment","Government will invest in improving farm drainage infrastructure and irrigation to control water run-off and saltwater intrusion.",""],[1,"111","14","Climate-Resilient Cane Variety Development","Through the Sugar Research Institute of Fiji (SRIF), FSC will develop improved cane varieties to improve resilience of crops and production systems to climate change.",""],[1,"112","4","Climate-Resilient Cane Variety Development","Develop climate resilient cane varieties",""]],"134":[[1,"113","2","Commodity Production Expansion under Bilateral Quarantine Agreements","In the next 5 years, key interventions will be pursued to increase production of commodities under bilateral quarantine agreements (eggplant, okra, pawpaw, chillies, and breadfruit), as well as rice, taro, cassava, fruits and vegetables, kava, organic products, livestock and dairy products.",""],[1,"113","3","Commodity Plans for Each Product","Commodity plans for each product will be developed or reviewed.",""],[1,"113","3","Crop Replanting and Agricultural Support Package","Government will support initiatives for crop replanting, supplying agro inputs, extension services and training for young farmers, relevant crop-oriented research, provision of high-yielding and climate-resilient seeds and crop varieties, and better land-use planning.",""],[1,"113","3","Cluster Farming, Contract Farming, and Agricultural Finance Guidance","the commodity plans will provide directions for cluster farming, contract farming, and access to finance and labour requirements.",""],[1,"113","4","Agricultural Mechanisation and Technology Adoption Support","Mechanisation and new technologies will be adopted through government support and through private sector partnerships in areas of hydroponics, livestock and dairy, organic farming, and processing of agricultural products (ginger, rice, fresh fruits and vegetables) and fruit drinks.",""],[1,"113","5","Small Farm Commercialization Support Initiative","Small farms will also be assisted to graduate to semi-commercial status.",""],[1,"113","6","Agricultural Marketing Authority Strengthening","The Agricultural Marketing Authority (AMA) will be strengthened to provide effective marketing support to farmers in the rural and outer islands, while avoiding crowding out private sector participation.",""],[1,"113","6","Farm-to-Market Linkage Development","Stronger links will be forged between farms and markets to create greater synergy between the agricultural sector and the tourism industry.",""],[1,"113","7","Export Market Expansion for Agricultural Produce","For export development, we will continue to capitalise on our favourable trade and quarantine arrangements that allow exports of agricultural produce to Australia, New Zealand, the US, Europe, Canada, China and neighbouring Pacific Island countries.",""],[1,"113","7","Overseas Supermarket Export Promotion","Opportunities to expand Fiji's exports for sale in mainstream supermarket chains overseas will also be pursued in the future.",""],[1,"114","1","Broad-Based Agricultural Support Programme","Continue broad-based support to agriculture as a key driver to economic growth and poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"114","2","Agricultural Marketing Support Review","Review the role and effectiveness of AMA in supporting the marketing of agro-produce, particularly for smallholder farms.",""],[1,"114","2","Agriculture-Tourism Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen links and synergy between the agricultural sector and the tourism industry to promote locally grown",""],[1,"114","2","Fiji Crops and Livestock Council Coordination Mechanism","Develop effective synergy between the Fiji Crops and Livestock Council and major industry players to drive foods.",""],[1,"114","2","Smallholder Incentives and Agricultural Finance Package","Development of tailor-made incentives and financial packages for smallholder farmers and incentivise investment into value addition and larger commercial agriculture ventures.",""],[1,"114","2","Agricultural Commodities Marketing Stimulus","Provide stimulus for agricultural commodities' marketing both for domestic and export markets.",""],[1,"114","2","Farmer Graduation Programme","Establish and implement a programme to graduate farmers from subsistence to semi-commercial to full commercial farming.",""],[1,"114","2","Farmer Cooperatives and Cluster Arrangement Promotion","Establish farmer cooperatives and promote cluster arrangements to raise synergy amongst farmers.",""],[1,"114","3","Targeted Commodity Support Programme","Provide targeted support to selected commodities.",""],[1,"114","4","Commodity and Industry Planning Framework","Develop commodity and industry plans involving relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"114","4","Niche Agricultural Commodities Development","Develop agricultural commodities that have potential niche markets.",""],[1,"114","4","Priority Commodity Concentration Strategy","Concentrate resources and efforts on selected commodities for which Fiji has a competitive advantage and where there is an available domestic or export market: (i) BQA crops (Nadi), (ii) Dairy (Korovou), (iii) Pineapple and Mango (Rakiraki, Seaqaqa), (iv) Root crops (Bua), (v) Fruits and Vegetables (Sigatoka), (vi) Coconut (Taveuni) and (vii) Organic farming for Outer Islands (Levuka).",""],[1,"114","4","Rural Agricultural Infrastructure Provision","Provide infrastructure such as roads, utilities, packing and cold storage facilities.",""],[1,"114","4","Public-Private Partnership Collection Centre Operations","Encourage development of public-private partnership arrangements in operating collection centres",""],[1,"114","5","Sustainable Agricultural Land Use and Farm Efficiency Improvement","Empower farmers through agricultural land use practices, and improved farm efficiency that promote sustainability in resource utilisation.",""],[1,"114","6","Agriculture Support Services Strengthening","Strengthen the delivery of agriculture support services of research, extension training, soil health and water use, animal health, and credit assistance to improve farm productivity and efficiency.",""],[1,"114","6","Traditional Farming Skills Revitalisation Programme","Revitalisation and enhancement of traditional farming skills and knowledge (Food and nutrition security).",""],[1,"114","6","Backyard Farming Technology Training","Increase understanding of and training in the use of backyard farming technologies such as container farming.",""],[1,"114","6","Organic Farming and Controlled-Environment Agriculture Support","Develop and introduce organic farming methods to farmers and provide incentives for organic farming, and investment in greenhouse and hydroponic technology.",""],[1,"114","6","Farm Waste Utilization Initiative","Continue initiatives to improve the use of farm waste for animal feed, organic fertilizer or biogas.",""]],"135":[[1,"114","2","Research and Extension Services Division Reform","Strengthen research and development through a review and restructure of the Research and Extension Services Division.",""],[1,"114","2","Agricultural Statistics Database Development","Develop a modern agricultural statistical database to better support decision-making.",""],[1,"114","2","Agriculture Census Survey","Undertake an Agriculture Census Survey by 2019.",""],[1,"114","2","Livestock Sector Strategy Implementation","Adoption and implementation of Livestock Sector Strategy.",""],[1,"114","2","National Land Use Plan","Formulation and adoption of a National Land Use Plan.",""],[1,"114","2","Land and Water Resources Management Bill","Enactment of the Land and Water Resources Management Bill.",""],[1,"114","2","Agricultural Mechanisation Upgrade","Improve production and productivity of the agriculture sector through increased mechanisation.",""],[1,"114","2","FNU Agriculture Curriculum Review","Review agriculture curriculum at the Fiji National University (FNU) to identify practical components and pathways into commercial agriculture.",""],[1,"114","2","Farmer Training Institutionalisation","Institutionalise a system of farmer training that encourages a new generation of farmers to receive relevant hands-on training as has been successfully demonstrated by the Tutu Training Centre.",""],[1,"114","2","National Seed Policy","Formulation and endorsement of the national seed policy.",""],[1,"114","2","Local Seed Industry Development","Establish a local seed industry to ensure strategic availability of seed and other planting material.",""],[1,"114","4","Farmer Field Schools Training System","Institutionalise a system of community-based training to farmers through Farmer Field Schools.",""],[1,"114","6","Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management Training for Farmers","Collaborate with community-based partners to provide training in the proper approach to climate change and disaster risk management.",""],[1,"114","6","Farmer Field Schools on Land Use and Risk Management","Farmer Field Schools training to include proper land use practices and risk management.",""]],"136":[[1,"116","19","Construction of Namosi 3rd Dam","Construction of Namosi 3rd dam",""]],"137":[[1,"118","2","Fishing Industry Regulatory and Resource Management Oversight","government providing the regulatory and resource-management oversight and pursuing adherence to regional and international commitments",""],[1,"118","3","National Fisheries Policy for Sustainable Fisheries Management","The National Fisheries Policy that will be finalised soon will guide the management and development of sustainable fisheries within the offshore, inshore, coastal and aquaculture sub-sectors.",""],[1,"118","4","Offshore Fisheries Regulatory Framework","The Offshore Fisheries Decree 2014 and the Offshore Fisheries Management Regulations 2014 will continue to guide the development and sustainable management of the tuna fishery as well as the overall offshore fisheries",""],[1,"118","5","Strengthened Fisheries Monitoring and Enforcement","Monitoring and enforcement will be strengthened to minimise illegal, unreported and unregulated fishing.",""],[1,"118","7","Marine Protected Areas Expansion and Inshore Fisheries Management Measures","The inshore fisheries sector will be sustainably managed through the further establishment of Marine Protected Areas (MPA) and other measures to provide for better catch management.",""],[1,"118","7","Review of Permits and Licences for Customary Fishing Rights","The issue of permits and licences for traditional fishing rights of Qoligoli (Customary Fishing Rights Area) is currently under review in consultation with relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"118","7","Mangrove and Coral Revitalisation and Conservation Support","Government, in collaboration with its partners, will continue to support the revitalisation and conservation of mangroves and corals.",""],[1,"118","7","Coastal and Inshore Fisheries Data-Gathering Framework","To ensure better management of coastal and inshore fisheries, a reliable data-gathering framework will be established to track the level of catch and fish stock on a regular basis.",""],[1,"119","3","National Fisheries Policy Finalisation and Fisheries Act Review","Finalise the National Fisheries Policy and its coverage of offshore-processing, value-addition and niche · Review the Fisheries Act 1942 and its support for sustainable and viable growth and management of markets.",""],[1,"119","3","Fisheries Research and Industry Uptake Promotion","Encourage further research and industry uptake into value-adding and niche markets and encourage fisheries. processing to capture more value through Pacific Fishing Company Limited (PAFCO) and other private · Undertake a 'look to the future exercise' that focuses on long-term tangible outcomes and the costs and players.",""],[1,"119","3","Fisheries Stakeholder Engagement Platform","Create a platform for the active engagement of private sector, regional partners and other key stakeholders to discuss offshore fisheries sector policies and programme initiatives.",""],[1,"119","3","Regional Fisheries Partnership Development","Engage in regional fisheries partnerships to develop and implement a coherent approach to optimal and sustained fisheries developments.",""],[1,"119","4","Sustainable Inshore and Coastal Fisheries Management and Development","Support inshore/ coastal fisheries through sustainable fisheries management and development.",""],[1,"119","5","Coastal Fisheries Management Division Establishment","Establish a Coastal Fisheries Management Division responsible for the monitoring, control and surveillance of coastal fisheries.",""],[1,"119","5","Inshore Marine Resources Database Upgrade","Upgrade existing database to capture data on the status of inshore/coastal marine resources including regeneration and harvesting levels.",""],[1,"119","5","Inshore Fisheries Resource Assessment Programme","Conduct resource assessment survey to manage inshore fisheries.",""],[1,"119","5","Inshore Fisheries Valuation Framework Development","Develop an appropriate valuation framework for inshore fisheries.",""],[1,"119","5","Fishing Permit Assistance Streamlining","Review the procedures and streamline processes to obtaining assistance such as obtaining a fishing permit.",""],[1,"119","5","Fish Stock Assessment and Commodity Profiling","Undertake resource assessments and commodity profiling to establish the status of fish stocks.",""],[1,"119","5","Inshore Fisheries Fees and Charges Review","Also finalise the review of fees and charges.",""],[1,"119","5","Inshore Fisheries Management Decree Review","Finalise the review of the Inshore Fisheries Management Decree and formalise a supportive inshore policy and regulations.",""],[1,"119","5","Recreational Fisheries Policy Completion","Complete a recreational fisheries policy to support activities such as game fishing.",""],[1,"119","5","Sustainable Fisheries Management Measures","Promote sustainable fisheries management and the replenishment of fish stocks through management tools such as establishment of MPAs, seasonal closures, size limits and quotas, and gear restrictions.",""],[1,"119","5","Mangrove and Coral Conservation Support","Support the revitalisation and conservation of mangroves and corals.",""],[1,"119","5","Fish Warden Training and Equipment Programme","Conduct training and equip fish wardens for effective monitoring and enforcement.",""],[1,"119","5","Community-Based Integrated Sustainable Resource Management Partnerships","Intensify collaboration with development partners to empower community-based, integrated sustainable resource management and development initiatives through ongoing fisheries programmes.",""],[1,"120","21","Fishing License and Fee Procedure Review","Review the procedure for obtaining fishing licenses and fees and charges",""],[1,"120","29","Program Support Unit Establishment","Establish separate program support unit",""],[1,"120","31","Establishment of Coastal Fisheries Management Division","Establishment of Coastal Fisheries Management Division",""],[1,"121","8","Mangrove Rehabilitation Programme","Mangrove Rehabili- tation Programme",""],[1,"121","11","Marine Protected Areas Expansion","Establish MPAs targeting 30% of Fiji's marine areas (%)",""]],"138":[[1,"118","8","Aquaculture Private Sector Investment Support","private sector investments will be supported in aquaculture projects through tax incentives, provision of juvenile fry and post-larva stocks, and research and extension services.",""],[1,"118","8","Multispecies Hatchery Development Investment","The government will continue investment in the development of a multispecies hatchery.",""],[1,"118","9","Fish Product Value Addition Support and Promotion","Value addition of fish products will also be supported and promoted.",""],[1,"119","6","Aquaculture Industry Development Support","Support growth of aquaculture industries.",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Private Investment and Partnership Promotion","Promote private sector investment in aquaculture through public and private partnerships, tax incentives,",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Commercial Development Support","Support the cost-benefit analysis of the commercial development of aquaculture industries including research and extension services, provision of juvenile fry and post larva stocks.",""],[1,"119","7","Small-Scale Aquaculture Support Programme","Support small-scale farmers and community-based aquaculture production for food and nutrition security existing and potential commodities such as tilapia, prawn, shrimp and seaweed.",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Farmer Technical and Financial Support","Improve access to technical advice, training, quality seed and feed supply, and financial support to and livelihoods.",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Facility Upgrading Programme","Upgrade existing aquaculture facilities to boost brood and seed stock production.",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Fees and Charges Review","Review existing fees and charges for brood and feed stock supply.",""],[1,"119","7","Fisheries Value Chain Analysis and Market Development","Undertake a value chain analysis of fisheries products including value-addition and marketing.",""],[1,"119","7","Niche Fisheries Commodity Market Exploration","Further explore fish commodities and products targeting potential niche markets such as bêche-de-mer, sea grapes,",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Development Decree Implementation","Implement the Aquaculture Development Decree, along with regulations and the aquaculture strategic",""],[1,"119","7","Commodity Development Plan and Fiji Aquaculture Strategy Finalisation","Finalise the Commodity Development Plan and Fiji Aquaculture Strategy. plan.",""],[1,"119","7","Aquaculture Farm Technical and Financial Support","Improve access to technical advice and financial support to aquaculture farms.",""],[1,"120","14","National Aquaculture Strategy and Five-Year Development Plan Finalization","Finalize the National Aquaculture Strategy and 5 year development plan",""],[1,"120","24","Aquaculture Fees and Charges Review","Review existing fees and charges for aquaculture",""]],"139":[[1,"118","2","Fishing Industry Support for Export Diversification and Trade Facilitation","Government has also supported the industry in the diversification of export markets, trade facilitation, product research and development, conducive fiscal and tax environment and infrastructure.",""],[1,"118","6","Tuna Stabilisation Fund Financial Assistance Scheme","The Government is devising a distribution model to provide financial assistance to domestic fishing companies through the Tuna Stabilisation Fund.",""],[1,"118","6","Sustainable Harvesting Certification and Review","To obtain premium prices in export markets, certification for sustainable harvesting practices will continue and will be periodically monitored and reviewed.",""]],"140":[[1,"122","4","Downstream Timber Processing and Value Addition Strategy","Strategies will be put in place to capture better returns from greater value addition by incorporating more down-stream processing.",""],[1,"122","5","Support for Cottage Industry Development in Forestry","Support will continue to be given to the development of small-to-medium cottage industries through the timber utilisation and research division within the Ministry of Forests.","Ministry of Forests"],[1,"122","6","Private Sector Partnerships for Wood Bio-energy","Private sector partnerships will continue to be supported in this area.",""],[1,"122","10","Private Sector Participation in Plantation Development","Encourage private sector participation in plantation development.",""],[1,"122","11","Private Sector Investment Enablement for Plantation Development","Provide the enabling environment for private sector investment in plantation development.",""],[1,"122","12","Timber Product Development Promotion","Encourage the growth of timber product development.",""],[1,"122","13","Wood Product Research and Promotion Support","Strengthen wood product research and promotion through the provision of appropriate infrastructure (e.g. facilities, machines, equipment).",""],[1,"122","13","MSME Niche Product Development Scheme","Support Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) in their development of niche products through appropriate MSME schemes.",""],[1,"122","13","Fiji Pine Group Plant and Machinery Upgrade","Upgrade plant and machinery used by Fiji Pine Group of Companies.",""],[1,"123","13","Tropik Wood Industries Limited Sawmill, Kiln and Boiler Coils Upgrade","Upgrade of Tropik Wood Industries Limited's Sawmill, kiln and Boiler Coils",""],[1,"123","15","Wairiki Wood Chipping Facility Upgrade","Upgrade of Tropik Wood Products Limited's Wairiki wood chipping facility",""],[1,"123","17","Fiji Forest Industries Plant Machinery Upgrade","Upgrade of Fiji Forest Industries Ltd plant machinery",""]],"141":[[1,"124","7","Groundwater Development and Borehole Drilling Programme","Investigation of potential groundwater sites will continue in order to increase production and access to sustainable, clean and safe drinking water.",""],[1,"124","7","Mining Department Drill Rig Procurement","The mining department will purchase a drill rig in 2017/18.","the mining department"],[1,"124","7","Local Water Quality Testing Laboratory Upgrade","Local laboratories will be upgraded to undertake water-quality testing and geochemical analysis so that samples do not need to be sent overseas for analysis.",""]],"142":[[1,"125","3","Oil Exploration Benefit Maximization","Maximise benefit from any exploration activity in particular for oil exploration.",""],[1,"125","4","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion","Encourage and accelerate growth through FDI.",""],[1,"125","5","Investment Fiji Promotion and Marketing Integration","Promotion and marketing activities integrated with Investment Fiji programme.",""],[1,"125","5","Fiscal Incentives for Mineral Exploration Investment","Consider fiscal initiatives to attract and retain mineral exploration investment.",""],[1,"125","5","Geoscience Data Access for Investors","Ensure geoscience data readily available to assist investors.",""],[1,"125","5","Mineral Investigation Database Update and Investor Packaging","Update Mineral Investigation Programme database and package findings for investors.",""],[1,"126","9","Mineral Exploration Licensing and Quarry Approval Streamlining","Maintain mineral exploration licenses and streamline quarry approvals and licensing",""]],"143":[[1,"128","8","International Tourism Marketing Programme Expansion","Expand international marketing programmes and continue to build the image of Fiji tourism.",""],[1,"128","9","Destination Fiji Promotion in Emerging Tourist Markets","Aggressive promotion of destination Fiji in emerging tourist markets.",""],[1,"128","9","Brand Fiji Cultural Marketing Initiative","Incorporate traditional culture and art into developing \"Brand Fiji\".",""],[1,"128","9","Specialised Tourism Niche Market Development","Promote high growth niche markets for specialised tourism to address market seasonality.",""],[1,"128","9","Sustainable Luxury Tourism Package Development","Incorporate and market sustainable tourism packages with luxury tourism.",""],[1,"128","9","Regional and Provincial Visitor Guide Platform","Develop multiplatform visitor guides that are demarcated by region and province.",""]],"144":[[1,"128","14","Tourism Product Development and Sector Innovation Initiative","Identify tourism products for further development and foster sector innovation for increased value addition.",""],[1,"128","15","Tourism Value Addition and Product Development","Aggressively promote value addition in all tourism services and market segments.",""],[1,"128","15","Tourism Development Sector Analysis","Sector analysis of potential areas for tourism development.",""],[1,"128","15","Community Tourism Awareness and Resource Use Education","Educate communities about tourism and ways to make sustainable use of natural resources for tourism purposes.",""],[1,"128","15","Village and Rural Community Tourism Enterprise Support","Assist villages and rural communities to develop tourism products and services unique to their culture and surroundings.",""],[1,"128","15","Fashion Industry Development Support","Stimulate fashion industry development to complement Fiji's unique retail industry for visitors.",""],[1,"128","15","MSME Online Booking and Upgrade Support","Support MSMEs via establishment of online booking systems and focused assistance for upgrading and retrofitting.",""],[1,"128","15","Fijian Made - Buy Fijian Local Products Campaign","Develop quality locally made products that can be marketed to international visitors through the Fijian Made - Buy Fijian Campaign.",""],[1,"128","16","Tourism Market Linkage Development","Increase value addition by developing market linkages between tourism and other local sectors.",""],[1,"128","17","Agricultural Capacity Development for Tourism Supply","Develop agricultural capacity to meet tourism demands.",""],[1,"128","17","Manufacturing Sector Support for Tourism Markets","Develop the manufacturing sector to supply high quality locally made products to tourism markets.",""],[1,"128","17","Local Product Substitution in Tourism Markets","Promote substitution of imported products in favour of local products in the tourism market.",""],[1,"128","17","Extended Tourism Business Hours and Retail Development","Increase business hours in tourism hotspots and develop high-end retail outlets.",""]],"145":[[1,"128","13","Tourism-Related Illegal Activity Crackdown","Increase crackdown on illegal activities that can be associated with tourism (i.e. drugs, prostitution and human trafficking).",""],[1,"128","15","Tourism Culture and Environment Mainstreaming","Mainstream culture and environment into existing and new tourism packages.",""],[1,"129","1","Sustainable Tourism Mainstreaming","Mainstream sustainable tourism operations.",""],[1,"129","2","Sustainable Tourism Environmental Compliance and Resilience Measures","Mandate sustainable use of water and energy throughout the tourism sector.",""],[1,"129","2","Environmental Management Act and EIA Enforcement","Strengthen enforcement of the Environment Management Act (EMA) and Environment Impact Assessments",""],[1,"129","2","Climate-Resilient and Energy-Efficient Building Code Enforcement","Enforce building codes that promote climate resilient infrastructure and energy efficiency.",""],[1,"129","2","Tourism Biodiversity Conservation Programme","Strengthen conservation of biodiversity for sustainable tourism.",""],[1,"129","2","Tourism Waste Management and Recycling Initiative","Enhance waste management in tourism and promote innovative recycling.",""],[1,"129","2","Climate Risk Insurance Package Development","Work with the insurance industry to develop insurance packages for climate related adversities.",""]],"146":[[1,"128","5","Industry Quality and Accreditation Standards","Establish industry quality and accreditation standards.",""],[1,"132","2","Customs, Biosecurity, and Port Services Streamlining Reform","Customs procedures, biosecurity inspections and port services will be further streamlined and improved to reduce red tape.",""],[1,"132","3","Tariff Policy Review","Tariff policy reviews will be consistent with our economic development aspirations and priorities, taking into account the potential risks to revenue, industrial growth, employment and social conditions and the facilitation of private sector adjustment.",""],[1,"132","12","Trade Facilitation and Single Window Clearance Implementation","Facilitate the efficient flow of trade through compliance with the WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement and successful implementation of single window clearance.",""],[1,"132","12","Trade-Related Infrastructure Improvement","Support the improvement of trade related infrastructure.",""],[1,"132","12","Trade Information Services for Traders and Business","Provide trade or market information to traders and the business community.",""],[1,"132","12","Investment and Productivity Enhancement Measures","Create conditions for sustained increase in investment and the increase in total factor productivity.",""],[1,"132","12","Domestic Firm Efficiency and Competitiveness Support","Assist domestic firms to increase their levels of efficiency and competitiveness.",""],[1,"132","12","Value-Addition Research and Development Promotion","Stimulate and encourage value-addition activities through research and development.",""],[1,"132","12","Trade Support Institution Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacities of trade support institutions particularly those directly engaged with trade policy, customs, standards, trade facilitation, competition, consumer protection and provisions of trade -related information.",""],[1,"133","15","Trade Information Portal","Creation of Trade Information Portal",""]],"147":[[1,"132","7","Pacific Island Dialogue and Consensus-Building Platform","platform for dialogue and consensus building will be promoted on critical development issues for all Pacific Island countries.",""],[1,"132","8","Regional Dialogue and Consensus-Building through PIDF","Fiji acknowledges and aims to strengthen regional dialogue and consensus-building through the Pacific Island Development Forum (PIDF).",""],[1,"132","8","Green Growth Framework Adoption and Mainstreaming","The Forum promotes regional cooperation in pursuit of home-grown solutions to address sustainable development challenges faced by Pacific Small Island States, including the adoption and mainstreaming of the Green Growth Framework for Fiji.",""],[1,"132","8","Regional Cooperation through the MSG","Similarly, this commitment will also be pursued through the MSG.",""],[1,"132","10","South-South Cooperation and Regional Partnership Promotion","Fiji will strengthen its regional standing through South- South Cooperation, as a development partner in the region promoting cooperation to enhance regional integration and active cooperation in addressing common regional issues at both regional and international fora.",""]],"148":[[1,"135","6","Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Strengthen the regulatory framework.",""],[1,"135","7","Telecommunications Fee Consolidation Reform","Consolidate all existing fees for telecommunications operators (e.g. special international call handling levy, ICT levy, licensing fees, universal service obligation fund, etc.) into a single standard fee.",""],[1,"135","7","Telecommunications Regulatory Framework Development","Consider establishment of a new regulatory framework for telecommunications under the multi-sector regulator model.",""],[1,"135","7","Cybersecurity Policy and Framework Development","Develop a cyber-security policy and framework.",""],[1,"135","11","National Identity Card Feasibility Review",". Further examine the possibility of adopting a national identity card.",""],[1,"136","16","Cyber Security Policy and Framework Development","Develop a cyber- security policy and framework",""],[1,"136","17","Cyber Security Policy and Framework","Complete cyber- security policy and framework",""],[1,"136","21","National ICT Policy Review","Review the National ICT Policy",""],[1,"136","24","Telecommunications Fee Consolidation Reform","Consolidate all existing fees for telecommunications operators into a single standard fee",""],[1,"136","31","National Identity Card System","Create a national identity card",""]],"149":[[1,"135","11","Hydrometeorological Early Warning Systems and Forecasting Infrastructure",". Support the installation, operation and maintenance of adequate national/regional Early Warning\nSystems (EWSs) and forecasting infrastructure for hydro meteorological events (such as tropical cyclones, floods, etc.) and programmes for both monitoring on-going hazards and building resilience for the future.",""]]}});